          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6f808974e875a701edbd6bfc\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The insect\u2019s weight was truly surprising, and, after thinking it all through, I could hardly blame Jupiter for his opinion about it. Still, I couldn\u2019t understand why Legrand agreed with that opinion, and I couldn\u2019t figure it out, no matter how hard I tried.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he said in a grand, dramatic voice, after I finished examining the beetle. \u201cI sent for you so I could have your advice and help in carrying out Fate\u2019s plans\u2014and the plans of the bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I interrupted, \u201cyou must be sick. You should take some precautions. Go to bed, and I\u2019ll stay with you for a few days until you feel better. You\u2019re feverish, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he said.\\n\\nI did, and honestly, I found no sign of fever at all.\\n\\n\u201cBut you could still be ill without having a fever. Let me prescribe for you just this once. First, go to bed. Next\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019re wrong,\u201d he cut in. \u201cI\u2019m as well as I can be, considering the excitement I\u2019m feeling. If you truly want to help me, you\u2019ll calm this excitement.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how would we do that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery simply. Jupiter and I are going on an expedition into the hills, out on the mainland. In this trip, we\u2019ll need someone we can trust. You are the only person we can rely on. Whether we succeed or fail, the excitement you see in me will be just as quickly settled.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll do what I can to help,\u201d I said. \u201cBut are you saying that this awful beetle has anything to do with your trip into the hills?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I can\u2019t take part in something so ridiculous.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m sorry\u2014very sorry,\u201d he said. \u201cWe\u2019ll have to try it on our own.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTry it yourselves? The man must be out of his mind!\u2014but wait. How long do you plan to be gone?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProbably all night. We\u2019ll leave right away, and we\u2019ll be back by sunrise, at the latest.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you promise me, on your honor, that when your little scheme is finished\u2014and the bug business (good God!) is settled the way you want\u2014you\u2019ll return home and follow my advice exactly, as if it came from your physician?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. I promise. Now come on\u2014we have no time to waste.\u201d\\n\\nWith a heavy heart, I went with him. We left at about four o\u2019clock: Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and me. Jupiter brought the scythe and the spades, and he insisted on carrying all of them. It seemed to me he did it less out of hard work or willingness to help, and more out of fear that his master might not be able to be trusted with the tools within reach.\"}"
