          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"961552928a8f74427086b1c4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"You won\u2019t, won\u2019t you? Oh, you precious little flat!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s naughty, isn\u2019t it, Oliver?\u201d Charley Bates asked. \u201cHe\u2019ll end up getting scragged, won\u2019t he?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know what that means,\u201d Oliver replied.\\n\\n\u201cSomething like that, old fellow,\u201d Charley said. As he spoke, Master Bates caught hold of the end of his neckerchief; holding it upright in the air, he dropped his head onto his shoulder, jerked it, and made a strange sound through his teeth\u2014showing, with a lively bit of pantomime, that scragging and hanging were the same thing.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s what it means,\u201d Charley said. \u201cLook how he stares, Jack! I never saw such top-notch company as that boy\u2014he\u2019ll be the death of me, I know he will.\u201d Master Charley Bates laughed heartily again, then went back to his pipe, tears in his eyes.\\n\\n\u201cYou were brought up badly,\u201d the Dodger said, looking over Oliver\u2019s polished boots with satisfaction. \u201cFagin will make something of you, though\u2014if not, you\u2019ll be the first one he ever had that turned out unprofitable. You\u2019d better start right away, because you\u2019ll be in the trade long before you even think about it, and you\u2019re only wasting time, Oliver.\u201d\\n\\nMaster Bates backed up this advice with a string of moral lectures of his own; once those were exhausted, he and his friend Mr. Dawkins launched into a glowing description of the many pleasures that came with the life they led. They sprinkled it with hints to Oliver that the best thing he could do would be to win Fagin\u2019s favor without delay, using the same methods they themselves had used to get it.\\n\\n\u201cAnd always put this in your pipe, Nolly,\u201d the Dodger said, as the Jew was heard unlocking the door upstairs. \u201cIf you don\u2019t take fogels and tickers\u