          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1a18071829c944258d94ccf4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI\u2019m going, Mr. Will\u2014honestly, I am,\u201d the man replied at once\u2014\u201cI\u2019m out to the end now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201c_Out to the end!_\u201d Legrand fairly screamed. \u201cDo you mean you\u2019re out to the end of that limb?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSoon to the end, sir\u2014o-o-o-o-oh! Lor-gol-a-marcy! what is this up on the tree?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell!\u201d Legrand cried, delighted. \u201cWhat is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing but a skull, sir\u2014someone left it with its head up in the tree, and the crows have gobbled every bit of the meat off.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA skull, you say!\u2014all right\u2014how is it fastened to the limb?\u2014what holds it on?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSure enough, sir; I gotta look. Why, this is a strange thing, I swear\u2014there\u2019s a big nail in the skull that fastens it to the tree.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell now, Jupiter, do exactly what I tell you\u2014do you hear me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPay attention, then\u2014find the skull\u2019s left eye.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHum! hoo! that\u2019s good! why there ain\u2019t no eye left at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCurse your stupidity! Do you know your right hand from your left?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I knows that\u2014knows all about that\u2014\u2019tis my left hand what I chop the wood with.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course! You\u2019re left-handed; and your left eye would be on the same side as your left hand. Now, I suppose, you can find the skull\u2019s left eye\u2014or where the left eye used to be. Have you found it?\u201d\\n\\nThere was a long pause. At last the man asked,\\n\\n\u201cIs the skull\u2019s left eye on the same side as the skull\u2019s left hand, too?\u2014\u2019cause the skull don\u2019t have any hand at all\u2014never mind! I got the left eye now\u2014here\u2019s the left eye! what do I do with it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet the beetle drop through it, as far as the string will reach\u2014but be careful not to let go of the string.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll done, Mr. Will; that\u2019s mighty easy\u2014just put the bug through the hole\u2014watch out for him down there!\u201d\\n\\nDuring this exchange, no part of Jupiter\u2019s body could be seen; but the beetle he had let down was now visible at the end of the string, and it glistened, like a globe of burnished gold, in the last rays of the setting sun, some of which still faintly lit the height where we stood. The _scarab\u00e6us_ hung clear of any branches, and if it were allowed to fall, it would have fallen at our feet. Legrand immediately took the scythe and cleared, with it, a circular space three or four yards across directly beneath the insect; then, having done so, he ordered Jupiter to let go the string and come down from the tree.\"}"
