. In my madness I even told myself, \u2018Diana died to give you life. Her mother\u2019s spirit was put into your body, and you should be Diana to me.\u2019 No matter how hard I try to throw this love off, it clings even closer. This guilty love is more unnatural than hate. It destroys your hopes and destroys me forever.\\n\\nBetter to love despair, and safer to kiss her.\\n\\nNo time or distance can take from my soul what is part of it. Since I arrived here, I have not stopped feeling the Hell of passion that has been planted in me\u2014to burn until everything is cold, stiff, and dead.\u201d\"}"
