e as lifeless as possible. Basil was, in truth, rather dull. He interested me only once\u2014years ago\u2014when he told me he had a wild devotion for you, and that you were the guiding motive of his art.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI was fond of Basil,\u201d said Dorian, with a touch of sadness. \u201cBut don\u2019t people say he was murdered?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, some of the papers say so. It doesn\u2019t strike me as likely. I know there are dreadful quarters in Paris, but Basil wasn\u2019t the kind of man to go there. He had no curiosity. That was his chief failing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd what would you say, Harry, if I told you that I had murdered Basil?\u201d asked the younger man.\"}"
