          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"e5f5f2c75fa448df3bbe4431\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Of course, he was amusing, and all that, but I was really disappointed. When I asked him about the coat of mail, he only laughed and said it was far too cold to wear in England. Ah, here is Mr. Podgers! Now, Mr. Podgers, I want you to tell the Duchess of Paisley\u2019s fortune. Duchess, you must take your glove off. No, not the left hand\u2014the other one.\\n\\n\u201cDear Gladys, I don\u2019t think this is quite right,\u201d said the Duchess, slowly unfastening a rather dirty kid glove.\\n\\n\u201cNothing interesting ever is,\u201d said Lady Windermere. \u201cThat\u2019s just how the world is. But I must introduce you. Duchess, this is Mr. Podgers, my favorite palm reader. Mr. Podgers, this is the Duchess of Paisley. And if you say she has a bigger \u2018mountain of the moon\u2019 than I do, I\u2019ll never believe in you again.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m sure, Gladys, there\u2019s nothing like that in my hand,\u201d said the Duchess seriously.\\n\\n\u201cYour Grace is right,\u201d said Mr. Podgers, looking at the little fat hand with its short, square fingers. \u201cThe mountain of the moon isn\u2019t developed. But the line of life is excellent. Please bend your wrist. Thank you. Three clear lines on the rascette! You\u2019ll live to a great age, Duchess, and you\u2019ll be extremely happy. Ambition\u2014very moderate. The line of intellect\u2014nothing exaggerated. The line of the heart\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow, do be discreet, Mr. Podgers,\u201d Lady Windermere called out.\\n\\n\u201cNothing would please me more,\u201d said Mr. Podgers, bowing, \u201cif the Duchess had ever been, but I\u2019m sorry to say I see strong, lasting affection mixed with a firm sense of duty.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPlease go on, Mr. Podgers,\u201d said the Duchess, looking pleased.\\n\\n\u201cEconomy is one of Your Grace\u2019s virtues,\u201d Mr. Podgers continued, and Lady Windermere burst into laughter.\\n\\n\u201cEconomy is a very good thing,\u201d the Duchess said, pleased with herself. \u201cWhen I married Paisley, he had eleven castles, and not a single house that was fit to live in.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd now he has twelve houses, and not a single castle,\u201d Lady Windermere said.\\n\\n\u201cWell, my dear,\u201d the Duchess began.\\n\\n\u201cComfort,\u201d said Mr. Podgers. \u201cModern improvements. Hot water in every bedroom. Your Grace is right. Comfort is the only thing our civilization can offer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019ve described the Duchess\u2019s character wonderfully, Mr. Podgers. Now you must describe Lady Flora\u2019s,\u201d and, as the smiling hostess nodded, a tall girl with sandy Scotch hair stepped awkwardly out from behind the sofa and held out a long, bony hand with spatula-like fingers.\\n\\n\u201cAh, a pianist!\u201d said Mr. Podgers. \u201cI see. An excellent pianist, but perhaps not quite a real musician.\u201d\"}"
