m and almost friendly, pushed his chair aside. He turned his back to the audience and began drawing a map of America on the blackboard, to keep the geography class busy. But he struggled with it because his hand was unsteady. A quiet ripple of laughter spread through the room. He knew what was happening, and tried to fix it. He wiped out the lines and redrew them, but he only made them worse, and the laughter grew louder. He focused hard on his work, as if determined not to be defeated by the amusement. He felt that everyone was watching him. He believed he was doing better, yet the laughter continued\u2014and it even clearly increased.\"}"
