          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7c6faceabcaaf48178f5f6c7\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The exquisite gentlemen of the finest breeding wore small dangling trinkets that chimed as they moved languidly; their golden fetters rang like precious little bells; and between that ringing and the rustle of silk and brocade and fine linen, there was a flutter in the air that fanned Saint Antoine and his devouring hunger far away.\\n\\nDress was the one reliable talisman and charm used to keep everything in its proper place. Everyone was dressed for a Fancy Ball that was never meant to end. From the Palace of the Tuileries, through Monseigneur and the entire Court, through the Chambers, the Tribunals of Justice, and all society (except the scarecrows), the Fancy Ball descended to the Common Executioner\u2014who, in keeping with the charm, was required to officiate \u201cfrizzled, powdered, in a gold-laced coat, pumps, and white silk stockings.\u201d At the gallows and the wheel\u2014the axe was a rarity\u2014Monsieur Paris, as it was the episcopal style among his fellow Professors in the provinces, Monsieur Orleans, and the rest, presided in that dainty outfit. And who among the company at Monseigneur\u2019s reception in that seventeen hundred and eightieth year of our Lord could possibly doubt that a system rooted in a frizzled hangman, powdered, gold-laced, pumped, and white-silk stockinged, would see the very stars out!\\n\\nAfter Monseigneur had relieved his four men of their burdens and taken his chocolate, he had the doors of the Holiest of Holiests thrown open, and he came out. Then what submission, what cringing and fawning, what servility, what abject humiliation! As for bowing down in body and spirit, nothing of that sort was left for Heaven\u2014which may have been one of the reasons the worshippers of Monseigneur never bothered with it.\\n\\nWith a word of promise here and a smile there, a whisper to one happy slave and a wave of the hand to another, Monseigneur passed affably through his rooms to the remote region of the Circumference of Truth. There, Monseigneur turned and came back again, and in due course of time got himself shut up in his sanctuary by the chocolate sprites, and was seen no more.\\n\\nWhen the show was over, the flutter in the air became a little storm, and the precious little bells went ringing downstairs. Soon there was only one person left from the whole crowd, and he, with his hat under his arm and his snuff-box in his hand, slowly made his way out, passing among the mirrors.\\n\\n\u201cI devote you,\u201d said this person, stopping at the last door on his way and turning toward the sanctuary, \u201cto the Devil!\u201d\\n\\nWith that, he shook the snuff from his fingers as if he were shaking dust from his feet, and quietly walked downstairs.\"}"
