          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1108d551d07bf847a9ace911\",\"rewritten_text\":\"For a moment, I was so shocked that I couldn\u2019t think clearly or accurately. I knew my design was different in the details, though the overall outline was similar. Soon I took a candle and sat at the other end of the room, then studied the parchment more closely. When I turned it over, I saw my own sketch on the back, exactly as I had made it.\\n\\nAt first, I was only surprised by how closely the outlines matched. I couldn\u2019t ignore the strange coincidence that, without my knowing it, there was a skull on the other side of the parchment, directly beneath my figure of the _scarab\u00e6us_. Even more astonishing, the skull matched my drawing not just in outline, but in size. This coincidence stunned me completely for a time. That is what such coincidences usually do. The mind tries to connect everything, to build a chain of cause and effect. But when it can\u2019t, it feels temporarily paralyzed.\\n\\nThen, as the shock faded, a conviction began to form slowly, and it startled me even more than the coincidence itself. I started to remember clearly, positively, that when I made my sketch of the _scarab\u00e6us_, there had been no drawing on the parchment. I was sure of it. I remembered turning it over, first one side and then the other, looking for the cleanest spot. If the skull had been there at that time, of course I would have noticed it. This was a mystery I felt I couldn\u2019t explain. Still, even then, I sensed\u2014faintly, in the deepest and most hidden part of my mind\u2014a kind of idea, like a glow-worm, about the truth that last night\u2019s adventure had shown so clearly.\\n\\nI stood up at once. I put the parchment away securely and stopped thinking about it until I was alone.\\n\\n\u201cWhen you had gone, and when Jupiter was fast asleep, I turned to a more careful investigation. First, I thought about how the parchment had come into my possession. The spot where we found the _scarab\u00e6us_ was on the mainland coast, about a mile east of the island, and only a short distance above the high-water line. When I picked it up, it bit me sharply, and I had to drop it. Jupiter, as cautious as ever, before he seized the insect\u2014after it flew toward him\u2014looked around for a leaf, or something like that, to use as a way to hold it.\u201d\"}"
