          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f6496cd72466f11a6c705b11\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI\u2019m going, Mr. Will\u2014yes, I am,\u201d the negro answered quickly. \u201cI\u2019m out to the end now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOut to the end!\u201d Legrand shouted. \u201cDo you mean you\u2019re out to the end of that branch?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSoon to the end, sir\u2014o-o-o-o-oh! Lord, mercy! what is this thing up in the tree?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell!\u201d Legrand said, very pleased. \u201cWhat is it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt ain\u2019t nothing but a skull. Somebody left it up there with its head in the tree, and the crows have eaten every bit of the meat off.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cA skull, you say! All right\u2014how is it attached to the branch? What keeps it there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSure enough, sir. I have to look. This is a strange thing, I swear\u2014there\u2019s a big nail in the skull that holds it to the tree.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, Jupiter, do exactly what I tell you. Do you hear me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cListen, then. Find the skull\u2019s left eye.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHum! What? There ain\u2019t no left eye at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCurse your foolishness! Do you know your right hand from your left?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I know that. I know all about it. It\u2019s my left hand that I chop the wood with.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen of course you\u2019re left-handed, and your left eye is on the same side as your left hand. Now, I suppose you can find the skull\u2019s left eye\u2014or where the left eye used to be. Have you found it?\u201d\\n\\nThere was a long pause. At last the negro asked, \u201cIs the skull\u2019s left eye on the same side as the skull\u2019s left hand, too? \u2019Cause the skull don\u2019t have any hand at all. Never mind! I got the left eye now\u2014here it is. What do I do with it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet the beetle drop through it, as far as the string will reach\u2014but don\u2019t let go of the string.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll done, Mr. Will. That\u2019s easy enough. I\u2019ll put the bug out through the hole. Watch out for it down there!\u201d\\n\\nDuring this talk, Jupiter\u2019s body couldn\u2019t be seen at all. But the beetle he had let down was now visible at the end of the string, shining like a globe of polished gold in the last rays of the setting sun. Those rays still faintly lit the hill where we stood. The scarab hung clear of any branches, and if it were allowed to fall, it would drop right at our feet. Legrand immediately took the scythe and cleared a circular patch, three or four yards across, directly under the insect. Then he told Jupiter to let go of the string and come down from the tree.\u201d}\"}"
