rapped in a burning fire. Then he got confused and frightened and ran as fast as he could, not even knowing what he was doing.\\n\\nIt all happened in a minute. The moment Oliver started running, the old gentleman reached into his pocket, realized the handkerchief was gone, and turned sharply around. Seeing the boy sprinting away, he naturally assumed the boy was the thief. He shouted, \u201cStop thief!\u201d as loudly as he could, and ran after him with his book still in his hand.\"}"
