          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d39bf4e4e317d9894fb3cc1e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I consider it one of the first refinements of polished societies.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly, sir; and it has the added advantage of being fashionable even among the less polished societies of the world: every savage can dance.\u201d\\n\\nSir William only smiled. \u201cYour friend performs delightfully,\u201d he continued after a pause, seeing Bingley join the group; \u201cand I doubt not that you are yourself an adept in the science, Mr. Darcy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou saw me dance at Meryton, I believe, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, indeed, and I took no small pleasure in the sight. Do you often dance at St. James\u2019s?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t you think it would be a proper compliment to the place?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s a compliment I never pay to any place if I can avoid it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou have a house in town, I conclude?\u201d\\n\\nMr. Darcy bowed.\\n\\n\u201cI once had thoughts of settling in town myself, for I\u2019m fond of superior society; but I wasn\u2019t quite certain that the air of London would agree with Lady Lucas.\u201d\\n\\nHe paused, hoping for an answer; but his companion was not disposed to give one. At that instant Elizabeth moved toward them, and he was struck by the idea of doing something very gallant, so he called out to her,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Miss Eliza, why aren\u2019t you dancing? Mr. Darcy, you must allow me to present this young lady to you as a very desirable partner. You can\u2019t refuse to dance, I\u2019m sure, when so much beauty is before you.\u201d And, taking her hand, he would have offered it to Mr. Darcy, who, though extremely surprised, was not unwilling to receive it, when she instantly drew back and said, with some discomposure to Sir William,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, sir, I have no intention at all of dancing. I beg you not to suppose that I came this way in order to ask for a partner.\u201d\