uddenly the man pulled up with a jerk at the top of a dark lane. Over the low roofs and jagged chimney-stacks of the houses rose the black masts of ships. Bands of white mist clung to the yards like ghostly sails.\\n\\n\u201cSomewhere about here, sir, ain\u2019t it?\u201d he asked hoarsely through the trap.\\n\\nDorian started and looked round. \u201cThis will do,\u201d he said; and after he had got out quickly and handed the driver the extra fare he\u2019d promised, he walked fast toward the quay. Here and there a lantern shone at the stern of some great merchantman. The light trembled and shattered in the puddles. A red flare came from an outward-bound steamer that was coaling. The slimy pavement looked like wet mackintosh.\"}"
