          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"70c2640f797465051a08077a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"A little after noon, the boys borrowed a small skiff from a citizen who was away, and they set off right then. A few miles below \u201cCave Hollow,\u201d Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cNow, look at this bluff. It all looks the same from the cave hollow\u2014no houses, no wood-yards, just bushes that look alike. But do you see that white spot up there? That\u2019s from a landslide. That\u2019s one of my marks. We\u2019ll go ashore now.\u201d\\n\\nThey landed.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Huck, where we\u2019re standing, you could reach that hole I dug out with a fishing pole. See if you can find it.\u201d\\n\\nHuck looked around carefully, but he couldn\u2019t find anything. Tom walked in with confidence into a thick clump of sumach bushes and said, \u201cHere it is! Look, Huck. It\u2019s the snuggiest hole in the whole country. You keep quiet about it. All along I\u2019ve wanted to be a robber, but I knew I needed a place like this, and the hard part was finding where it was. We\u2019ve got it now, and we\u2019ll keep it secret. But we\u2019ll let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers in, because of course there has to be a gang, or it wouldn\u2019t have any style. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds great, doesn\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt sure does, Tom. But who are we going to rob?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAlmost anybody. We\u2019ll stop people on the road\u2014that\u2019s mostly how it\u2019s done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd kill them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot always. We\u2019ll lock them in the cave until they raise a ransom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s a ransom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMoney. You make them get as much as they can from their friends, and if after a year they still haven\u2019t raised it, then you kill them. That\u2019s the usual way. But you don\u2019t kill the women. You keep the women quiet, but you don\u2019t kill them. They\u2019re always beautiful and rich, and they\u2019re terribly scared. You take their watches and other things, but you always take off your hat and act polite. Robbers are the most polite people, you\u2019ll see that in any book. Well, the women start to like you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave for a week or two, they stop crying. After that, you couldn\u2019t get them to leave. If you tried to drive them out, they\u2019d just turn around and come back. That\u2019s how it is in all the books.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s really great, Tom. I think it\u2019s better than being a pirate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, it\u2019s better in some ways, because it\u2019s close to home, and there are circuses and all that.\u201d\\n\\nBy then everything was ready, and the boys went into the hole, with Tom leading. They worked their way to the far end of the tunnel, then tied their spliced kite strings in place and moved on.\"}"
