rk cavern. Listen to me, and let yourself be softened by speech in which no selfish passion remains.\\n\\n\u201cWe do not know what all this wide world signifies\u2014how it mixes good and evil in such strange measure. Still, we have been placed here and commanded to live and hope. I cannot say what we are meant to hope for; but there is some good beyond us that we must seek, and that is our earthly work. If misfortune comes against us, we must stand against her; we must cast her aside and go on, still trying to discover what it is our nature to desire. Whether this promise of future good is meant as preparation for another existence, I cannot tell; or whether it is simply that, as workers in God\u2019s vineyard, we must lend a hand to smooth the way for those who come after us.\u201d\"}"
