onds meant to keep their tongues quiet were thought to be locked up, with the key tossed away.\\n\\nA shape slipped through a gap at the far end of the ruined building, but they didn\u2019t see it.\\n\\n\u201cTom,\u201d Huckleberry whispered, \u201cdoes this stop us from ever talking\u2014always?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSure it does. It doesn\u2019t matter what comes along\u2014we\u2019ve got to keep mum no matter what. We\u2019d drop down dead\u2014don\u2019t you know that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I guess that\u2019s true.\u201d\\n\\nThey kept whispering for a little while longer. Soon after, a dog began a long, mournful howl just outside\u2014within ten feet of them. The boys clutched at each other at once, in pure terror.\\n\\n\u201cWhich one of us does he mean?\u201d Huckleberry blurted.\\n\\n\u201cI dono\u2014peep through the crack. Quick!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, _you_, Tom!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t\u2014I can\u2019t _do_ it, Huck!\u201d\"}"
