          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"5561842fa2ad5a2dd1c99cc9\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Raymond paced up and down the room, furious. I stood ready to take his complaints and answer them. Adrian leaned against the wall. \u201cThis is completely ridiculous,\u201d he said loudly. \u201cIf you were schoolboys, you couldn\u2019t act more foolishly than this.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou don\u2019t understand,\u201d Raymond replied. \u201cThis is only part of a system\u2014a plan of tyranny that I will never accept. Because I\u2019m the Protector of England, am I supposed to be the only slave in its empire? They invade my privacy, judge my actions, and insult my friends. But I will get rid of the whole thing at once. Be witnesses,\u201d he said, and he pulled the star\u2014the insignia of his office\u2014from his chest and threw it onto the table. \u201cI renounce my office. I give up my power. Whoever wants it can take it!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet him take it,\u201d Adrian snapped. \u201cWhoever thinks he can claim it, or whoever the world decides is your superior. There isn\u2019t a man in England with enough arrogance to do that. Know yourself, Raymond, and your anger will fade, and your self-satisfaction will come back. A few months ago, whenever we prayed for our country\u2019s prosperity\u2014or our own\u2014we prayed at the same time for the Protector\u2019s life and well-being, because they were tied together. Your hours were spent for our benefit. Your ambition was to earn our approval. You decorated our towns with buildings, gave us useful institutions, and made the land more fertile. The powerful and unfair feared you, and the poor and oppressed rose up like flowers in the morning, bright under the sunshine of your protection.\\n\\n\u201cCan you really be surprised that we\u2019re all shocked and grieving when it seems to have changed? But this angry mood is already passing. Go back to your duties. Your supporters will welcome you. Your enemies will be silenced. Our love, honor, and duty toward you will show themselves again. Control yourself, Raymond. The world will be yours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of that would make sense,\u201d Raymond said bitterly, \u201cif it were meant for someone else. Learn the lesson yourself, and you, the first peer of the land, might become its ruler. You, the good, the wise, the just, could rule everyone\u2019s heart. But I see, too soon for my own happiness and too late for England\u2019s good, that I took on a job I can\u2019t handle. I can\u2019t even rule myself. My passions control me; even my smallest impulse is my master. Do you think I gave up the Protectorate\u2014yes, I have given it up\u2014just out of anger? By the God who lives, I swear I will never take that trinket again. Never again will I burden myself with the weight of care and misery that it represents.\u201d\"}"
