          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9a842b78c242c9e63b120f27\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Just as they were leaving the dining-room, midnight began to boom from the clock tower, and when the last stroke sounded they heard a crash and a sudden, shrill cry. A dreadful peal of thunder shook the house; an eerie strain of music drifted through the air. A panel at the top of the staircase flew back with a loud noise, and on the landing\u2014looking very pale and white, with a small casket in her hand\u2014Virginia stepped out. In an instant, they all rushed up to her. Mrs. Otis seized her passionately in her arms, the Duke overwhelmed her with violent kisses, and the twins spun around the group in a wild war-dance.\\n\\n\u201cGood heavens, child! Where have you been?\u201d Mr. Otis demanded, rather angrily, convinced she must have been pulling some foolish trick on them. \u201cCecil and I have been riding all over the country looking for you, and your mother has been frightened to death. You must never play these practical jokes again.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cExcept on the Ghost! Except on the Ghost!\u201d the twins shrieked as they capered about.\\n\\n\u201cMy own darling\u2014thank God you are found. You must never leave my side again,\u201d Mrs. Otis murmured, kissing the trembling child and smoothing the tangled gold of her hair.\\n\\n\u201cPapa,\u201d Virginia said quietly, \u201cI\u2019ve been with the Ghost. He is dead, and you must come and see him. He had been very wicked, but he was truly sorry for everything he\u2019d done, and before he died he gave me this box of beautiful jewels.\u201d\\n\\nThe whole family stared at her in mute amazement, but she was completely grave and serious. Then, turning around, she led them through the opening in the wainscoting into a narrow secret corridor, with Washington following and holding a lighted candle he had grabbed from the table. At last they reached a great oak door, studded with rusty nails. When Virginia touched it, it swung open on its heavy hinges, and they found themselves in a small, low room with a vaulted ceiling and one tiny grated window. Set into the wall was a huge iron ring, and chained to it was a gaunt skeleton stretched out at full length on the stone floor, as if it were trying to grasp\u2014using its long, fleshless fingers\u2014an old-fashioned trencher and ewer placed just out of reach. The jug had evidently once been filled with water, since the inside was covered with green mould. There was nothing on the trencher but a pile of dust. Virginia knelt beside the skeleton, folded her little hands together, and began to pray silently, while the rest of the party watched in wonder at the terrible tragedy whose secret had now been revealed to them.\"}"
