          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"400cdc16be3a05fa2f21eec0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But don\u2019t suppose that I felt it wasn\u2019t an evil in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDepend upon it, they were all quite at ease.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI may not like it the better for that, perhaps. With so many women and children on board, they have no _right_ to be comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you talk in the most idle fashion. Pray, what would become of us poor sailors\u2019 wives\u2014who are often eager to be taken to one port or another\u2014after our husbands, if everyone had your way of thinking?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou see, my feelings didn\u2019t stop me from taking Mrs Harville and all her family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I can\u2019t bear to hear you speak as if you were some fine gentleman, and women were all fine ladies, instead of sensible creatures. None of us expects to be in smooth water every day of our lives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201cwhen he has a wife, he\u2019ll change his tune. Once he\u2019s married\u2014if we\u2019re lucky enough to live to another war\u2014we shall see him do as you and I, and many others, have done. He\u2019ll be very thankful to anyone who can bring his wife to him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAy, that he will.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I have done,\u201d cried Captain Wentworth. \u201cThe moment married people start attacking me with,\u2014\u2018Oh! you\u2019ll feel quite differently when you are married.\u2019 I can only answer, \u2018No, I shan\u2019t;\u2019 and then they say again, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and that\u2019s the end of it.\u201d\\n\\nHe rose and went away.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a fine traveller you must have been, ma\u2019am!\u201d said Mrs Musgrove to Mrs Croft.\\n\\n\u201cPretty well, ma\u2019am, in the fifteen years since I married; though many women have done more. I\u2019ve crossed the Atlantic four times, and been once to the East Indies, and back again, and only once; besides having been in different places at home\u2014Cork, and Lisbon, and Gibraltar. But I never went beyond the Streights, and I never was in the West Indies. We don\u2019t call Bermuda or Bahama, you know, the West Indies.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove had nothing to object; she couldn\u2019t accuse herself of ever having called them anything else in the whole course of her life.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d Mrs Croft went on, \u201cthat nothing can surpass the accommodations of a man-of-war; I mean, of course, the higher rates. When you come to a frigate, you\u2019re more shut in; though any reasonable woman may be perfectly happy in one. And I can safely say that the happiest part of my life has been spent on board a ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to be feared.\u201d\"}"
