          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8c3fd830678b6725173c7010\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The most exquisite gentlemen, bred to the finest degree, wore small pendant gewgaws that chimed as they drifted along in languor; those golden fetters rang out like tiny, treasured bells. Between that tinkling and the whisper of silk, brocade, and fine linen, the air seemed to flutter\u2014fanning Saint Antoine and his devouring appetite far off in the distance.\\n\\nDress was the one sure talisman and charm for keeping everything in its proper place. Everyone was arrayed for a Fancy Ball that was never meant to end. From the Palace of the Tuileries, through Monseigneur and the entire Court, through the Chambers, the Tribunals of Justice, and all society (save the scarecrows), the Fancy Ball descended to the Common Executioner. In keeping with the charm, he was to appear \u201cfrizzled, powdered, in a gold-laced coat, pumps, and white silk stockings.\u201d At the gallows and the wheel\u2014where the axe was a rarity\u2014Monsieur Paris, as was the episcopal fashion among his fellow Professors in the provinces, Monsieur Orleans, and the rest, presided in that dainty attire. And who among the company at Monseigneur\u2019s reception, in that seventeen hundred and eightieth year of our Lord, could possibly doubt that a system planted in a frizzled hangman, powdered, gold-laced, pumped, and white-silk stockinged, would put the very stars to shame!\\n\\nHaving relieved his four men of their burdens and taken his chocolate, Monseigneur caused the doors of the Holiest of Holiests to be thrown open, and then he came forth. After that, what submission, what cringing and fawning, what servility, what abject humiliation! As for bowing down in body and spirit, Heaven was left nothing to receive\u2014which may have been one of the reasons the worshippers of Monseigneur never bothered it.\\n\\nWith a word of promise here and a smile there, a whisper to one fortunate slave and a wave of the hand to