          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ec2a55471b7bd24747a9d9e5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d Duff replied.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, translating the word yokel for the ladies, I take it you mean that this attempt was not made by a countryman?\u201d asked Mr. Losberne, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s it, master,\u201d Blathers said. \u201cThis is all about the robbery, isn\u2019t it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll,\u201d the doctor answered.\\n\\n\u201cNow, what\u2019s this about that boy the servants keep talking about?\u201d Blathers asked.\\n\\n\u201cNothing at all,\u201d the doctor replied. \u201cOne of the frightened servants decided he must have something to do with the attempt to break into the house, but that\u2019s nonsense\u2014pure absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasy enough to dismiss, if it is,\u201d Duff remarked.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is right,\u201d Blathers agreed, nodding as if to confirm it, and idly playing with the handcuffs, as though they were castanets. \u201cBut who is the boy? What story does he tell about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t just fall out of the clouds, did he, master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d the doctor said, glancing nervously at the two ladies. \u201cI know his whole history, but we can talk about that later. First, you\u2019d like to see where the thieves tried to get in, I suppose?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d Mr. Blathers replied. \u201cWe should inspect the place first, then look at the servants afterward. That\u2019s the usual way of doing things.\u201d\\n\\nLights were brought in. Then Messrs. Blathers and Duff, with the native constable Brittles, Giles, and everyone else who was there, went into the small room at the end of the passage and looked out the window. After that, they walked around across the lawn and looked in through the window again. Then someone handed out a candle so they could inspect the shutter. After that, they used a lantern to trace the footsteps. Then they brought out a pitchfork to poke at the bushes. When all of that was done, with everyone watching in breathless excitement, they went back inside. Mr. Giles and Brittles were then made to act out, in a melodramatic way, their part in the adventures from the previous night. They did it about six times, contradicting each other in not more than one important detail the first time, and in no more than a dozen details the last.\\n\\nOnce that was finished, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a long meeting together. It was, for secrecy and seriousness, about as far from a doctor\u2019s discussion of the hardest medical question as you could get.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced in the next room, looking very uneasy. Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched him with anxious faces.\\n\\n\u201cHonestly,\u201d he said, stopping after turning back and forth a great many times, \u201cI hardly know what to do.\u201d\"}"
