          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1298a429b9664a1c3e3b4bab\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At the stairs where we had taken him abroad, and ever since, I had watched closely for any sign that we were being suspected. I had seen nothing. We certainly were not suspected, and at that time we were not being followed or watched by any boat either. If a boat had been waiting for us, I would have run to shore and made it go on, or else made its purpose clear. But we went on without any sign of being bothered.\\n\\nHe had his boat-cloak on, and, as I said, he looked like a natural part of the scene. It was strange, though maybe the miserable life he had lived explains it, that he was the least worried of all of us. He was not indifferent. He told me he hoped to live long enough to see his gentleman become one of the best gentlemen in a foreign country. He was not the kind of man who would give up or accept things quietly, as I understood it. But he also had no intention of meeting danger halfway. When danger came, he faced it, but only when it arrived.\\n\\n\u201cIf you knew, dear boy,\u201d he said to me, \u201cwhat it\u2019s like to sit here with you, alonger my dear boy, and have my smoke, after being shut up day by day behind four walls, you\u2019d envy me. But you don\u2019t know what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think I know the joys of freedom,\u201d I answered.\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d he said, shaking his head seriously. \u201cBut you don\u2019t know it as well as I do. You must have been locked up, dear boy, to know it as well as I do\u2014but I ain\u2019t going to be low.\u201d\\n\\nIt struck me as strange that, if he really wanted to protect his freedom, he would risk it\u2014and even his life. Still, I thought maybe freedom without danger meant less to him than it would to someone else, because danger had been part of his life for so long. I was not far off, since after smoking a little he said:\\n\\n\u201cYou see, dear boy, when I was over yonder, on the other side of the world, I was always looking back to this side. And it started to feel flat, even though I was getting rich. Everyone knew Magwitch, and Magwitch could come and go, and nobody\u2019s mind would be troubled about him. But they don\u2019t feel the same about me here, dear boy. They wouldn\u2019t, at least, if they knew where I was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf all goes well,\u201d I said, \u201cyou\u2019ll be free and safe again within a few hours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d he replied, letting out a long breath, \u201cI hope so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you think so?\u201d\"}"
