d my own. That jab made the fellow squirm. The abbot asked about the queen and the court, and he got this answer:\\n\\n\u201cThey be all on sleep, overcome by fatigue, just like the king.\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s just another lie. Half of them are off with their amusements. The queen and the other half are not sleeping\u2014they ride. Now maybe you can spread yourself a little and tell us where the king and queen and all the rest are going right now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey sleep now, as I said; but on the morrow they will ride, because they go on a journey toward the sea.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd where will they be the day after tomorrow at vespers?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFar to the north of Camelot, and half their journey will be done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s another lie, by the space of a hundred and fifty miles.\u201d\"}"
