e. At the same time, he often showed great generosity. He would work hard to meet other people\u2019s needs, while his own desires were satisfied just as fully. He gave his money, but he did not sacrifice any of his own wishes to the gifts he made. He gave his time, which he did not value, and he gave his affections, which he was happy to put into action in any way.\\n\\nI am not saying that, if his own desires had been forced to compete with those of others, he would have shown selfishness. But that test was never made. He was raised in prosperity and had all the advantages that came with it. Everyone loved him and wanted to please him.\"}"
