seen on the jury, was standing at the little counter, drinking while he talked with the Defarges\u2014husband and wife. The Vengeance took part in the conversation as if he were a regular member of the place.\\n\\nWhen Carton walked in, took his seat, and asked (in very indifferent French) for a small measure of wine, Madame Defarge gave him a careless glance, then a sharper one, then an even sharper one, and finally came over to him herself. She asked what he had ordered.\\n\\nHe repeated what he had already said.\\n\\n\u201cEnglish?\u201d asked Madame Defarge, inquisitively lifting her dark eyebrows.\\n\\nAfter looking at her, as though even the sound of a single French word took time for him to form, he answered in his earlier strong foreign accent.\"}"
