          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0ee511cab3f4f71789c0cec0\",\"rewritten_text\":\"They know well enough how sharp a lad he is; he\u2019ll be a lifer. They\u2019ll see that the Artful gets nothing short of a lifer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean by lagging and a lifer?\u201d Mr. Bolter demanded. \u201cWhat\u2019s the point of speaking like that to me\u2014why don\u2019t yer say it plain, so I can make out what yer mean?\u201d\\n\\nFagin was ready to put those puzzling phrases into the rougher tongue; and, once translated, Mr. Bolter would have been told that they amounted to that phrase, \u201ctransportation for life,\u201d when the talk was cut short by Master Bates coming in, hands shoved into his breeches-pockets, his face twisted in a kind of half-comic misery.\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s all over, Fagin,\u201d said Charley, once he and his new acquaintance had been introduced.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019ve found the gentleman that owns the box; two or three more\u2019s on the way to \u2019dentify him; and the Artful\u2019s booked for a passage out,\u201d Master Bates replied. \u201cI\u2019ll need a proper suit of mourning, Fagin, and a hatband, to wisit him before he starts off on his travels. To think of Jack Dawkins\u2014lummy Jack\u2014the Dodger\u2014the Artful Dodger\u2014going abroad for a common twopenny-halfpenny sneeze-box! I never figured he\u2019d do it under a gold watch, chain, and seals, at the very lowest. Oh, why couldn\u2019t he rob some rich old gentleman of all his walables, and go out as a gentleman, not like some common prig, with no honour nor glory!\u201d\\n\\nWith that burst of feeling for his unlucky mate, Master Bates settled himself in the nearest chair, looking full of chagrin and despair.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean, talking about him having neither honour nor glory!\u201d Fagin snapped, shooting an angry look at his pupil. \u201cWasn\u2019t he always the top-sawyer among you all? Is there one of you that could lay a hand on him, or get near him, on any scent? Eh?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot one,\u201d Master Bates answered, his voice thick with regret; \u201cnot one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen what are you going on about?\u201d Fagin said, still angry; \u201cwhat are you blubbering for?\u201d\\n\\n\u201c\u2019Cause it isn\u2019t on the rec-ord, is it?\u201d Charley said, smarting into open defiance of his old friend through the tide of his own regrets; \u201c\u2019cause it can\u2019t be brought out in the \u2019dictment; \u2019cause nobody will ever know half of what he was. How\u2019s he going to look in the Newgate Calendar? P\u2019raps not be there at all. Oh, my eye, my eye\u2014what a blow it is!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHa! ha!\u201d Fagin laughed, thrusting out his right hand and turning to Mr. Bolter, chuckling so hard it shook him as if he had the palsy. \u201cSee what a pride they take in their profession, my dear.\u201d\"}"
