          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7f1756c8da1722bb7bfcd854\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The insect\u2019s weight was astonishing, and, when I weighed everything, I could scarcely fault Jupiter for the opinion he formed about it; yet I could not, for the life of me, understand how Legrand came to agree with that same view.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he said, in a lofty, sweeping manner, once I had finished examining the beetle. \u201cI sent for you so that I might have your counsel and your help in carrying forward the designs of Fate\u2014and of the bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I broke in, \u201cyou must be unwell. You\u2019d do better to take a few precautions. Go to bed\u2014you shall\u2014and I\u2019ll stay with you for a few days until you\u2019ve shaken this off. You\u2019re feverish, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he replied.\\n\\nI did, and, to be honest, I found not the smallest sign of fever.\\n\\n\u201cBut you might be ill without having fever. Let me prescribe for you just this once. First of all, go to bed. Next\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019re mistaken,\u201d he cut in. \u201cI\u2019m as well as I can reasonably expect to be, given the agitation I\u2019m under. If you truly want me well, you\u2019ll help me put an end to this excitement.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how am I to do that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery simply. Jupiter and I are going on an expedition into the hills, onto the mainland. On this trip we\u2019ll need someone we can rely on. You\u2019re the only person we can trust. Whether we succeed or fail, the excitement you see in me now will be just as thoroughly quieted.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m glad to help in any way I can,\u201d I answered; \u201cbut are you saying that this infernal beetle has something to do with your journey into the hills?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I can\u2019t take part in any such ridiculous business.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m sorry\u2014terribly sorry,\u201d he said, \u201cbut we\u2019ll have to attempt it on our own.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAttempt it on your own! The man must be out of his mind!\u2014but wait\u2014how long do you mean to be gone?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProbably all night. We\u2019ll set out at once, and we\u2019ll be back, at the latest, by sunrise.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you promise me\u2014on your honor\u2014that once your little scheme is finished, and the bug matter (good God!) is settled to your satisfaction, you\u2019ll return home and follow my advice without question, as you would that of a physician?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes; I promise. Now come\u2014we have no time to waste.\u201d\\n\\nWith a heavy heart, I went along with my friend. We set out at about four o\u2019clock\u2014Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and I. Jupiter brought the scythe and the spades, all of which he insisted on carrying himself\u2014more, it seemed to me, out of fear of leaving any of the tools within his master\u2019s reach than from any real excess of diligence or willingness to oblige.\"}"
