          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"bd1f6ff0878680460592be4c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cYou haven\u2019t stayed in Bath long enough,\u201d said he, \u201cto enjoy the evening gatherings there.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh! no. Their usual sort of company has nothing to recommend it to me. I\u2019m no card-player.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou weren\u2019t before, I know. You never cared for cards; but time brings many changes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m not altered so much yet,\u201d cried Anne, and stopped, afraid she scarcely knew how her words might be taken. After a pause, he spoke again, as though the thought had risen at once within him: \u201cIt is indeed a period! Eight years and a half is a period.\u201d\\n\\nWhether he meant to go on further was left for Anne to consider in a calmer hour; for even while she still heard what he had just said, Henrietta startled her into other matters, eager to take advantage of the leisure and get out, urging her companions to make no delay, lest someone else should enter.\\n\\nThey had to rise. Anne declared herself perfectly ready, and tried to appear so; yet she felt that if Henrietta had known the regret and reluctance of her heart in leaving that chair, and then preparing to leave the room, she would have found, in all Anne\u2019s own feelings for her cousin, in the very security of his affection, enough to pity her.\\n\\nTheir preparations, however, were cut short. Disturbing sounds were heard; other visitors drew near, and the door was thrown open for Sir Walter and Miss Elliot, whose arrival seemed to send a chill through everything. Anne felt an instant oppression, and wherever she looked she saw the same signs. The comfort, the ease, the liveliness of the room had vanished, replaced by cold composure, fixed silence, or dull talk, meant to match the heartless elegance of her father and sister. How mortifying to think it was truly so!\\n\\nHer watchful jealousy was satisfied in one point. Captain Wentworth was received again by everyone, by Elizabeth even more kindly than before. She spoke to him once, and looked at him more than once. In fact, Elizabeth was working out a serious plan. The rest soon showed it. After wasting a few minutes on the proper trifles, she began to offer the invitation that would cover all the remaining obligations of the Musgroves. \u201cTo-morrow evening, to meet a few friends: no formal party.\u201d Everything was said with great grace; the cards she had prepared\u2014the \u201cMiss Elliot at home\u201d\u2014were laid on the table with a courteous, comprehensive smile for all, and one smile and one card more pointedly for Captain Wentworth. The truth was that Elizabeth had been in Bath long enough to know how important it was to have a man of such an air and appearance as his.\"}"
