          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2ef2144405257a0304f2537d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNow I hurry to the more moving part of my story. I will describe events that struck me with feelings which, from what I had been, have made me what I am.\\n\\n\u201cSpring advanced quickly; the weather turned fine, and the skies were cloudless. It surprised me that what had been desert and gloomy should now bloom with the most beautiful flowers and green growth. My senses were delighted and refreshed by a thousand delightful scents and a thousand sights of beauty.\\n\\n\u201cIt was on one of these days, when my cottagers periodically rested from their labor\u2014the old man played his guitar, and the children listened\u2014that I noticed Felix\u2019s face was melancholy beyond expression. He sighed often, and once his father paused in his music, and I guessed from his manner that he was asking about the cause of his son\u2019s sorrow. Felix answered in a cheerful tone, and the old man was starting his music again when someone tapped at the door.\\n\\n\u201cIt was a lady on horseback, accompanied by a countryman who served as her guide. The lady wore a dark suit and was covered by a thick black veil. Agatha asked a question, and the stranger replied only by speaking, in a sweet accent, the name of Felix. Her voice was musical, but unlike that of either of my friends. At the sound of that word, Felix hurried to the lady. When she saw him, she lifted her veil, and I saw a face of angelic beauty and expression. Her hair was a shining raven black, and curiously braided; her eyes were dark, yet gentle, though full of life. Her features were evenly proportioned, and her complexion was wonderfully fair, each cheek touched with a lovely pink.\\n\\n\u201cFelix seemed completely overwhelmed with joy when he saw her; every trace of sorrow vanished from his face, and it instantly showed a kind of ecstatic happiness I could hardly have believed possible. His eyes sparkled as his cheeks flushed with pleasure; and at that moment I thought him as beautiful as the stranger. She seemed moved by different feelings. Wiping away a few tears from her lovely eyes, she held out her hand to Felix, who kissed it rapturously and called her\u2014at least as I could make out\u2014his sweet Arabian. She did not seem to understand him, but she smiled. He helped her down from the horse, dismissed her guide, and led her into the cottage. Some conversation followed between him and his father. The young stranger then knelt at the old man\u2019s feet and would have kissed his hand, but he lifted her and embraced her warmly.\\n\\n\u201cI soon realized that although the stranger spoke in clear, articulated sounds and seemed to have a language of her own, she was neither understood by the cottagers nor did she herself understand them.\u201d\"}"
