d to wait while the widow bowed her head and grumbled a little about the food, even though there really wasn\u2019t anything wrong with it. The only problem was that everything was cooked separately. In a barrel of odds and ends, it\u2019s different. Things get mixed together, the juices trade places, and everything tastes better.\\n\\nAfter supper she took out her book and taught me about Moses and the Bulrushers. I was eager to learn everything about him, but later she let it slip that Moses had been dead for a long time. After that, I didn\u2019t care anymore, because I don\u2019t believe in dead people.\"}"
