o a question I\u2019m going to ask you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnother time, Lord Arthur, but the Duchess is anxious. I\u2019m afraid I have to go.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou won\u2019t go. The Duchess isn\u2019t in a hurry.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLadies shouldn\u2019t be kept waiting, Lord Arthur,\u201d said Mr. Podgers, with his sickly smile. \u201cThe fair sex is apt to be impatient.\u201d\\n\\nLord Arthur\u2019s finely cut lips curled with petulant disdain. The poor Duchess seemed to him of very little importance at that moment. He crossed the room to where Mr. Podgers was standing and held out his hand.\\n\\n\u201cTell me what you saw there,\u201d he said. \u201cTell me the truth. I have to know it. I\u2019m not a child.\u201d\"}"
