          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"9a81a38a3300bc5b918df487\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I wrapped him up in the paper and put the pieces in his mouth\u2014that was the way.\\n\\n\u201cAnd you think, then, that your master was really bitten by the beetle, and that the bite made him sick?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t think about it\u2014I know. Why would he dream about gold so much, if he wasn\u2019t bitten by the gold bug? I heard about those gold bugs before this.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut how do you know he dreams about gold?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow do I know? Because he talks about it in his sleep\u2014that\u2019s how I know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, Jup, perhaps you are right; but what lucky reason brings you here to visit me today?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s the matter, massa?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid you bring any message from Mr. Legrand?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, massa, I bring this here note;\u201d and here Jupiter handed me a note that said:\\n\\n\u201cMY DEAR \u2014\u2014Why have I not seen you for so long? I hope you have not been so foolish as to take offense at any little _brusquerie_ of mine; but no, that is unlikely. Since I saw you, I have had great cause for anxiety. I have something to tell you, but I can hardly say it, and I don\u2019t know whether I should tell it at all.\\n\\n\u201cI have not been quite well for some days now, and poor old Jup annoys me, almost beyond endurance, with his well-meant attentions. Would you believe it?\u2014the other day he had prepared a huge stick to punish me for slipping away and spending the day, _solus_, among the hills on the mainland. I truly believe my bad looks alone saved me from being flogged.\\n\\n\u201cI have made no additions to my cabinet since we met.\\n\\n\u201cIf you can, in any way, make it convenient, come over with Jupiter. _Do_ come. I want to see you tonight, on business of the _highest_ importance. I assure you it is of the _highest_ importance.\\n\\n\u201cEver yours, \u201cWILLIAM LEGRAND\u201d.\\n\\n\u201cThere was something in the tone of this note that made me feel very uneasy. Its style was quite different from Legrand\u2019s usual way of writing. What could he be thinking about? What new idea had taken over his excitable mind? And what Jupiter said about him did not sound good. I feared that the steady pressure of bad luck had finally shaken my friend\u2019s judgment. Without waiting, I decided to go with the negro.\\n\\n\u201cWhen we reached the wharf, I saw a scythe and three spades lying at the bottom of the boat we were going to take.\\n\\n\u201cWhat is the meaning of all this, Jup?\u201d\"}"
