          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1a037dde46b13ae67e8ef3ac\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Smallpox!\\n\\nI rushed to the king and spoke quietly in his ear.\\n\\n\u201cGo out the door right now, sire. The woman is dying of the disease that struck Camelot two years ago.\u201d\\n\\nHe didn\u2019t move.\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll stay,\u201d he said, \u201cand I\u2019ll help as well.\u201d\\n\\nI whispered again. \u201cKing, you can\u2019t do this. You must leave.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou mean well, and you\u2019re not speaking foolishly. But it would be shameful for a king to admit fear, and shameful for a knight with a belt to hold back his hand when people need help. I won\u2019t go. You must go instead. The Church\u2019s ban isn\u2019t on me, but it forbids you to be here. If she hears about your trespass, she will punish you severely.\u201d\\n\\nIt was a dangerous position for him, one that could cost him his life, but there was no point arguing. If he believed his knightly honor was at stake, then that was the end of the discussion. He would stay, and nothing would change his mind. So I dropped the subject.\\n\\nThe woman spoke.\\n\\n\u201cGood sir, will you climb the ladder there and bring me word about what you find? Don\u2019t be afraid to tell me. There may come a time when even a mother\u2019s heart can\u2019t break anymore\u2014because it has already broken.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWait,\u201d the king said. \u201cGive the woman something to eat. I\u2019ll go.\u201d Then he set down the knapsack.\\n\\nI started to turn, but the king had already begun to move. He stopped and looked down at a man lying in a dim light. He hadn\u2019t noticed us until now, and he hadn\u2019t spoken.\\n\\n\u201cIs that your husband?\u201d the king asked.\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs he asleep?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank God, yes\u2014that one mercy. For three hours.\u201d Her voice shook as she added, \u201cWhere can I ever repay you for that? My heart is bursting with gratitude for the sleep he has now.\u201d\\n\\nI said, \u201cWe\u2019ll be careful. We won\u2019t wake him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, no,\u201d she said. \u201cYou won\u2019t. He\u2019s dead.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDead?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. What a victory it is to know it. No one can harm him now, and no one can insult him anymore. He is in heaven, and happy\u2014or if he isn\u2019t, then he\u2019s in hell and content. In that place, he won\u2019t find any abbot or bishop. We were boy and girl together. We were man and wife for twenty-five years, and we were never apart until today. Think how long it is to love and suffer side by side. This morning he was out of his mind, and in his thoughts we were boy and girl again, wandering in the happy fields. And so, in that innocent, joyful talk, he wandered farther and farther\u2014into places we don\u2019t know about\u2014until he was shut away from the sight of mortal people.\u201d\"}"
