ce of their life. He felt more cheerful as he thought it through, and with sober determination he set out the course he would follow. He remembered that he had promised Perdita he would be there this very evening\u2014the 19th of October, the anniversary of his election as Protector\u2014at a festival held in his honor. This festival should be a good sign for the happiness of future years. First, he would go to see Evadne. He would not stay long. Still, he owed her some explanation, some compensation for his long absence and his silence. Then he would return to Perdita, to the world he had neglected, to the duties of society, to the pride of rank, and to the pleasures of power.\\n\\nAfter the scene described in the previous pages, Perdita had expected Raymond to change completely in his manners and behavior. She hoped for easier conversation and a return to the warm, affectionate way of being together that had always been the joy of her life.\"}"
