          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1aaf867053a3c488f4b4f686\",\"rewritten_text\":\"It looked like a collection of back lanes, ditches, and small gardens, giving the whole place the feel of a rather dull retirement. Wemmick\u2019s house was a little wooden cottage set among plots of garden, and the top of it had been cut out and painted to look like a battery bristling with guns.\\n\\n\u201cMy own doing,\u201d said Wemmick. \u201cLooks pretty, doesn\u2019t it?\u201d\\n\\nI highly commended it, I think it was the smallest house I\u2019d ever seen; with the strangest gothic windows (most of them were fake), and a gothic door almost too small to get into.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s a real flagstaff,\u201d said Wemmick. \u201cAnd on Sundays I run up a real flag. Then look here. After I\u2019ve crossed this bridge, I hoist it up\u2014like this\u2014and cut off the communication.\u201d\\n\\nThe bridge was just a plank, spanning a chasm about four feet wide and two deep. Still, it was pleasant to watch the pride with which he lifted it and secured it; he smiled while doing it, with real relish rather than just mechanically.\\n\\n\u201cAt nine o\u2019clock every night, Greenwich time,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cthe gun fires. There he is, you see! And when you hear him go, I think you\u2019ll say he\u2019s a Stinger.\u201d\\n\\nThe piece of ordnance he referred to was mounted in a separate fortress made of lattice-work. It was protected from the weather by an ingenious little tarpaulin contrivance, like an umbrella.\\n\\n\u201cThen, at the back,\u201d said Wemmick, \u201cout of sight, so it doesn\u2019t interfere with the idea of fortifications\u2014for it\u2019s a principle with me: if you have an idea, carry it out and keep it going\u2014now, I don\u2019t know whether that\u2019s your opinion\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI said, decisively.\\n\\n\u201c\u2014At the back there\u2019s a pig, and there are fowls and rabbits; then I knock together my own little frame, you see, and grow cucumbers; and you\u2019ll judge at supper what kind of salad I can raise. So, sir,\u201d said Wemmick, smiling again, but seriously too as he shook his head, \u201cif you can imagine the little place under siege, it would hold out a devil of a time when it comes to provisions.\u201d\\n\\nThen he led me to a bower about a dozen yards away, though you had to reach it by such clever twists of path that it took quite a while to get there; and in this retreat our glasses were already set out. Our punch was cooling in an ornamental lake, with the bower raised along its edge. This stretch of water\u2014circular in shape, with an island in the middle that might have been the salad for supper\u2014had a fountain in it. When you set a little mill going and took a cork out of a pipe, it played with such force that it made the back of your hand quite wet.\"}"
