          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"961de04087b645822bd30fc4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was plenty of cold water to finish the feast with. After a while, Becky suggested that they move on again. Tom was quiet for a moment. Then he said:\\n\\n\u201cBecky, can you handle it if I tell you something?\u201d\\n\\nBecky\u2019s face went pale, but she thought she could.\\n\\n\u201cWell, then, Becky, we have to stay here\u2014where there\u2019s water to drink. That little piece is our last candle!\u201d\\n\\nBecky broke into tears and loud, helpless wailing. Tom did what he could to comfort her, but it didn\u2019t help much. At last Becky said:\\n\\n\u201cTom!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, Becky?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019ll miss us and hunt for us!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, they will! Of course they will!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMaybe they\u2019re hunting for us right now, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, I guess maybe they are. I hope they are.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhen would they miss us, Tom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhen they get back to the boat, I reckon.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTom, it might be dark then\u2014would they notice we hadn\u2019t come?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. But either way, your mother would miss you as soon as they got home.\u201d\\n\\nA frightened look crossed Becky\u2019s face, and it snapped Tom back to his senses. He realized he\u2019d made a mistake. Becky wasn\u2019t supposed to go home that night! The children fell silent, each lost in thought. After a moment, Becky\u2019s grief surged again, and Tom understood that what he\u2019d been thinking had hit her too\u2014that Sabbath morning might already be half over before Mrs. Thatcher discovered that Becky wasn\u2019t at Mrs. Harper\u2019s.\\n\\nThe children stared at their little bit of candle and watched it melt slowly and mercilessly away; saw the wick, finally standing alone; saw the weak flame rise and fall, climb the thin column of smoke, linger at the top for a moment, and then\u2014total darkness took over, in all its horror!\\n\\nHow long afterward it was that Becky came to a slow awareness that she was crying in Tom\u2019s arms, neither of them could say. All they knew was that, after what felt like a long stretch of time, both of them woke from a dead, numb sleep and started suffering again. Tom said it might be Sunday now\u2014maybe Monday. He tried to get Becky to talk, but her sorrow was too heavy; all her hopes were gone. Tom said they must have been missed long ago, and no doubt the search was already underway. He tried to shout, and maybe someone would come. He did try it, but in the darkness the distant echoes sounded so dreadful that he stopped.\\n\\nThe hours dragged on, and hunger tormented them again. A portion of Tom\u2019s half of the cake was left; they divided it and ate it. But they seemed hungrier than before.\"}"
