ither continue on without noticing, or answer with a couple of words and then go back to say the sentence over again. So interruptions only did harm; and yet I had to interrupt\u2014quite often, too\u2014if I meant to save my life. A man would die if he let her monotony drip on him all day.\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d I said, in my distress. She simply went right back and began again:\\n\\n\u201cSo they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhich two?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSir Gawaine and Sir Uwaine. And so they came to an abbey of monks, and there were well lodged. So on the morn they heard their masses in the abbey, and so they rode forth till they came to a great forest; then was Sir Gawaine aware in a valley by a turret, of twelve fair damsels, and two knights armed on great horses, and the damsels went to and fro by a tree.\u201d\"}"
