          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"aeda5423a8c97f6770c20084\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I went from shop to shop, buying whatever I needed to match the change in his appearance. Once that was done, I turned my attention to Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was at his desk, but when he saw me come in, he stood up right away and positioned himself in front of his fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d he said, \u201cbe careful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I answered. As I walked there, I had already decided what I was going to say.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t commit yourself,\u201d Mr. Jaggers warned, \u201cand don\u2019t commit anyone else. You understand\u2014anyone. Don\u2019t tell me anything. I don\u2019t want to know anything. I am not curious.\u201d\\n\\nOf course, I could tell he knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI only want, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto make sure that what I\u2019ve been told is true. I don\u2019t really expect it to be false, but I can at least check it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cWhen you said \u2018told,\u2019 did you mean \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked. He kept his head tilted to one side. He wasn\u2019t looking at me; he was looking at the floor, as if he were listening to it. \u201cTold sounds like it was spoken to him. You can\u2019t have spoken communication with a man in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will say \u2018informed,\u2019 Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person named Abel Magwitch that he is the benefactor, the one I didn\u2019t even know about before.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers. \u201cIn New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd only him?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd only him,\u201d Mr. Jaggers said.\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m not so foolish, sir, as to think you\u2019re responsible for my mistakes and wrong conclusions. Still, I always thought it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you say, Pip,\u201d Mr. Jaggers replied. He looked at me calmly, then took a bite of his forefinger. \u201cI\u2019m not responsible for that at all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd yet it looked so much like it, sir,\u201d I said, my heart heavy.\\n\\n\u201cNot a bit of evidence, Pip,\u201d he said, shaking his head and gathering up his skirts. \u201cDon\u2019t trust how things look. Trust the evidence. That\u2019s the best rule.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing more to say,\u201d I sighed after standing quietly for a moment. \u201cI\u2019ve checked my information, and that\u2019s the end of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having finally revealed himself,\u201d Mr. Jaggers said, \u201cyou will understand, Pip, how strictly I have followed the facts in everything I\u2019ve said to you. There has never been the slightest change from the strict line of fact. You know that, don\u2019t you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cQuite, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI told Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014when he first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014that he must not expect me ever to stray from the strict line of fact.\u201d}\"}"
