          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"79f63e0fa5beb4332847e33e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d Oliver demanded.\\n\\n\u201cHush!\u201d answered the Dodger. \u201cDo you spot that old gentleman at the book-stall?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe one across the way?\u201d Oliver said. \u201cYes, I can see him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019ll do,\u201d said the Dodger.\\n\\n\u201cA fine choice,\u201d Master Charley Bates remarked.\\n\\nOliver stared from one to the other, utterly astonished; yet he wasn\u2019t allowed to ask questions. The two boys slipped quietly across the road and crept close behind the old gentleman toward whom they\u2019d directed his attention. Oliver followed a few paces, unsure whether to come on or fall back, and stood watching in silent amazement.\\n\\nThe old gentleman looked thoroughly respectable: a powdered head and gold spectacles. He wore a bottle-green coat with a black velvet collar, white trousers, and kept a smart bamboo cane tucked under his arm. He had picked up a book from the stall and stood there reading with the same intensity as if he were settled in his own arm-chair. It was quite likely he imagined himself there, too; for his absorption showed that he saw nothing of the book-stall, the street, the boys, or anything else\u2014only the book itself. He read straight through, turning over the leaf when he reached the bottom of a page, starting at the top line of the next, and carrying on with the greatest interest and eagerness.\\n\\nOliver\u2019s dread and alarm were immediate as he stood a few paces off, staring with his eyes as wide as they could be, to watch the Dodger thrust his hand into the old gentleman\u2019s pocket and pull out a handkerchief. Then to see him pass it to Charley Bates, and at last to witness both of them darting away around the corner at full speed!\\n\\nIn an instant, the whole business of the handkerchiefs, the watches, the jewels, and the Jew himself, came crashing into the boy\u2019s mind.\\n\\nFor a moment he stood frozen, the blood racing through his veins with terror, as though he were in a blazing fire; then, bewildered and frightened, he ran\u2014without knowing what he was doing\u2014making off as fast as his feet could carry him.\\n\\nIt was all over within a minute. The instant Oliver began to bolt, the old gentleman, reaching into his pocket and finding his handkerchief gone, wheeled sharply round. Seeing the boy tearing away at such a pace, he naturally took him for the thief; and, clutching his book, he shouted \u201cStop thief!\u201d with all his might and chased after him.\"}"
