d one tiny barred window. \\n\\nIn the wall was a large iron ring, and chained to it was a gaunt skeleton stretched out on the stone floor. It seemed to be trying to reach, with its long, fleshless fingers, for an old-fashioned trencher and ewer placed just out of reach. The jug had clearly once held water, because the inside was coated with green mould. There was nothing on the trencher except a pile of dust. Virginia knelt beside the skeleton, folded her hands, and began to pray silently. The rest of the group watched in wonder as the terrible secret of the tragedy was finally revealed to them.\"}"
