\\nThe old lady snapped around and pulled her skirts out of harm\u2019s way. The lad bolted at once, scrambled up the high board-fence, and vanished over it.\\n\\nHis aunt Polly stood there, startled for a beat, and then let out a gentle laugh.\\n\\n\u201cHang the boy\u2014can\u2019t I never learn anything? Ain\u2019t he played me tricks enough that I ought to be watching for him by now? But old fools is the biggest fools there is. Can\u2019t teach an old dog new tricks, as the saying goes. Still, goodness\u2014he never does it the same way two days running, and how\u2019s a body supposed to know what\u2019s coming? He \u2019pears to know just how long he can torment me before I get my dander up, and he knows if he can manage to put me off for a minute or make me laugh, then it\u2019s all gone again and I can\u2019t hit him a lick.\u201d\"}"
