          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ca468d97240352074a0d8afd\",\"rewritten_text\":\"By late reports from Rotterdam, that city seems to be in a state of intense philosophical excitement. Indeed, phenomena have there occurred of such a nature\u2014so completely unexpected, so entirely new, so utterly at odds with the opinions people held beforehand\u2014that I have no doubt in my mind that, long before now, all Europe will be in an uproar, all physics in a ferment, and all reason and astronomy will be at each other\u2019s throats.\\n\\nIt appears that on the\u2014\u2014 day of\u2014\u2014 (I\u2019m not sure of the date), a vast crowd of people, for purposes not specifically mentioned, gathered in the great square of the Exchange in the well-run city of Rotterdam. The day was warm\u2014unusually warm for the season\u2014there was hardly any breath of air stirring; and the multitude were in no bad mood about being, from time to time, lightly sprinkled with friendly showers of brief duration that fell from large white masses of cloud, which flickered and shifted across the blue vault of the sky. Still, around noon, a slight but remarkable agitation became clear in the crowd: the clattering of ten thousand tongues was heard; and, an instant later, ten thousand faces were tilted upward toward the heavens, ten thousand pipes were lowered at the same time from the corners of ten thousand mouths, and a shout\u2014something like nothing but the roaring of Niagara\u2014rang out, long, loud, and furious, through all the surrounding areas of Rotterdam.\\n\\nThe source of this commotion soon became obvious enough. From behind the huge bulk of one of those sharply defined masses of cloud already mentioned, there was seen slowly to emerge into an open stretch of blue space a strange, mixed, but apparently solid substance\u2014shaped so oddly, put together so whimsically\u2014that no one could make sense of it, and no one among the sturdy burghers standing below could stop staring. What could it be? In the name of all the vrows and devils in Rotterdam, what could it possibly mean? No one knew, no one could imagine; no one\u2014even the burgomaster, Mynheer Superbus Von Underduk\u2014had the slightest clue for unraveling the mystery. So, since nothing more reasonable could be done, each person, one by one, carefully put his pipe back in the corner of his mouth, cocked his right eye upward at the phenomenon, puffed, paused, waddled around, and grunted meaningfully\u2014then waddled back, grunted, paused, and finally\u2014puffed again.\\n\\nMeanwhile, though, the object of all that curiosity\u2014and the cause of all that smoke\u2014came lower and lower toward the good city. In just a few minutes it drew close enough to be seen clearly. It appeared to be\u2014yes!\u2014undoubtedly a species of balloon; but surely no such balloon had ever been seen in Rotterdam before.\"}"
