          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"df3db120a617cdf5e801702e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But in that harsh rant about Chantilly, printed in yesterday\u2019s \u201cMus\u00e9e,\u201d the satirist made some ugly references to how the cobbler changed his name when he took up the buskin. Then he quoted a Latin line we have talked about many times. I mean the line\\n\\nPerdidit antiquum litera prima sonum.\\n\\n\u201cI told you that this line was meant to refer to Orion, which used to be written Urion. And because of the sharp hints in the way I explained it, I knew you couldn\u2019t have forgotten. So it was obvious you would put together the two ideas of Orion and Chantilly. The fact that you did combine them was clear from the smile that crossed your lips. You were thinking about the poor cobbler\u2019s destruction. Up to then, you had been walking with a slight bend in your posture, but now I saw you straighten up to your full height. At that moment, I was sure you were thinking about how small Chantilly is. Then I interrupted your thoughts to say that, since he really was a very little man, Chantilly would do better at the Th\u00e9\u00e2tre des Vari\u00e9t\u00e9s.\u201d\\n\\nNot long after that, we were looking through an evening edition of the \u201cGazette des Tribunaux\u201d when the following paragraphs caught our attention.\\n\\n\u201cExtraordinary Murders.\u2014This morning, at about three o\u2019clock, the people of the Quartier St. Roch were woken from sleep by a series of terrifying screams. They seemed to be coming from the fourth floor of a house on the Rue Morgue, a place known to be occupied only by Madame L\u2019Espanaye and her daughter, Mademoiselle Camille L\u2019Espanaye. After some delay\u2014caused by a failed attempt to get in the usual way\u2014the gate was forced open with a crowbar. Eight or ten neighbors entered with two gendarmes. By then, the screams had stopped. But as the group rushed up the first flight of stairs, they could hear two or more rough voices arguing angrily, and it seemed the voices were coming from the top part of the house. When they reached the second landing, those sounds also stopped, and everything was perfectly quiet. The party searched room to room, moving quickly. When they arrived at a large back room on the fourth story\u2014where the door was found locked, with the key still inside, so they had to force it open\u2014they saw something that filled everyone there with horror as well as amazement.\\n\\n\u201cThe room was in the wildest mess. The furniture was broken and thrown in every direction. There was only one bedstead, and the bed had been taken off and thrown into the middle of the floor. On a chair sat a razor covered in blood.\u201d\"}"
