          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"450e5c48bd4612e3383c252c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Everything was settled in a friendly, satisfactory way, so the contract was formally agreed to with another small cup of the peppermint mixture. This was especially necessary because the lady\u2019s spirits were fluttering and unsettled. While the mixture was being finished, she told Mr. Bumble that the old woman had died.\\n\\n\u201cVery good,\u201d said Mr. Bumble, sipping his peppermint. \u201cI\u2019ll stop by Sowerberry\u2019s on my way home and tell him to send it tomorrow morning. Was it that which frightened you, love?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt wasn\u2019t anything in particular, dear,\u201d the lady said, trying to avoid the question.\\n\\n\u201cIt must have been something, love,\u201d Mr. Bumble pressed. \u201cWon\u2019t you tell your own B.?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot now,\u201d the lady replied. \u201cOne of these days. After we\u2019re married, dear.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAfter we\u2019re married!\u201d Mr. Bumble exclaimed. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t any impudence from any of those male paupers\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, no, love!\u201d the lady interrupted quickly.\\n\\n\u201cIf I thought it was,\u201d Mr. Bumble went on, \u201cif I thought any of them had dared to look at that lovely face\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey wouldn\u2019t have dared to do it, love,\u201d the lady answered.\\n\\n\u201cThey had better not!\u201d Mr. Bumble said, clenching his fist. \u201cLet me see any man, whether he\u2019s from the parish or not, who would presume to do it, and I\u2019ll tell him he won\u2019t do it a second time!\u201d\\n\\nWithout any fancy show of violence, this might not have sounded like the highest praise for the lady\u2019s looks. But because Mr. Bumble backed up his threat with plenty of angry, warlike gestures, she felt very touched by it and insisted, with great admiration, that he was truly a dove.\\n\\nThe dove then pulled up his coat collar and put on his cocked hat. After sharing a long, affectionate embrace with his future partner, he faced the cold night air again. He only paused for a few minutes in the male paupers\u2019 ward, where he let them have a bit of abuse, just to make sure he could do the job of workhouse-master with the right sharpness. Once he was satisfied he could handle it, Mr. Bumble left the building with a light heart and bright hopes of being promoted. Those thoughts kept him busy until he reached the undertaker\u2019s shop.\\n\\nNow, Mr. and Mrs. Sowerberry had gone out for tea and supper, and Noah Claypole was never the kind of person to take on more physical effort than was needed for eating and drinking. So the shop was not closed, even though it was past the usual time for shutting up. Mr. Bumble tapped his cane on the counter several times, but no one answered. Seeing a light through the glass window of the small back room, he decided to look in and see what was happening. When he saw what was happening, he was quite surprised.\"}"
