ing at Lady Windermere\u2019s. I hope her ladyship is doing well. Would you mind sitting with me while I finish breakfast? There\u2019s an excellent p\u00e2t\u00e9, and my friends say my Rhine wine is better than anything they get at the German Embassy.\u201d\\n\\nBefore Lord Arthur could fully get over the shock of being recognized, he found himself seated in the back room, sipping a delicious Marcobr\u00fcnner from a pale yellow hock-glass marked with the Imperial monogram, and chatting in the most friendly way with the well-known conspirator.\\n\\n\u201cExplosive clocks,\u201d said Herr Winckelkopf, \u201caren\u2019t very good for sending abroad. Even if they manage to get through the Custom House, the train service is so unreliable that they usually go off before they reach the place they were meant to arrive.\u201d\"}"
