 fear and worry, while the old housekeeper bathed her forehead with eau-de-cologne. \\n\\nMr. Otis immediately insisted that she should eat something, and he ordered supper for the whole party. It was a sad meal. Hardly anyone spoke, and even the twins were quiet and subdued, because they were very fond of their sister. After they finished, Mr. Otis, even though the little Duke begged him not to, ordered them all to bed. He said nothing more could be done that night, and that in the morning he would telegraph Scotland Yard to have detectives sent down right away.\"}"
