          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"15b694428add710706d74749\",\"rewritten_text\":\"This was invitation enough.\\n\\n\u201cWhy, my dear, you must know that Mrs. Long says Netherfield has been taken by a young man with a large fortune from the north of England. He came down on Monday in a carriage with four horses to look at the place, and he was so pleased with it that he agreed with Mr. Morris right away. He plans to move in before Michaelmas, and some of his servants will be in the house by the end of next week.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat is his name?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBingley.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs he married or single?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, single, my dear, of course! A single man with a large fortune\u2014four or five thousand a year. What a wonderful thing for our girls!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow so? How could it affect them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Mr. Bennet,\u201d his wife replied, \u201chow can you be so tiresome? You must know I\u2019m thinking about him marrying one of them.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs that his plan in settling here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPlan? Nonsense. How can you talk like that? But it\u2019s very possible he may fall in love with one of them, so you must visit him as soon as he arrives.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t see any reason for that. You and the girls can go\u2014or you can send them on their own, which might even be better. After all, you\u2019re as handsome as any of them, so Mr. Bingley might prefer you most of all.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear, you flatter me. I admit I once had my share of beauty, but I don\u2019t pretend to be anything extraordinary now. When a woman has five grown-up daughters, she should stop thinking about her own looks.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIn that case, a woman usually doesn\u2019t have much beauty to think about.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut, my dear, you really must go and see Mr. Bingley when he comes to the neighborhood.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m afraid I can\u2019t promise that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut think about your daughters. Just imagine what a good match it would be for one of them. Sir William and Lady Lucas are determined to go, just for that reason. You know they usually don\u2019t visit new people. In fact, you must go, because it will be impossible for us to visit him if you don\u2019t.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019re being too careful, surely. I\u2019m sure Mr. Bingley will be very happy to see you, and I will send a few lines by you to let him know I fully approve of his marrying whichever girl he chooses\u2014though I must add a good word for my little Lizzy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t want you to do that. Lizzy isn\u2019t any better than the others. And I\u2019m sure she isn\u2019t half as handsome as Jane, nor half as good-tempered as Lydia.\u201d\"}"
