thes, seemed to have been occupied arranging papers in the iron chest already mentioned, which had been wheeled into the middle of the room. It was open, and its contents lay beside it on the floor. The victims must have been seated with their backs toward the window; and, judging by the interval between the beast\u2019s entry and the screams, it seems likely it was not noticed at once. The shutter\u2019s sudden flapping would naturally have been blamed on the wind.\\n\\nAs the sailor peered in, the huge creature had already seized Madame L\u2019Espanaye by the hair\u2014loose, as she had been combing it\u2014and was brandishing the razor about her face, mimicking the movements of a barber.\"}"
