ds,\u201d printed there in Roman capitals of gigantic size.\\n\\n\u201cGadso!\u201d said the undertaker, grabbing Mr. Bumble by the gilt-edged lapel of his official coat. \u201cThat\u2019s exactly what I wanted to talk to you about. You know\u2014dear me, what an elegant button this is, Mr. Bumble! I never noticed it before.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I think it\u2019s rather pretty,\u201d said the beadle, looking down proudly at the large brass buttons that decorated his coat. \u201cThe design is the same as the parish seal\u2014the Good Samaritan healing the sick and bruised man. The board gave it to me on New Year\u2019s morning, Mr. Sowerberry. I remember putting it on for the first time to attend the inquest on that reduced tradesman who died in a doorway at midnight.\u201d\"}"
