          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d8fb6dfc48b8dd678662bbf5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cOne word more, Rose. Dearest Rose\u2014one more!\u201d Harry cried, throwing himself before her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014less fortunate, as the world would call it\u2014if some obscure and peaceful life had been my destiny\u2014if I had been poor, sick, helpless\u2014would you have turned from me then? Or has my likely rise to riches and honor given this hesitation its birth?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t press me to answer,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cThe question doesn\u2019t arise, and never will. It\u2019s unfair\u2014almost unkind\u2014to urge it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I almost dare to hope,\u201d Harry retorted, \u201cit will cast a gleam of happiness on my lonely path and light the way ahead. It isn\u2019t an idle thing to do, by speaking just a few brief words, for someone who loves you more than anything. Oh, Rose\u2014in the name of my ardent and enduring attachment; in the name of all I have suffered for you, and all you doom me to endure\u2014answer me this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, if your lot had been cast differently,\u201d Rose answered, \u201cif you had been even a little, but not so far, above me; if I could have been a help and comfort to you in some humble scene of peace and retirement, and not a stain and burden in ambitious, distinguished crowds\u2014I should have been spared this trial. I have every reason to be happy, very happy, now; but then, Harry, I admit I should have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nAs she made this confession, busy memories of old hopes\u2014cherished since she was a girl\u2014came crowding into Rose\u2019s mind; but they brought tears with them, as old hopes do when they return, dried up and ruined, and yet they also relieved her.\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t help this weakness, and it only makes my purpose stronger,\u201d Rose said, extending her hand. \u201cI must leave you now, indeed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI ask