          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"5c6f983a29b66696d48d78fe\",\"rewritten_text\":\"A little after noon, the boys borrowed a small skiff from a citizen who was away, and they set off right then. Several miles below \u201cCave Hollow,\u201d Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cNow, look at this bluff\u2014it all looks the same all the way down from the cave hollow. No houses, no wood-yards, just bushes that look alike. But do you see that white spot up there, where there\u2019s been a landslide? That\u2019s one of my marks. We\u2019ll get ashore now.\u201d\\n\\nThey landed.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Huck, right where we\u2019re standing, you could reach that hole I dug out with a fishing pole. See if you can find it.\u201d\\n\\nHuck searched the area and found nothing. Tom marched in proudly and pushed into a thick clump of sumach bushes.\\n\\n\u201cHere you are! Look at it, Huck\u2014it\u2019s the snuggiest hole in the whole country. You keep quiet about it. All along I\u2019ve wanted to be a robber, but I knew I\u2019d need something like this, and the hard part was finding where to stumble on it. We\u2019ve got it now, and we\u2019ll keep it secret. Only we\u2019ll let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers in\u2014because, of course, there has to be a Gang, or it wouldn\u2019t have any style. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds splendid, doesn\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, it does, Tom. And who are we going to rob?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, just about anybody. We mostly waylay people\u2014that\u2019s the main way.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd kill them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot always. Lock them up in the cave until they raise a ransom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s a ransom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMoney. You make them raise as much as they can from their friends, and after you\u2019ve kept them a year, if they haven\u2019t raised it, then you kill them. That\u2019s the general plan. Only you don\u2019t kill the women. You keep the women quiet, but you don\u2019t kill them. They\u2019re always beautiful and rich, and they\u2019re terribly scared. You take their watches and things, but you always take your hat off and talk politely. There aren\u2019t any robbers as polite as you\u2019ll see in any book. Well, the women end up loving you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave a week or two, they stop crying. After that, you couldn\u2019t get them to leave. If you drove them out, they\u2019d just turn around and come right back. That\u2019s how it is in all the books.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, it\u2019s really great, Tom. I think it\u2019s better than being a pirate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, it\u2019s better in some ways, because it\u2019s close to home, and there are circuses and all that.\u201d\\n\\nBy then everything was ready, and the boys entered the hole, Tom leading. They worked their way to the far end of the tunnel, then tied their spliced kite strings in place and moved on.\"}"
