          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"58286d30fe02b67efaf96d65\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNow I hurry to the more important part of my story. I will describe events that deeply affected me, and that, in the end, helped shape who I am.\\n\\n\u201cSpring came on quickly. The weather turned pleasant, and the sky stayed clear. I was surprised that what had been desert and gloomy now seemed to burst into bloom, covered with the most beautiful flowers and green growth. My senses were delighted and refreshed by a thousand pleasant smells and a thousand sights of beauty.\\n\\n\u201cIt was on one of those days, when my cottagers took their usual breaks from work. The old man played his guitar, and the children listened. That was when I noticed that Felix\u2019s face was filled with sorrow beyond anything I had seen. He sighed again and again. Once, his father stopped playing, and from the way he looked, I guessed he was asking about the reason for his son\u2019s sadness. Felix answered in a cheerful voice. The old man began playing again when someone tapped at the door.\\n\\n\u201cIt was a lady riding on horseback, with a countryman guiding her. The lady wore a dark outfit and a thick black veil. Agatha asked a question, but the stranger only answered by speaking, in a gentle, sweet voice, the name \u2018Felix.\u2019 Her voice was musical, but it did not sound like either of my friends. When Felix heard that name, he hurried to the lady. When she saw him, she lifted her veil, and I saw a face of angelic beauty and expression. Her hair was a shining raven black, and it was braided in a special way. Her eyes were dark, yet kind, though full of life. Her features were well proportioned, and her skin was wonderfully fair, with each cheek touched by a soft pink.\\n\\n\u201cFelix looked completely taken with joy when he saw her. Every trace of sorrow left his face. In an instant, it showed a kind of ecstatic happiness that I could hardly have believed he was capable of. His eyes 