          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7617233a312fbea47632f5da\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cAnd so I\u2019m the proprietor of some knights,\u201d I said as we rode off. \u201cWho would ever have thought I\u2019d live to list assets like that. I don\u2019t know what I\u2019ll do with them\u2014unless I raffle them off. How many are there, Sandy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSeven, if you please, sir\u2014and their squires.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s a good haul. Who are they? Where do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes\u2014where do they live?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, I didn\u2019t understand you. I\u2019ll tell you right away.\u201d Then she said, thinking to herself, softly, turning the words over on her tongue with care: \u201cHang they out\u2014hang they out\u2014where hang\u2014where do they hang out; eh, right so; where do they hang out. Honestly, the phrase has a fine, charming sound, and it\u2019s worded so prettily. I\u2019ll repeat it again and again in my idle time, so I might learn it. Where do they hang out. There\u2014already it trips off my tongue. And since\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t forget the cowboys, Sandy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCowboys?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes; the knights, you know. You were going to tell me about them. A while back, you remember. Figuratively speaking, the game\u2019s called.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGame\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes, yes! Go to bat. I mean, get to work on your statistics, and don\u2019t burn so much kindling getting your fire started. Tell me about the knights.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, and lightly I\u2019ll begin. So they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d\\n\\nYou see, I recognized my mistake at once. I\u2019d set her going; it was my own fault. She\u2019d take thirty days to get down to those facts. And she usually started without a preface and finished without a result. If you interrupted her, she\u2019d either keep going without noticing, or answer with a couple of words and then go back and say the sentence again. So interruptions only did harm; and yet I had to interrupt\u2014and interrupt pretty often, too\u2014to save my life. A person would die if they let her monotony drip on them all day.\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d I said, in my distress. She went right back and began over again:\\n\\n\u201cSo they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhich two?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSir Gawaine and Sir Uwaine. And so they came to an abbey of monks, and they were well lodged. So on the morning they heard their masses in the abbey, and then they rode forth until they came to a great forest; then was Sir Gawaine aware of a valley with a turret, of twelve fair damsels, and two knights armed on great horses, and the damsels went to and fro by a tree.\u201d\"}"
