          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a37c28571eee724d43cddd9c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJust one word more, Rose. My dearest Rose\u2014one more!\u201d Harry cried, throwing himself in front of her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014less fortunate, as the world might phrase it\u2014if some obscure, quiet life had been what fate allotted me\u2014if I had been poor, ill, helpless\u2014would you have turned away from me then? Or does my likely rise to wealth and distinction give rise to this scruple?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo not urge me to answer,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cThe matter is not to be raised, and it never will be. It is unjust\u2014almost cruel\u2014to press it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your reply is what I can scarcely bring myself to hope,\u201d Harry retorted, \u201cit will cast a little gleam of happiness along my lonely road, and show me the way. It is no small thing to do, with only a few brief words, for one who loves you more than anything. Oh, Rose\u2014in the name of my burning, lasting devotion; in the name of all I have endured for you, and all you mean to make me suffer\u2014answer me this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, if my fate had been set differently,\u201d Rose rejoined, \u201cif you had been even a little, but not so far, above me; if I could have been of use and comfort to you in some lowly scene of peace and retirement, and not a stain and hindrance in ambitious, distinguished circles\u2014I should have been spared this trial. I have every reason to be content, very content, now; yet, Harry, I confess I should have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nAs she spoke, Rose\u2019s mind filled with busy recollections of old hopes, cherished in her girlhood; but they came back with tears, as old hopes do when they return, faded and ruined\u2014and still they eased her.\\n\\n\u201cI cannot help this weakness, and it only strengthens my resolve,\u201d said Rose, reaching out her hand. \u201cI must leave you now, indeed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI want one promise,\u201d Harry said. \u201cOnly once more\u2014once, and no more\u2014say within a year, though it may be sooner\u2014I may speak with you again on this subject, for the last time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to press me to change my settled determination,\u201d Rose answered, wearing a melancholy smile; \u201cthat would be pointless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Harry. \u201cTo hear you repeat it\u2014if you will\u2014at last, repeat it. I will lay at your feet whatever rank or fortune I may come to possess; and if you still hold to your present resolution, you will not, by word or deed, try to alter it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it stand so,\u201d Rose replied. \u201cIt is only one pang more, and by then I may be better able to bear it.\u201d\\n\\nShe held out her hand once again.\"}"
