h of them assured her that she could do so safely, she went on in a voice so low that it was often hard for the listener to make out even what she meant. She described, by name and location, the public house where she had been followed that night. From the way she occasionally paused, it seemed as though the gentleman was making quick notes of what she was telling him. Once she had fully explained the layout of the place, the best spot from which to watch it without drawing attention, and the night and hour when Monks was most likely to go there, she seemed to stop and think for a few moments\u2014trying to bring his face and appearance back more clearly.\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019s tall,\u201d the girl said. \u201cA strongly built man, but not stout. He has a kind of furtive walk, and as he walks he keeps looking over his shoulder\u2014first to one side, then to the other.\u201d\"}"
