          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"d00be58b4990a1691613e552\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNow I examined the death\u2019s-head with care. Its outer edges\u2014the edges of the drawing nearest the edge of the vellum\u2014were far clearer than the others. It was obvious that the action of the caloric had been imperfect or uneven. I immediately lit a fire and subjected every part of the parchment to a glowing heat. At first, the only result was that the faint lines in the skull grew stronger; but if I kept at the experiment, then, at the corner of the slip, diagonally opposite the spot where the death\u2019s-head was drawn, there became visible the figure of what I at first took to be a goat. A closer look, though, convinced me it was meant to be a kid.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHa! ha!\u201d said I. \u201cSurely I have no right to laugh at you\u2014an amount of money like a million and a half is too serious a matter for mirth\u2014but you\u2019re not about to set up a third link in your chain. You won\u2019t find any special connection between your pirates and a goat. Pirates, you know, have nothing to do with goats; they belong to the farming interest.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I\u2019ve just said the figure wasn\u2019t that of a goat.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, then\u2014a kid. Pretty much the same thing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPretty much, but not entirely,\u201d said Legrand. \u201cYou may have heard of one Captain Kidd. I immediately took the animal\u2019s figure as a kind of punning or hieroglyphical signature. I say signature, because its position on the vellum suggested that idea. The death\u2019s-head at the corner diagonally opposite had, in the same way, the look of a stamp or seal. But I was deeply frustrated by the absence of everything else\u2014of the body to my imagined instrument, of the text to go with my context.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI suppose you expected to find a letter between the stamp and the signature.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSomething like that. The fact is, I felt irresistibly struck by a presentiment of some vast good fortune about to happen. I can hardly say why. Maybe it was more desire than real belief\u2014but do you know that Jupiter\u2019s silly words, about the bug being solid gold, had a remarkable effect on my imagination? And then there was the whole series of accidents and coincidences\u2014so extraordinary. Do you notice how it was just an accident that these events happened on the only day of the year that is cool enough for fire, and that without the fire, or without the dog\u2019s intervention at the exact moment he appeared, I would never have noticed the death\u2019s-head\u2014and so would never have become the possessor of the treasure?\u201d\"}"
