          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"2fcd08faed2cacecf59eff5e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"When the wedding happened about three weeks later, St. Peter\u2019s was packed with a crowd of smart, well-dressed people. The service was led in a very impressive way by the Dean of Chichester, and everyone agreed they had never seen a prettier couple than the bride and the bridegroom. They were not only handsome, though\u2014they were happy. Lord Arthur never once regretted what he had gone through for Sybil\u2019s sake, and Sybil, in return, gave him the best things a woman can give a man: worship, tenderness, and love. For them, romance was not destroyed by real life. They always felt young.\\n\\nA few years later, after they had two beautiful children, Lady Windermere visited Alton Priory, a lovely old place that the Duke had given as a wedding present to his son. One afternoon, she sat with Lady Arthur under a lime-tree in the garden, watching the little boy and girl play up and down the rose-walk, darting about like flashes of sunlight. Then she suddenly took her hostess\u2019s hand and asked, \u201cAre you happy, Sybil?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDear Lady Windermere, of course I am happy. Aren\u2019t you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t have time to be happy, Sybil. I always like the last person who is introduced to me, but once I get to know people, I usually get tired of them.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t your lions satisfy you, Lady Windermere?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, no! Lions are only good for one season. The moment their manes are cut, they become the dullest creatures you can imagine. And besides, they behave very badly if you are really kind to them. Do you remember that dreadful Mr. Podgers? He was a terrible fraud. Of course, I didn\u2019t mind that at all, and even when he wanted to borrow money I forgave him, but I couldn\u2019t stand him trying to make love to me. He has really made me hate cheiromancy. I\u2019m into telepathy now. It\u2019s much more fun.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou mustn\u2019t say anything against cheiromancy here, Lady Windermere. It\u2019s the only subject that Arthur doesn\u2019t like people to tease him about. I can assure you he takes it very seriously.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou don\u2019t mean to say he actually believes in it, Sybil?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAsk him, Lady Windermere. He\u2019s here\u201d; and Lord Arthur came over to them in the garden, holding a large bunch of yellow roses, with his two children running around him.\\n\\n\u201cLord Arthur?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Lady Windermere.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSo you mean to tell me you believe in cheiromancy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course I do,\u201d the young man said, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cBut why?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBecause it gave me all the happiness of my life,\u201d he said softly, sinking into a wicker chair.\"}"
