d set his cocked hat; and, after exchanging a long and affectionate embrace with his future partner, he faced the cold wind of the night again\u2014only pausing for a few minutes in the male paupers\u2019 ward, to scold them a little, so as to satisfy himself that he could carry out the workhouse-master\u2019s office with the proper sharpness. Convinced of his fitness, Mr. Bumble left the building with a light heart and bright hopes of his coming promotion, which kept his mind busy until he reached the undertaker\u2019s shop.\\n\\nNow, Mr. and Mrs. Sowerberry had gone out to tea and supper, and Noah Claypole was never inclined to take on more physical exertion than was necessary for the convenient performance of eating and drinking; so the shop was not shut, though it was past the usual time for closing. Mr. Bumble tapped his cane on the counter several times, but getting no answer, and seeing a light shining through the glass-window of the little parlour at the back of the shop, he ventured to peep in and see what was going on; and when he saw what was going on, he was by no means a little surprised.\"}"
