          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"1effd715d1cf7079f21301ff\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJoseph!! Joseph!!!\u201d Then he shook his head and tapped it, showing that he felt he was lacking something in Joseph.\\n\\n\u201cBut my dear young friend,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, \u201cyou must be hungry, you must be exhausted. Sit down. Here is a chicken that has come from the Boar; here is a tongue that has come from the Boar; here are one or two little things that have come from the Boar, and I hope you won\u2019t despise them. But do I,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, standing up again the moment after he sat down, \u201csee before me the same one I used to play with in his happy infancy? And may I\u2014may I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nThis \u201cmay I\u201d meant, of course, that he wanted to shake hands. I agreed, and he was very eager, and then he sat down again.\\n\\n\u201cHere is wine,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook. \u201cLet us drink\u2014thanks to Fortune\u2014and may she always choose her favourites with the same good judgment! And yet I cannot,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, standing up again, \u201csee before me One, and drink to One, without saying again\u2014May I\u2014may I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nI told him he could, and he shook hands with me again, then emptied his glass and turned it upside down. I did the same; and if I had turned myself upside down before drinking, the wine could not have gone more straight to my head.\\n\\nMr. Pumblechook helped me to the liver wing, and to the best slice of tongue (none of those unusual No Thoroughfares of Pork now), and he took, in comparison, almost no care of himself at all. \u201cAh! poultry, poultry! You little thought,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, speaking to the fowl in the dish, \u201cwhen you were a young fledgling, what was waiting for you. You little thought you would be refreshment under this humble roof for one who\u2014call it a weakness if you like,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, standing up again, \u201cbut may I? may I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nSoon it was no longer necessary to repeat that he could, so he did it right away. I don\u2019t know how he managed to do it so many times without cutting himself with my knife.\\n\\n\u201cAnd your sister,\u201d he went on after a little steady eating, \u201cwho had the honour of bringing you up by hand! It\u2019s a sad picture to think she can no longer fully understand the honour. May\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI saw he was about to start again, and I stopped him.\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019ll drink her health,\u201d said I.\\n\\n\u201cAh!\u201d cried Mr. Pumblechook, leaning back in his chair, quite limp with admiration, \u201cthat\u2019s the way you know \u2019em, sir!\u201d (I don\u2019t know who Sir was, but it certainly wasn\u2019t me, and there was no third person there); \u201cthat\u2019s the way you know the noble-minded, sir!\u201d\"}"
