rious. When Jupiter tried again to muzzle him, the dog fought back fiercely. Then he leaped into the hole and clawed at the soil in a frenzy. In a few seconds he had uncovered a mass of human bones, enough to form two complete skeletons, mixed together, along with several metal buttons and what looked like the dust of decayed wool. One or two quick strokes of the spade turned up the blade of a large Spanish knife. As we dug farther, three or four loose pieces of gold and silver coin came to light as well.\"}"
