          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"20128eaf215751d31cd6cfd2\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After dinner, the whole gang went out to hunt for turtle eggs on the bar. They wandered around poking sticks into the sand, and when they found a soft spot, they dropped to their knees and dug with their hands. Sometimes they would pull fifty or sixty eggs out of a single hole. The eggs were perfectly round, white things, just a little smaller than an English walnut. That night they had a famous fried-egg feast, and another on Friday morning.\\n\\nAfter breakfast, they ran out onto the bar, shouting and prancing, chasing each other in circles and shedding their clothes as they went until they were naked. Then they kept up the play, running farther and farther up the shoal water of the bar against the stiff current, which kept tripping their legs out from under them now and then and making it even more fun. Every so often they would huddle together and splash water in each other\u2019s faces with their palms, moving closer while keeping their faces turned away to avoid the choking sprays. Finally they would grab and wrestle until the best man ducked his neighbor, and then they all went under in a tangle of white legs and arms, coming up at the same time, blowing, sputtering, laughing, and gasping for breath.\\n\\nWhen they were good and worn out, they would run out and sprawl on the dry, hot sand, then lie there and cover themselves with it. After a while they\u2019d break for the water again and go through the whole performance once more. Eventually it occurred to them that their naked skin looked pretty much like flesh-colored \u201ctights,\u201d so they drew a ring in the sand and put on a circus, with three clowns in it, since none of them would give up that proudest role to his neighbor.\\n\\nNext they got their marbles and played \u201cknucks,\u201d \u201cringtaw,\u201d and \u201ckeeps\u201d until that stopped being fun. Then Joe and Huck went for another swim, but Tom wouldn\u2019t\u2014because when he kicked off his trousers he\u2019d kicked his string of rattlesnake rattles off his ankle, and he couldn\u2019t understand how he\u2019d avoided cramps so long without the protection of that mysterious charm. He didn\u2019t try again until he found it, and by then the other boys were tired and ready to rest. They drifted apart, dropped into the \u201cdumps,\u201d and lay there staring longingly across the wide river at the village, drowsing in the sun. Tom found himself writing \u201cBECKY\u201d in the sand with his big toe; he scratched it out and got angry with himself for being weak. But he wrote it again anyway; he couldn\u2019t help it. He erased it once more, and then pulled himself away from temptation by driving the other boys together and joining them.\"}"
