 studied together, made plans for their future work, and drank in love and joy from each other\u2019s eyes and words, hardly resenting the postponement of their full union. Woodville rose forever in glory, and Elinor became more lovely and wise under the lessons of her accomplished lover.\\n\\nIn two months Elinor would be twenty-one: everything was ready for their union. How can I tell of the catastrophe when so much joy was in the air? But the earth would not be the earth it is, covered as it is with blight and sorrow, if such angelic creatures as these had been allowed to exist for one another. Search the world over, and you will not find the perfect happiness their marriage would have brought them; there must have been a revolution in the order of things as it is established among us miserable earth-dwellers to allow such consummate joy.\"}"
