          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"455ddff5d775d0a6cc810f48\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhy, you don\u2019t mean to say\u2014\u201d my sister began.\\n\\n\u201cYes I do, Mum,\u201d said Pumblechook; \u201cbut wait a bit. Go on, Joseph. Good for you! Go on!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat would respectable company say,\u201d Joe continued, \u201cto twenty pounds?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHandsome would be the word,\u201d my sister replied.\\n\\n\u201cWell, then,\u201d said Joe, \u201cit\u2019s more than twenty pounds.\u201d\\n\\nThat abject hypocrite, Pumblechook, nodded again and said, with a patronizing laugh, \u201cIt\u2019s more than that, Mum. Good again! Follow her up, Joseph!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen to wrap it up,\u201d Joe said, delightedly handing the bag to my sister; \u201cit\u2019s five-and-twenty pounds.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s five-and-twenty pounds, Mum,\u201d echoed the basest of swindlers, Pumblechook, rising to shake hands with her; \u201cand it\u2019s no more than your merits (as I said when my opinion was asked), and I wish you joy of the money!\u201d\\n\\nIf the villain had stopped there, his case would have been bad enough, but he made his guilt even darker by taking me into custody, with a kind of patronage that made all his earlier criminality seem small by comparison.\\n\\n\u201cNow you see, Joseph and wife,\u201d said Pumblechook, taking me by the arm above the elbow, \u201cI\u2019m one of those people who always see things through once they\u2019ve started. This boy must be bound, right away. That\u2019s _my_ way. Bound right away.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGoodness knows, Uncle Pumblechook,\u201d my sister said (grasping the money), \u201cwe\u2019re deeply obliged to you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t mind me, Mum,\u201d returned that diabolical cornchandler. \u201cA pleasure\u2019s a pleasure for everyone. But this boy, you know\u2014we have to have him bound. I said I\u2019d see to it\u2014to tell you the truth.\u201d\\n\\nThe Justices were sitting in the Town Hall nearby, and we went at once to have me bound apprentice to Joe in the Magisterial presence. I say we went, but Pumblechook shoved me forward, just as if I\u2019d picked a pocket or fired a shot that very moment; in fact, that was the general impression in Court\u2014that I\u2019d been caught red-handed. As Pumblechook pushed me through the crowd, I heard people say, \u201cWhat\u2019s he done?\u201d and others, \u201cHe\u2019s a young \u2019un, too, but he looks bad, doesn\u2019t he?\u201d One person, mild and benevolent in appearance, even handed me a tract with a woodcut of a malevolent young man fitted out with a perfect sausage-shop of fetters, and titled TO BE READ IN MY CELL.\\n\\nThe Hall was a strange place, I thought, with higher pews than a church\u2014and people leaning over the pews to watch\u2014and with the mighty Justices (one with a powdered head) leaning back in chairs, arms folded, or taking snuff, or nodding off, or writing, or reading the newspapers. And on the walls there were some shining black portraits, which my untrained eye took for a mix of hardbake and sticking-plaster.\"}"
