me to mind\u2014Rose spent a sleepless, anxious night. The next day, after thinking even more, she reached a desperate decision: she would consult Harry.\\n\\n\u201cIf it hurts him to come back here,\u201d she thought, \u201cit will hurt me too. But maybe he won\u2019t come. He might write, or he might come himself and carefully avoid seeing me, the way he did when he left. I didn\u2019t really think he would. Still, it\u2019s better for both of us.\u201d\\n\\nAt that point, Rose put down her pen and turned away, as if the paper that was supposed to carry her message should not have to see her cry.\"}"
