as plenty to enjoy. Could Anne really be surprised that her father and sister were happy? She might not be surprised, but she still had to sigh that her father felt no shame in his change. He saw nothing to regret in the duties and dignity of a resident landholder, and he found plenty to be proud of in the small, empty things a town offers. She had to sigh, and smile, and wonder too, as Elizabeth threw open the folding doors and walked with excitement from one drawing-room to the next, boasting about their space\u2014especially the fact that this woman, who had once been mistress of Kellynch Hall, could now feel proud of the size of rooms between two walls, perhaps only thirty feet apart.\\n\\nBut this was not all that made them happy. They had Mr Elliot as well.\"}"
