ouch it, they complete a path to the negative brush through the ground, and they drop dead. Don\u2019t you see?\u2014you\u2019re not using energy until it\u2019s actually required; your lightning is waiting there, ready like the charge in a gun, but it costs you nothing until you pull the trigger. Oh, yes\u2014the single ground connection\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cExactly! I don\u2019t know how I missed that. It\u2019s not just cheaper, it\u2019s more effective than the other plan, because if wires break or tangle, nothing bad happens.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, especially if we keep a tell-tale in the cave and disconnect the broken wire. All right, then\u2014the gatlings?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. In the middle of the inner circle, on a broad platform six feet high, I\u2019ve arranged a battery of thirteen gatling guns, with plenty of ammunition.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s it. They\u2019ll cover every approach, and when the Church\u2019s knights arrive, there\u2019ll be music. The cliff\u2019s edge above the cave\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ve got a wire fence there too, and a gatling.\u201d}\"}"
