          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"48ad6fd96c6be6fbb9b66ac4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"If, however, you want one for home use, I can supply you with an excellent article, and I guarantee you\u2019ll be satisfied with the result. May I ask who it\u2019s intended for? If it\u2019s for the police, or for anyone connected with Scotland Yard, I\u2019m afraid I can\u2019t do anything for you. The English detectives are really our best friends, and I\u2019ve always found that by relying on their stupidity, we can do exactly what we like. I can\u2019t spare one of them.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI assure you,\u201d said Lord Arthur, \u201cit has nothing to do with the police at all. In fact, the clock is meant for the Dean of Chichester.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDear me! I had no idea you felt so strongly about religion, Lord Arthur. Few young men do nowadays.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m afraid you\u2019re overrating me, Herr Winckelkopf,\u201d said Lord Arthur, blushing. \u201cThe fact is, I really know nothing about theology.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen it\u2019s purely a private matter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPurely private.\u201d\\n\\nHerr Winckelkopf shrugged, and left the room. A few minutes later he returned with a round cake of dynamite about the size of a penny, and a pretty little French clock, topped with an ormolu figure of Liberty trampling on the hydra of Despotism.\\n\\nLord Arthur\u2019s face brightened when he saw it. \u201cThat\u2019s exactly what I want,\u201d he cried. \u201cAnd now tell me how it goes off.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh! there\u2019s my secret,\u201d answered Herr Winckelkopf, regarding his invention with a look of pride that was entirely justified. \u201cLet me know when you want it to explode, and I\u2019ll set the machine for the moment.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, today is Tuesday, and if you could send it off right away\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s impossible; I have a great deal of important work to do for some friends of mine in Moscow. Still, I might send it off tomorrow.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, it will be quite time enough!\u201d Lord Arthur said politely. \u201cIf it\u2019s delivered tomorrow night or Thursday morning. For the moment of the explosion\u2014say Friday at noon exactly. The Dean is always at home at that hour.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFriday, at noon,\u201d Herr Winckelkopf repeated, and he made a note of it in a large ledger lying on a bureau near the fireplace.\\n\\n\u201cAnd now,\u201d said Lord Arthur, rising from his seat, \u201cpray let me know how much I owe you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s such a small matter, Lord Arthur, that I don\u2019t care to make any charge. The dynamite comes to seven and sixpence, the clock will be three pounds ten, and the carriage about five shillings. I\u2019m only too pleased to oblige any friend of Count Rouvaloff\u2019s.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut what about your trouble, Herr Winckelkopf?\u201d\"}"
