t flitting before me forever. The northern breeze, when it refreshed me, seemed sweeter and more gentle, as though it carried some part of your spirit along with it. I often imagined that I would return at once and take you with me to some fertile island, where we might live in peace forever. But when I came back, my ardent hopes were crushed by so many fears; my impatience became, in the highest degree, painful. I dared not think that the sun might shine and the moon rise over anything but your living form, not your grave. Yet no\u2014it is not so. I have my Mathilda, my consolation, and my hope.\u201d\u2014\"}"
