ble or fear of being interrupted.\\n\\nJust as breakfast was finished, there was a knock at the door. Huck sprang up for a hiding place, because he had no desire to be connected in any way to what had happened. The Welshman let in several ladies and gentlemen, including the Widow Douglas, and noticed that groups of citizens were climbing up the hill\u2014to stare at the stile. So the news had spread. The Welshman had to tell the story of the night to the visitors. The widow\u2019s gratitude for her rescue was plain to see.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t say a word about it, madam. There\u2019s another you\u2019re more indebted to than you are to me and my boys, maybe\u2014but he won\u2019t let me tell his name. We wouldn\u2019t have been there but for him.\u201d\"}"
