iddy asked, with a timid sort of air.\\n\\n\u201cGetting at?\u201d I said, in a self-satisfied tone. \u201cNow, don\u2019t repeat me. You didn\u2019t used to, Biddy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDidn\u2019t!\u201d said Biddy. \u201cOh, Mr. Pip! Didn\u2019t!\u201d\\n\\nWell! I thought I might as well surrender that point too. After one more silent turn in the garden, I took up my main argument again.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d said I, \u201cI made a remark about my coming down here often to see Joe, and you met it with a marked silence. Do me the kindness, Biddy, and tell me why.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAre you quite sure, then, that you WILL come to see him often?\u201d asked Biddy, stopping on the narrow path and looking at me beneath the stars with a clear, straightforward gaze.\"}"
