r would keep quiet. Duchess, I\u2019m sure you\u2019re tired?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot at all, dear Gladys,\u201d the Duchess answered as she waddled toward the door. \u201cI have enjoyed myself immensely, and the cheiropodist, I mean the cheiromantist, is most interesting. Flora, where can my tortoise-shell fan be? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, so much. And my lace shawl, Flora? Oh, thank you, Sir Thomas, how kind. And at last she managed to get downstairs without dropping her scent-bottle more than twice.\u201d\\n\\nAll this time Lord Arthur Savile had stayed standing by the fireplace, feeling the same dread and the same sickening sense that something evil was coming. He gave his sister a sad smile as she passed him on Lord Plymdale\u2019s arm, looking lovely in her pink brocade and pearls. He barely even heard Lady Windermere when she told him to follow her. He thought of Sybil Merton, and the idea that anything could come between them made his eyes fill with tears.\"}"
