          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"895c642bdbe78c9dc932fe53\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At the sight of it, Jupiter\u2019s joy could barely be held back, but his master\u2019s face showed extreme disappointment. Still, he urged us to keep working, and the words were barely out of his mouth when I tripped and fell forward, catching my boot toe on a large iron ring half buried in the loose earth.\\n\\nWe now worked with real effort, and I never went ten minutes without feeling intense excitement. In that time we had managed to uncover an oblong wooden chest. Its perfect preservation and remarkable hardness showed that it had clearly been subjected to some mineralizing process\u2014perhaps that of the bi-chloride of mercury. The box was three and a half feet long, three feet wide, and two and a half feet deep. It was held firmly in place by bands of wrought iron, riveted on, forming a kind of open trelliswork over the whole. On each side of the chest, near the top, were three iron rings\u2014six in all\u2014by which six people could get a solid grip. All our combined efforts only managed to shift the coffer slightly in its bed. We immediately saw that removing so heavy a thing was impossible. Luckily, the only fastenings on the lid were two sliding bolts. We pulled them back, trembling and panting with anxious urgency. In an instant, a treasure of incalculable value lay gleaming before us. As the lantern rays fell into the pit, a flash of light shot upward\u2014glow and glare\u2014from a confused heap of gold and jewels, so dazzling it made our eyes ache.\\n\\nI won\u2019t pretend to describe what I felt as I stared. Amazement, of course, dominated everything. Legrand looked worn out by excitement and said very little. For several minutes, Jupiter\u2019s face wore a deadly pallor\u2014about as deadly as any negro\u2019s features can take on. He seemed stunned, struck as if by lightning. Then he dropped to his knees in the pit and, burying his bare arms up to the elbows in gold, left them there as though he were enjoying the luxury of a bath. At last, with a deep sigh, he exclaimed, as if speaking to himself:\\n\\n\u201cAn dis all cum ob de goole-bug! de putty goole-bug! de poor little goole-bug, what I boosed in dat sabage kind ob style! Aint you shamed ob yourself, nigger?\u2014answer me dat!\u201d\\n\\nEventually, it became necessary for me to rouse both master and valet to the practical need of removing the treasure. It was getting late, and we had to push ourselves so we could get everything secured before daylight. It was hard to say what should be done, and a great deal of time was spent deliberating, because everyone\u2019s thoughts were so tangled.\"}"
