d Mr. Lorry.\\n\\n\u201cI dare say not,\u201d rejoined Stryver, nodding in a smoothing, final fashion; \u201cnever mind, never mind.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut it does matter,\u201d Mr. Lorry pressed.\\n\\n\u201cNo, it doesn\u2019t; I assure you it doesn\u2019t. Having supposed there was sense where there is no sense, and a proper ambition where there is no proper ambition, I\u2019m well out of my mistake, and no harm is done. Young women have fallen into like follies often enough before, and have repented of them in poverty and obscurity often enough before. In one light, I\u2019m sorry the matter is dropped, because it would have been a bad thing for me in a worldly point of view; in another, I\u2019m glad it\u2019s dropped, because it would have been a bad thing for me in a worldly point of view\u2014though it hardly needs saying that I could have gained nothing by it.\u201d}\"}"
