          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"74e55a2d51be67aa1347b7da\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After supper, the whole crew spilled out to the bar to look for turtle eggs. They wandered around with sticks, prodding the sand, and whenever they struck a yielding spot they dropped to their knees and dug with their bare hands. At times they hauled fifty or sixty eggs from a single hole. The eggs were perfectly round, white as anything, just a bit smaller than an English walnut. That night they had a celebrated fried-egg feast, and again on Friday morning.\\n\\nAfter breakfast they went out yelling and prancing across the bar, circling each other and shedding their clothes as they went, until they were completely naked; then the play carried them farther up the shoal water of the bar, right against the stiff current, which kept knocking their legs out from under them now and then and made it all the more hilarious. Now and then they would huddle together and splash water in each other\u2019s faces with their palms, edging closer with their faces turned aside to dodge the choking sprays, until it came to grabbing and wrestling\u2014until the best man ducked his neighbor\u2014and then they all went under in a tangle of white legs and arms. When they came up, they were blowing, sputtering, laughing, and gasping for breath all at once.\\n\\nOnce they were properly worn out, they ran back and sprawled on the dry, hot sand, then lay there and covered themselves with it. After a while they broke for the water again and went through the same business over. At last it struck them that their bare skin looked remarkably like flesh-colored \u201ctights,\u201d so they drew a ring in the sand and put on a circus, with three clowns in it\u2014since none of them would give up that proud spot to his neighbor.\\n\\nThen they took up their marbles and played \u201cknucks,\u201d \u201cringtaw,\u201d and \u201ckeeps\u201d until that game lost its charm. Joe and Huck went for another swim, but Tom wouldn\u2019t, because when he kicked off his trousers he\u2019d also kicked loose his string of rattlesnake rattles off his ankle; he kept wondering how he\u2019d managed to avoid cramps so long without the protection of that mysterious charm. He didn\u2019t try again until he\u2019d found the rattles, and by then the other boys were worn out and ready to rest. They drifted off one by one, dropped into the \u201cdumps,\u201d and stared longingly across the broad river toward the village, lying drowsy in the sun. Tom caught himself writing \u201cBECKY\u201d in the sand with his big toe; he scratched it out and felt annoyed at his own weakness. Still, he wrote it again\u2014he couldn\u2019t help it. He erased it once more, and then tried to break the temptation by herding the other boys together and joining them.\"}"
