d it, and with sober resolve he laid out the course of action he would follow. He remembered that he had promised Perdita to be present this very evening\u2014the 19th of October, the anniversary of his election as Protector\u2014at a festival held in his honor. This festival should be a good sign for the happiness of future years. First, he would go by and see Evadne; he would not stay long. But he owed her some explanation, some compensation for his long absence without word. Then, to Perdita, to the forgotten world, to the duties of society, to the splendor of rank, to the enjoyment of power.\\n\\nAfter the scene described in the preceding pages, Perdita had been considering a complete change in Raymond\u2019s manners and behavior. She expected more freedom in their communication and a return to the affectionate habits that had made up the joy of her life.\"}"
