here\u2019s something strange about this. She is going to marry the nephew of Monsieur the Marquis, for whom Gaspard was raised to such a great height, in other words, the present Marquis. But in England he lives without being known as a marquis. There he is simply Mr. Charles Darnay. D\u2019Aulnais is the name of his mother\u2019s family.\u201d\\n\\nMadame Defarge kept knitting, but the news clearly affected her husband. No matter what he did behind the little counter\u2014whether he tried to strike a light or light his pipe\u2014he was still troubled, and his hand was not steady. The spy would not have been a spy if he hadn\u2019t noticed it, and if he hadn\u2019t kept it in his mind.\\n\\nAfter making at least this one point, whatever it might be worth, and with no customers coming in to help Defarge, Mr. Barsad paid for what he had drunk and left. Before he went, he said, in a polite way, that he looked forward to seeing Monsieur and Madame Defarge again.\"}"
