honor of her hand, but it was no use. Elizabeth was determined, and Sir William did not manage to change her mind with his attempts to persuade her.\\n\\n\u201cYou dance so well, Miss Eliza, that it would be cruel to deny me the happiness of seeing you. And although this gentleman dislikes the amusement in general, I\u2019m sure he won\u2019t mind doing us the favor for half an hour.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMr. Darcy is nothing but politeness,\u201d said Elizabeth, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cHe is, indeed. But with such an invitation, my dear Miss Eliza, we can\u2019t really blame him for being willing. Who could refuse a partner like that?\u201d\\n\\nElizabeth looked slyly at him and turned away. Her refusal did not upset the gentleman, and he was pleased to think of her, when Miss Bingley approached and spoke to him\u2014\"}"
