          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"cbfaad013b3f5044ab41fa8f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cBut I may ask you two questions, may I?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou may ask,\u201d said Monks, with some show of surprise; \u201cbut whether I answer or not is another question.\u201d\\n\\n\u201c\u2014Which makes three,\u201d observed Mr. Bumble, trying to sound facetious.\\n\\n\u201cIs that what you expected to get from me?\u201d demanded the matron.\\n\\n\u201cIt is,\u201d replied Monks. \u201cThe other question?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you propose to do with it? Can it be used against me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNever,\u201d rejoined Monks; \u201cnor against me either. Listen\u2014don\u2019t take a step forward, or your life won\u2019t be worth a bulrush.\u201d\\n\\nWith that, he suddenly shoved the table aside, and yanked an iron ring set into the boarding. He threw back a large trapdoor that opened right at Mr. Bumble\u2019s feet, forcing that gentleman to stumble back several paces in a rush of panic.\\n\\n\u201cLook down,\u201d said Monks, lowering the lantern into the dark opening. \u201cDon\u2019t be afraid of me. I could have let you down quietly enough when you were sitting over it, if that had been my plan.\u201d\\n\\nEncouraged, the matron stepped closer to the edge; and even Mr. Bumble himself, driven by curiosity, did the same. The muddy water, swollen by the heavy rain, was surging rapidly below; and every other sound was swallowed by the noise of it splashing and churning against the green, slimy piles. There had once been a water-mill beneath. The tide, foaming and snapping around the few rotten stakes and fragments of machinery still left there, seemed to dart onward with fresh force once it was freed from obstacles that had tried in vain to stop its headlong rush.\\n\\n\u201cIf you threw a man\u2019s body down there, where would it be tomorrow morning?\u201d said Monks, swinging the lantern back and forth in the dark well.\\n\\n\u201cTwelve miles down the river\u2014and