after assuring herself with some anxiety that there had been no fall\u2014that Anne had not, at any time lately, slipped down and struck her head\u2014was perfectly convinced there had been no fall; and she could part with her readily, depending on finding her better by night.\\n\\nWith anxious care not to omit any possible precaution, Anne struggled and said\u2014\\n\\n\u201cI am afraid, ma\u2019am, that it is not quite understood. Pray, be so good as to tell the other gentlemen that we hope to see your whole party this evening. I fear there has been some mistake; and I wish you particularly to assure Captain Harville and Captain Wentworth that we hope to see them both.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh! my dear, it is quite understood; I give you my word.\u201d\"}"
