201d\\n\\nThe old lady spun around and yanked her skirts out of danger. The boy bolted at once, scrambled up the high board fence, and disappeared over it.\\n\\nHis aunt Polly stood there, surprised for a moment, and then broke into a gentle laugh.\\n\\n\u201cHang the boy\u2014can\u2019t I never learn anything? Hasn\u2019t he played me tricks enough that I should be watching for him by now? But old fools are the biggest fools there is. You can\u2019t teach an old dog new tricks, as the saying goes. But goodness, he never plays them the same way two days in a row, and how is a person supposed to know what\u2019s coming? He seems to know just how long he can torment me before I get mad, and he knows if he can manage to distract me for a minute or make me laugh, then it\u2019s all gone again and I can\u2019t hit him a lick.\u201d\"}"
