          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"82ce69142aa470703115783a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, everybody does it that way, Huck.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTom, it don\u2019t make no difference. I ain\u2019t everybody, and I can\u2019t _stand_ it. It\u2019s awful being tied up so. And food comes too easy\u2014I don\u2019t take any interest in eating that way. I got to ask to go fishing; I got to ask to go swimming\u2014damn if I haven\u2019t got to ask to do everything. And I\u2019d have to talk so nice it wasn\u2019t no comfort. I\u2019d have to go up in the attic and tear out awhile every day just to get a taste in my mouth, or I\u2019d a died, Tom. The widow wouldn\u2019t let me smoke; she wouldn\u2019t let me yell, she wouldn\u2019t let me gape, nor stretch, nor scratch in front of people\u2014\u201d [Then with a spasm of special irritation and injury]\u2014\u201cAnd dad would fetch it, she prayed all the time! I never see such a woman! I _had_ to shove, Tom\u2014I just had to. And besides, that school\u2019s going to open, and I\u2019d have had to go to it\u2014well, I wouldn\u2019t stand _that_, Tom. Look here, Tom, being rich ain\u2019t what it\u2019s cracked up to be. It\u2019s just worry and worry, and sweat and sweat, and wishing you was dead all the time. Now these clothes suit me, and this barrel suits me, and I ain\u2019t ever going to shake \u2019em off again. Tom, I wouldn\u2019t ever got into all this trouble if it hadn\u2019t been for that money; now you just take my share of it along with yours, and give me a ten-cent piece sometimes\u2014not many times, because I don\u2019t give a damn for a thing unless it\u2019s tolerably hard to get\u2014and you go and talk the widow out of it for me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, Huck, you know I can\u2019t do that. It ain\u2019t fair; and besides, if you try this thing just a little longer, you\u2019ll come to like it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLike it! Yes\u2014the way I\u2019d like a hot stove if I sat on it long enough. No, Tom, I won\u2019t be rich, and I won\u2019t live in them cursed stuffy houses. I like the woods, and the river, and hogsheads, and I\u2019ll stick with \u2019em, too. Blame it all! just as we\u2019d got guns, and a cave, and everything all set up for robbing\u2014here this damn foolishness has got to come along and spoil it all!\u201d\\n\\nTom saw his chance\u2014\\n\\n\u201cLook here, Huck, being rich isn\u2019t going to stop me from turning robber.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo! Oh, good grief; are you in real dead-wood earnest, Tom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJust as dead earnest as I\u2019m sitting here. But Huck, we can\u2019t let you into the gang if you ain\u2019t respectable, you know.\u201d\\n\\nHuck\u2019s joy was cut short.\\n\\n\u201cCan\u2019t let me in, Tom?\u201d\"}"
