moments, not a trace of the bloodstain could be seen.\\n\\n\u201cI knew Pinkerton would do it,\u201d he said triumphantly, looking around at his admiring family. But no sooner had he spoken than a terrible flash of lightning lit up the gloomy room, followed by a fearful crash of thunder that made them all jump to their feet, and Mrs. Umney fainted.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a monstrous climate!\u201d the American Minister said calmly as he lit a long cheroot. \u201cI guess the old country is so overpopulated that they don\u2019t have decent weather for everyone. I\u2019ve always believed emigration is the only solution for England.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Hiram,\u201d Mrs. Otis cried, \u201cwhat can we do with a woman who faints?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCharge it to her like breakages,\u201d the Minister answered. \u201cShe won\u2019t faint after that.\u201d And within moments, Mrs. Umney certainly came around.\"}"
