ould she possibly mean!\u201d He repeated her words with such confidence, and with such showy pretending surprise, that she could not help replying quickly,\\n\\n\u201cMr. Elton, this is the most extraordinary behavior! I can explain it only in one way: you are not yourself, or you could not speak to me, or about Harriet, in such a way. Command yourself enough to say no more, and I will try to forget it.\u201d\\n\\nBut Mr. Elton had drunk enough wine to lift his spirits, not enough to confuse his mind. He understood exactly what he meant. After warmly protesting against her suspicion, saying it was the most harmful thing she could believe, and after touching lightly on his respect for Miss Smith as her friend\u2014though admitting he was surprised that Miss Smith was even mentioned\u2014he returned at once to his own feelings. He was very urgent for a favorable answer.\"}"
