          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"932cca793559e4092bd45760\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJust a tick.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere\u2019d you get him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOut in the woods.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019ll you take for him?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know. I don\u2019t want to sell him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll right. Anyway, it\u2019s a pretty small tick.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, anyone can catch a tick that doesn\u2019t belong to them. I\u2019m happy with it. It\u2019s good enough for me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSure, there are plenty of ticks. I could have a thousand if I wanted.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, why don\u2019t you? You know you can\u2019t. This is an early tick, I think. It\u2019s the first one I\u2019ve seen this year.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSay, Huck\u2014I\u2019ll trade you my tooth for him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLet me see it.\u201d\\n\\nTom pulled out some paper and carefully unrolled it. Huckleberry looked at it with longing. The temptation was very strong. Finally he said:\\n\\n\u201cIs it real?\u201d\\n\\nTom lifted his lip and showed the empty spot.\\n\\n\u201cWell, all right,\u201d Huckleberry said. \u201cIt\u2019s a trade.\u201d\\n\\nTom put the tick into the percussion-cap box that had recently been the pinchbug\u2019s prison, and the boys went their separate ways, each feeling richer than before.\\n\\nWhen Tom got to the little, isolated frame schoolhouse, he walked in quickly, acting like he\u2019d come with nothing but honest business. He hung his hat on a peg and sat down at once, eager and ready to work. The teacher sat up high in his big splint-bottom chair, dozing off, lulled by the sleepy hum of lessons. The interruption woke him.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer!\u201d\\n\\nTom knew that when his full name was said, it meant trouble.\\n\\n\u201cYes, sir!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCome up here. Now, sir, why are you late again, like always?\u201d\\n\\nTom was about to make up a lie, but then he saw two long tails of yellow hair hanging down a back he recognized with the quick feeling of love; and that was the only empty spot on the girls\u2019 side of the schoolhouse. He immediately said:\\n\\n\u201cI stopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn!\u201d\\n\\nThe teacher\u2019s pulse seemed to stop. He stared, helpless. The quiet buzz of study died away. The students wondered if the boy had lost his mind. The teacher said:\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2014you did what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStopped to talk with Huckleberry Finn.\u201d\\n\\nThere was no doubt about what he\u2019d said.\\n\\n\u201cThomas Sawyer, this is the most unbelievable confession I\u2019ve ever heard. No ordinary punishment will cover this. Take off your jacket.\u201d\\n\\nThe teacher\u2019s arm worked until it was tired, and the switches were clearly running low. Then he ordered:\\n\\n\u201cNow, sir, go sit with the girls! And let this be a warning to you.\u201d\\n\\nThe little ripple of laughter around the room made the boy seem embarrassed, but it was really because he was overwhelmed by his worshipful awe of his secret idol and the happy thrill of getting such a good outcome.\"}"
