          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"da65b06ac6858d31983361d3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhat\u2019s the matter?\u201d Oliver demanded.\\n\\n\u201cHush!\u201d the Dodger replied. \u201cDo you see that old fellow at the book-stall?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe old gentleman across the way?\u201d Oliver said. \u201cYes, I see him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHe\u2019ll do,\u201d said the Dodger.\\n\\n\u201cA fine choice,\u201d Master Charley Bates observed.\\n\\nOliver looked from one to the other, utterly astonished, but he wasn\u2019t allowed to ask questions. The two boys moved stealthily across the road and slipped close behind the old gentleman toward whom his attention had been directed. Oliver followed a few paces behind them; not knowing whether to step forward or back, he stood watching in silent amazement.\\n\\nThe old gentleman was a very respectable-looking man, with a powdered head and gold spectacles. He wore a bottle-green coat with a black velvet collar, white trousers, and carried a smart bamboo cane under his arm. He had picked up a book from the stall and stood there reading as intensely as if he were in his own study, in his elbow-chair. It was very possible he imagined himself there, too; his deep focus made it clear he wasn\u2019t seeing the book-stall, the street, the boys, or anything at all\u2014except the book itself. He read straight through, turning the page when he reached the bottom, starting at the top line of the next, and continuing steadily on with the greatest interest and eagerness.\\n\\nWhat horror and alarm seized Oliver as he stood a few paces away, watching with his eyes wide open as they could possibly be\u2014seeing the Dodger plunge his hand into the old gentleman\u2019s pocket and pull out a handkerchief! Seeing him pass it to Charley Bates. And then, finally, watching them both run away around the corner at full speed!\\n\\nIn an instant, the whole mystery of the handkerchiefs, the watches, the jewels, and the Jew came rushing into the boy\