          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"096a29dac2eaba4b08647a7b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"After dinner, the whole gang went out on the bar to hunt for turtle eggs. They poked sticks into the sand, and when they found a soft spot, they dropped to their knees and dug with their hands. Sometimes they pulled fifty or sixty eggs from one hole. The eggs were perfectly round and white, a little smaller than an English walnut. That night they had a big fried-egg feast, and another one on Friday morning.\\n\\nAfter breakfast, they ran out onto the bar shouting and prancing, chasing each other in circles and throwing off their clothes as they went. Soon they were naked, and they kept playing, running farther up the shoal water of the bar, right against the strong current. The current would trip their legs now and then, which made it even funnier. Every so often they would huddle together and splash water in each other\u2019s faces with their palms, moving closer while keeping their faces turned away to avoid the harsh sprays. Then they would grab and wrestle until the best man ducked his neighbor, and after that they all went under in a tangle of white legs and arms. When they came up, they were blowing, sputtering, laughing, and gasping for breath all at once.\\n\\nWhen they were worn out, they ran back out onto the dry, hot sand and sprawled there. They covered themselves with sand, then later broke for the water again and did the whole thing over. At last they realized their naked skin looked a lot like flesh-colored \u201ctights.\u201d So they drew a ring in the sand and put on a circus, with three clowns in it, because none of them would give up that proud role to anyone else.\\n\\nAfter that, they got their marbles and played \u201cknucks,\u201d \u201cringtaw,\u201d and \u201ckeeps\u201d until it stopped being fun. Then Joe and Huck went for another swim, but Tom wouldn\u2019t, because when he kicked off his trousers he had also kicked his string of rattlesnake rattles off h