          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6358e53c833fa7694e9e995f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cI agree. It\u2019s the best thing. Just hold hands and swear that we\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no, not like that. This is good enough for small, ordinary things, especially with girls, because they always turn on you and then they run their mouths if they get mad. But for something big like this, there ought to be writing. And blood.\u201d\\n\\nTom\u2019s whole body seemed to approve of the idea. It felt deep, dark, and awful. The hour, the situation, and the place all fit it. He picked up a clean pine shingle lying in the moonlight, took a small piece of \u201cred keel\u201d from his pocket, held it up to the moon, and carefully wrote the words. He pressed his tongue between his teeth to make each slow stroke, then eased up on the upstrokes.\\n\\n\u201cHuck Finn and Tom Sawyer swears they will keep mum about This and They wish They may Drop down dead in Their Tracks if They ever Tell and Rot.\u201d\\n\\nHuckleberry was full of admiration for Tom\u2019s skill in writing and for how grand the words sounded. He immediately took a pin from his lapel and started to prick his own flesh, but Tom stopped him.\\n\\n\u201cWait! Don\u2019t do that. A pin is brass. It might have verdigris on it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s verdigris?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s poison. That\u2019s what it is. If you swallow it once, you\u2019ll see.\u201d\\n\\nSo Tom pulled the thread out from one of his needles. Then each boy pricked the ball of his thumb and squeezed out a drop of blood. After many squeezes, Tom finally managed to sign his initials, using the ball of his little finger as a pen. Then he showed Huckleberry how to make an H and an F, and the oath was finished. They buried the shingle near the wall, with gloomy ceremonies and strange chants. The fetters that were supposed to bind their tongues were treated as locked, and the key was thrown away.\\n\\nA figure crept through a gap at the other end of the ruined building, but they didn\u2019t notice it.\\n\\n\u201cTom,\u201d Huckleberry whispered, \u201cdoes this stop us from ever telling\u2014always?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course it does. It doesn\u2019t matter what happens. We have to keep quiet. We\u2019d drop down dead\u2014don\u2019t you know that?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, I guess that\u2019s true.\u201d\\n\\nThey kept whispering for a little while. Then, just outside\u2014within ten feet of them\u2014a dog let out a long, mournful howl. The boys grabbed each other suddenly, shaking with terror.\\n\\n\u201cWhich one of us does he mean?\u201d Huckleberry gasped.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t know\u2014look through the crack. Quick!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, you, Tom!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t\u2014I can\u2019t do it, Huck!\u201d\"}"
