          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"718be21b9a2ec40188273976\",\"rewritten_text\":\"His face, badly sunburned, was more than half hidden by whiskers and a _mustache_. He had with him a huge oak cudgel, but otherwise seemed to be unarmed. He bowed awkwardly and greeted us with \u201cgood evening,\u201d in French accents that, though a bit Neufch\u00e2tel-like, were still clear enough to suggest a Parisian origin.\\n\\n\u201cSit down, my friend,\u201d said Dupin. \u201cI suppose you\u2019ve come about the Ourang-Outang. Honestly, I almost envy you for having him\u2014a remarkably fine animal, and no doubt very valuable. How old do you think he is?\u201d\\n\\nThe sailor drew a long breath, with the look of a man relieved of some unbearable burden, and then answered in a confident tone:\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t really say\u2014but he can\u2019t be more than four or five years old. Do you have him here?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh no. We didn\u2019t have any way to keep him here. He\u2019s at a livery stable in the Rue Dubourg, just around the corner. You can get him in the morning. Of course you\u2019re prepared to identify the property?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course I am, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll be sorry to part with him,\u201d said Dupin.\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t mean you should go to all this trouble for nothing, sir,\u201d the man replied. \u201cYou couldn\u2019t expect that. I\u2019m very willing to pay a reward for finding the animal\u2014that is, anything reasonable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d my friend answered, \u201cthat\u2019s all very fair, of course. Let me think! What should I have? Oh! I\u2019ll tell you. My reward will be this: you will give me all the information you can about these murders in the Rue Morgue.\u201d\\n\\nDupin spoke the last words in a very low voice, and very quietly. Just as quietly, he walked to the door, locked it, and put the key in his pocket. Then he drew a pistol from his bosom and set it on the table without the slightest flurry.\\n\\nThe sailor\u2019s face flushed, as if he were struggling for breath. He sprang to his feet and grabbed his cudgel, but the next moment he sank back into his seat, trembling violently, with the expression of death itself. He didn\u2019t say a word. I pitied him from the bottom of my heart.\\n\\n\u201cMy friend,\u201d said Dupin, in a kind tone, \u201cyou\u2019re frightening yourself unnecessarily\u2014you really are. We mean you no harm at all. I give you my word as an honorable gentleman, and as a Frenchman, that we intend you no injury. I know perfectly well that you\u2019re innocent of the atrocities in the Rue Morgue. Still, it won\u2019t do to deny that you\u2019re in some measure implicated in them.\u201d\"}"
