          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c8741193932fd184e4123307\",\"rewritten_text\":\"At the stairs where we had taken him abroad, and ever since, I had watched warily for any sign that we were suspected. I saw none. We certainly weren\u2019t, and at that time we were certainly not being attended or followed by any boat. If we had been met by any boat, I would have run to shore and told it to go on, or made its purpose clear. But we kept our course without any sign of being bothered.\\n\\nHe had his boat-cloak on, and, as I\u2019ve said, he looked like a natural part of the scene. It was remarkable\u2014though perhaps the miserable life he\u2019d led explains it\u2014that he was the least anxious of all of us. He wasn\u2019t indifferent; he told me he hoped to live long enough to see his gentleman become one of the best gentlemen in a foreign country. He wasn\u2019t disposed to be passive or resigned, as I understood it; but he had no intention of meeting danger halfway. When danger came for him, he faced it, but it had to arrive before he would trouble himself.\\n\\n\u201cIf you knew, dear boy,\u201d he said to me, \u201cwhat it is to sit here alonger my dear boy and have my smoke, arter having been day by day betwixt four walls, you\u2019d envy me. But you don\u2019t know what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI think I know the delights of freedom,\u201d I answered.\\n\\n\u201cAh,\u201d he said, shaking his head gravely. \u201cBut you don\u2019t know it equal to me. You must have been under lock and key, dear boy, to know it equal to me\u2014but I ain\u2019t a-going to be low.\u201d\\n\\nIt struck me as inconsistent that, for any plan to work, he should have risked his freedom\u2014and even his life. But I thought maybe freedom without danger was too far removed from the habits of his whole existence for it to feel to him the way it would to another man. I wasn\u2019t far off, since he said, after smoking a little\u2014\\n\\n\u201cYou see, dear boy, when I was over yonder, t\u2019other side the world, I was always a looking to this side; and it come flat to be there, for all I was a growing rich. Everybody knowed Magwitch, and Magwitch could come, and Magwitch could go, and nobody\u2019s head would be troubled about him. They ain\u2019t so easy concerning me here, dear boy\u2014wouldn\u2019t be, leastwise, if they knowed where I was.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf all goes well,\u201d I said, \u201cyou\u2019ll be perfectly free and safe again within a few hours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell,\u201d he replied, drawing a long breath, \u201cI hope so.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd think so?\u201d\"}"
