ty to know everyone, and I remember seeing you one evening at Lady Windermere\u2019s. I hope her ladyship is quite well. Would you mind sitting with me while I finish my breakfast? There\u2019s an excellent p\u00e2t\u00e9, and my friends are kind enough to say that my Rhine wine is better than any they get at the German Embassy.\u201d Before Lord Arthur had fully recovered from the shock of being recognized, he found himself seated in the back room, sipping the most delicious Marcobr\u00fcnner from a pale yellow hock-glass marked with the Imperial monogram, and chatting in the friendliest possible way with the famous conspirator.\\n\\n\u201cExplosive clocks,\u201d said Herr Winckelkopf, \u201caren\u2019t very good for foreign export. Even if they manage to get through the Custom House, the train service is so irregular that they usually go off before they\u2019ve reached their proper destination.\u201d\"}"
