          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8c866a99045304b2bcbd81f6\",\"rewritten_text\":\"This was Mrs. Umney, the housekeeper, whom Mrs. Otis had agreed to keep on in her old job, at Lady Canterville\u2019s firm request. When they stepped out, Mrs. Umney bowed low to each of them and said, in a quaint, old-fashioned way, \u201cI bid you welcome to Canterville Chase.\u201d After her, they walked through the Tudor hall and into the library, a long, low room with black oak paneling. At the far end was a large stained-glass window. Tea was already laid out for them. After they took off their wraps, they sat down and began to look around, while Mrs. Umney served them.\\n\\nSuddenly Mrs. Otis noticed a dull red stain on the floor near the fireplace. Without thinking about what it meant, she said to Mrs. Umney, \u201cI\u2019m afraid something has been spilled there.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, madam,\u201d the old housekeeper answered in a low voice. \u201cBlood has been spilled on that spot.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow awful,\u201d Mrs. Otis said. \u201cI don\u2019t want blood stains in a sitting-room. It has to be cleaned right away.\u201d\\n\\nThe old woman smiled and replied in the same quiet, mysterious tone, \u201cIt is the blood of Lady Eleanore de Canterville, who was murdered right there by her own husband, Sir Simon de Canterville, in 1575. Sir Simon lived for nine years after her death, and then disappeared under very strange circumstances. His body was never found, but his guilty spirit still haunts the Chase. The stain has been admired by tourists and others, and it cannot be removed.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s nonsense,\u201d Washington Otis snapped. \u201cPinkerton\u2019s Champion Stain Remover and Paragon Detergent will take care of it in no time.\u201d Before the frightened housekeeper could stop him, he dropped to his knees and quickly scrubbed the floor with a small stick that looked like a black cosmetic. In a few moments, the blood stain was gone.\\n\\n\u201cI knew Pinkerton would do it,\u201d he said triumphantly, looking around at his impressed family. But the moment he finished speaking, a terrible flash of lightning lit up the dark room. A fearful crash of thunder followed, and they all jumped up. Mrs. Umney fainted.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a dreadful climate,\u201d the American Minister said calmly as he lit a long cheroot. \u201cI guess the old country is so crowded that they don\u2019t have decent weather for everyone. I\u2019ve always believed that emigration is the only answer for England.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Hiram,\u201d Mrs. Otis cried, \u201cwhat can we do with a woman who faints?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTreat it like a breakage,\u201d the Minister replied. \u201cShe won\u2019t faint after that.\u201d In a few moments, Mrs. Umney did come around.\"}"
