          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ef41d5444e67c46102ed56c5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Sydney Carton paused in the street, unsure where to go. \u201cAt Tellson\u2019s banking house at nine,\u201d he said, looking as if he were thinking. \u201cShould I show myself in the meantime? I think I should. It\u2019s important that these people know there\u2019s a man like me here. It\u2019s a sensible precaution, and it may be necessary. But\u2014care, care, care! I need to think it through.\u201d\\n\\nHe checked his steps, which had started to lead him toward some purpose, then turned down a couple of streets that were already growing darker. He followed the idea in his mind and considered what it might lead to. His first thought was right. \u201cIt\u2019s best,\u201d he decided at last, \u201cthat these people should know there is such a man as I here.\u201d Then he turned his face toward Saint Antoine.\\n\\nThat day, Defarge had said he was the owner of a wine shop in the Saint Antoine suburb. If you knew the city, it was easy to find his house without asking questions. Once Carton knew where it was, he went back out into the nearby streets and ate dinner at a place where people could refresh themselves. After dinner, he fell into a deep sleep. For the first time in many years, he didn\u2019t have any strong drink. Since last night, he\u2019d had only a little light, thin wine. And last night he had set the brandy down on Mr. Lorry\u2019s hearth slowly, as if he were done with it.\\n\\nHe woke up refreshed at about seven o\u2019clock and went back out into the streets. As he walked toward Saint Antoine, he stopped at a shop window with a mirror. He adjusted his loose cravat, his coat collar, and his wild hair, making them look slightly more disordered. Then he went straight to Defarge\u2019s and went inside.\\n\\nThere was no customer in the shop, only Jacques Three, with his restless fingers and his croaking voice. Carton had seen him at the Jury. Now he stood at the small counter, drinking while he talked with the Defarges\u2014husband and wife. The Vengeance took part in the conversation as if it were a normal member of the place.\\n\\nWhen Carton came in, he took a seat and asked, in very indifferent French, for a small measure of wine. Madame Defarge gave him a casual look at first, then a sharper one, then an even sharper one. After that, she came over to him and asked what he had ordered.\\n\\nHe repeated what he had already said.\\n\\n\u201cEnglish?\u201d Madame Defarge asked, lifting her dark eyebrows.\\n\\nHe looked at her as if even a single French word took time to form in his mind, and then answered in the same strong foreign accent as before.\"}"
