ave written to Colonel Forster to acquaint him with our present arrangements, and to ask that he will satisfy the several creditors of Mr. Wickham in and near Brighton with assurances of speedy payment, for which I have pledged myself. And will you take the trouble of carrying similar assurances to his creditors at Meryton, of whom I shall add a list, according to his information? He has stated all his debts; I hope at least he has not deceived us. Haggerston has our instructions, and everything will be finished in a week. They will then join his regiment, unless they are first invited to Longbourn; and I learn from Mrs. Gardiner that my niece is very eager to see you all before she leaves the south.\u201d\"}"
