          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8c28afbaa8107e7bb9c8e5cd\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWell, Jup,\u201d I said, \u201cwhat\u2019s the matter now?\u2014how is your master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, to tell the truth, sir, he ain\u2019t so very well as he ought to be.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot well! I\u2019m truly sorry to hear it. What is he complaining of?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDar! That\u2019s it\u2014he never \u2019plains of anything at all, but he\u2019s mighty sick for all that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery sick, Jupiter\u2014why didn\u2019t you say so at once? Is he confined to bed?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, sir, he ain\u2019t!\u2014he ain\u2019t found anywhere\u2014this is where the shoe pinches; my mind has got to be very heavy about poor Massa Will.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJupiter, I\u2019d like to understand what you\u2019re talking about. You say your master is sick. Hasn\u2019t he told you what\u2019s wrong?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, sir, it ain\u2019t worth getting mad about the matter\u2014Massa Will says nothing at all is the matter with him; but then why does he go about looking this way, with his head down and he\u2019s all soldiered up, and as white as a goose? And then he keeps a siphon all the time\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cKeeps a what, Jupiter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cKeeps a siphon with the figures on the slate\u2014those queerest figures I ever did see. I\u2019m getting scared, I tell you. I\u2019ve got to keep a mighty tight eye on him. The day before yesterday he slipped me before sunrise and was gone the whole blessed day. I had a big stick ready, cut out to give him a deuced good beating when he did come\u2014but I\u2019m such a fool that I didn\u2019t have the heart for it; he looked so very poorly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEh?\u2014what?\u2014ah yes!\u2014on the whole, I think you\u2019d better not be too severe with the poor fellow. Don\u2019t flog him, Jupiter\u2014he can\u2019t very well stand it. But can you form no idea of what has caused this illness, or rather this change in his conduct? Has anything unpleasant happened since I saw you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, sir, there ain\u2019t been nothing unpleasant since then\u2014only it was before then that I\u2019m afraid\u2014on the very day you were there.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow? What do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, sir, I mean the bug\u2014there now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe what?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe bug. I\u2019m very sure Massa Will got bitten somewhere about the head by that goole-bug.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd what makes you think that, Jupiter?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cClaws enough, sir, and mouth too. I never did see a sick bug\u2014he kicked and he bit everything that came near him. Massa Will caught him at first, but had to let him go again mighty quick, I tell you\u2014because that was the time he must have got the bite. I didn\u2019t like the look of the bug\u2019s mouth myself, no how, so I wouldn\u2019t take hold of him with my finger; but I caught him with a piece of paper that I found.\u201d}\"}"
