          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7cc8d0868f82cc25b2d149fb\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cCertainly not,\u201d Duff replied.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, translating the word yokel for the ladies\u2019 benefit, I take it you mean that this attempt wasn\u2019t made by a countryman?\u201d said Mr. Losberne, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s it, master,\u201d Blathers answered. \u201cThis is all about the robbery, isn\u2019t it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll,\u201d the doctor replied.\\n\\n\u201cNow, what\u2019s this about that boy\u2014about the one the servants are talking about?\u201d Blathers asked.\\n\\n\u201cNothing at all,\u201d the doctor said. \u201cOne of the frightened servants got it into his head that he had something to do with this attempt to break into the house; but it\u2019s nonsense\u2014pure absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery easily dealt with, if it is,\u201d Duff remarked.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is perfectly right,\u201d Blathers observed, nodding as if to confirm it, and idly playing with the handcuffs, as though they were a pair of castanets. \u201cWho is the boy? What story does he tell about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t just drop out of the clouds, did he, master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOf course not,\u201d the doctor replied, casting a nervous glance at the two ladies. \u201cI know his whole history, but we can talk about that later. First, you\u2019d like to see the place where the thieves made their attempt, I suppose?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly,\u201d Mr. Blathers said. \u201cWe\u2019d better inspect the premises first, and then question the servants. That\u2019s the usual way of doing business.\u201d\\n\\nLights were then brought in. Messrs. Blathers and Duff, accompanied by the native constable Brittles, Giles, and everyone else in short, went into the small room at the end of the passage and looked out through the window; then they went around by way of the lawn and looked in through the window; after that, a candle was handed out so they could inspect the shutter; then a lantern to trace the footsteps; and after that, a pitchfork to poke the bushes. When all this was done, amid the breathless interest of everyone watching, they went back in. Mr. Giles and Brittles were then put through a melodramatic retelling of their part in the previous night\u2019s adventures: they performed it some six times, contradicting each other in not more than one important respect the first time, and in not more than a dozen the last. Once that was finished, Blathers and Duff cleared the room and held a long council together\u2014one that, for secrecy and solemnity, would make a consultation of great doctors on the knottiest point in medicine seem like a child\u2019s game.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the doctor paced up and down in the next room in a state of deep unease, while Mrs. Maylie and Rose watched with anxious faces.\\n\\n\u201cUpon my word,\u201d he said, stopping after a great many very rapid turns, \u201cI hardly know what to do.\u201d\"}"
