          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b51eb0a0302d7cc79e8d665e\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cNot at all,\u201d Duff answered.\\n\\n\u201cAnd, to put the word yokel in plain terms for the ladies, I take it you mean that this attempt wasn\u2019t made by some country fellow?\u201d said Mr. Losberne, smiling.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s it, master,\u201d Blathers replied. \u201cIt\u2019s all about the robbery, isn\u2019t it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEverything,\u201d the doctor said.\\n\\n\u201cThen what\u2019s this about a boy\u2014this here boy\u2014servants have been talking of?\u201d Blathers asked.\\n\\n\u201cNothing whatever,\u201d the doctor returned. \u201cOne of the frightened servants fancied to himself that he had some part in the attempt to force his way into the house; but it\u2019s nonsense\u2014pure absurdity.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cEasy enough disposed of, if that\u2019s the case,\u201d Duff remarked.\\n\\n\u201cWhat he says is perfectly right,\u201d Blathers observed, nodding as though to confirm it, and idly turning the handcuffs about in his hands, as if they were castanets. \u201cBut who is the boy? What story does he tell about himself? Where did he come from? He didn\u2019t just drop out of the clouds, did he, master?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCertainly not,\u201d the doctor said, casting a quick, nervous look toward the two ladies. \u201cI\u2019m acquainted with his whole background; but we can speak of that presently. First, I suppose you\u2019d like to see the spot where the thieves made their attempt?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBy all means,\u201d Mr. Blathers answered. \u201cWe\u2019d better examine the premises first, and then the servants. That\u2019s the proper order of business.\u201d\\n\\nLights were then brought in. Messrs. Blathers and Duff, with the native constable Brittles, Giles, and everyone else in short, went into the little room at the end of the passage and peered out at the window; then they went round by way of the lawn and looked in at the window there; after that