          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"7baec7d05f1a69ae356ed5fb\",\"rewritten_text\":\"With everything arranged amicably and to everyone\u2019s satisfaction, the contract was solemnly ratified with another cupful of the peppermint mixture\u2014something made all the more necessary by the fluttering, agitated state of the lady\u2019s spirits. As the drink was being finished, she told Mr. Bumble that the old woman had died.\\n\\n\u201cVery good,\u201d said he, sipping his peppermint. \u201cI\u2019ll call at Sowerberry\u2019s on my way home and tell him to send tomorrow morning. Was it that which frightened you, love?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt wasn\u2019t anything particular, dear,\u201d the lady said, trying to dodge the question.\\n\\n\u201cIt must have been something, love,\u201d Mr. Bumble pressed. \u201cWon\u2019t you tell your own B.?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot now,\u201d she replied. \u201cOne of these days. After we\u2019re married, dear.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAfter we\u2019re married!\u201d Mr. Bumble exclaimed. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t any impudence from any of those male paupers\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, no, love!\u201d the lady interrupted quickly.\\n\\n\u201cIf I thought it was,\u201d he went on, \u201cif I thought any one of them had dared to lift his vulgar eyes to that lovely face\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey wouldn\u2019t have dared to do it, love,\u201d she answered.\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019d better not!\u201d Mr. Bumble said, clenching his fist. \u201cLet me see any man, parish or non-parish, who would presume to do it\u2014and I\u2019ll tell him he won\u2019t do it a second time!\u201d\\n\\nWithout any fancy show of violence in his gestures, it might not have sounded like the highest compliment to the lady\u2019s looks; but because Mr. Bumble backed the threat with plenty of warlike motions, she was deeply moved by what she took as proof of his devotion. With great admiration, she insisted that he was indeed a dove.\\n\\nThe dove then raised his coat collar and put on his cocked hat. After exchanging a long, affectionate embrace with his future partner, he braved the cold night air again\u2014only pausing for a few minutes in the male paupers\u2019 ward to scold them a little, just to satisfy himself that he could carry out the workhouse-master\u2019s job with the right kind of sharpness. Convinced of his qualifications, Mr. Bumble left the building with a light heart and bright visions of his coming promotion, which kept his mind occupied until he reached the undertaker\u2019s shop.\\n\\nNow, Mr. and Mrs. Sowerberry had gone out for tea and supper, and Noah Claypole was never inclined to take on more physical effort than was necessary for the convenient performance of the two functions of eating and drinking. So the shop wasn\u2019t closed, even though it was past the usual time for shutting up. Mr. Bumble tapped his cane on the counter several times, but getting no response, and seeing a light shining through the glass window of the small parlor at the back of the shop, he had the nerve to peek in and see what was going on. And when he saw what was going on, he was far from unsurprised.\"}"
