u could see it on his face, and said:\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019ve heard him. Is it true?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPart of it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot all, then\u2014not all! What part is true?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat the spirit with the Russian name has put his spell on the well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGod\u2019s wounds\u2014then we\u2019re ruined!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPossibly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut not certainly? You mean, not certainly?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSo when he says none can break the spell\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. When he says that, he\u2019s saying something that isn\u2019t necessarily true. There are conditions under which an attempt to break it might have some chance\u2014some small chance, some trifling chance\u2014of success.\u201d\"}"
