          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ed78d050853b1f743a7749ef\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cStarve you to death? Oh, Mr. Ghost\u2014no, Sir Simon\u2014are you hungry? I have a sandwich in my case. Would you like it?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, thank you. I don\u2019t eat anything anymore. Still, it\u2019s very kind of you, and you\u2019re much nicer than the rest of your awful, rude, vulgar, dishonest family.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStop!\u201d Virginia shouted, stamping her foot. \u201cYou\u2019re the rude one\u2014horrid and vulgar. And as for dishonesty, you know you stole the paints from my box to try to fix up that ridiculous blood stain in the library. First you took all my reds, including vermilion, so I couldn\u2019t paint any more sunsets. Then you took the emerald green and the chrome yellow, and in the end I had nothing left but indigo and Chinese white. That meant I could only paint moonlight scenes, and they\u2019re always depressing to look at, and they\u2019re not easy to paint at all. I never told on you, even though I was very annoyed. It was all so ridiculous\u2014who ever heard of emerald green blood?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, really,\u201d the Ghost said, sounding rather timid. \u201cWhat was I supposed to do? Getting real blood is very hard these days. And since your brother started it all with his Paragon Detergent, I saw no reason why I shouldn\u2019t use your paints. As for color, that\u2019s a matter of taste. The Cantervilles have blue blood, for instance\u2014the bluest in England. But I know Americans don\u2019t care much about things like that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou know nothing about it. The best thing you can do is move to another country and improve your mind. My father will be more than happy to give you free passage. And even though there\u2019s a heavy tax on spirits of every kind, there won\u2019t be any trouble at the Custom House, because the officers are all Democrats. Once you\u2019re in New York, you\u2019ll be a huge success. I know plenty of 