e walking along the brink of a precipice, while thousands press toward it, striving to hurl me into the abyss. William and Justine were murdered, and the murderer goes free; he moves through the world unpunished, and perhaps even respected. Yet even if I were condemned to endure death upon the scaffold for the same crimes, I would not trade places with such a wretch.\u201d\\n\\nI listened to her words with the most intense anguish. Though not in deed, I was, in effect, the true murderer. Elizabeth saw my distress in my face, and, taking my hand with gentleness, said, \u201cMy dearest friend, you must try to steady yourself. These events have affected me\u2014God knows how deeply\u2014but I am not as wretched as you are.\u201d\"}"
