          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b3bec2ae108e911da33416fd\",\"rewritten_text\":\"We proclaimed ourselves freemen so loudly and so earnestly that we caught the attention of that liberty-mouthing orator and his patriotic crowd. They gathered around us and took on a very determined attitude. The orator said:\\n\\n\u201cIf, indeed, you are freemen, you have nothing to fear\u2014the God-given liberties of Britain are around you as your shield and shelter! (Applause.) You\u2019ll see soon. Bring forth your proofs.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat proofs?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProof that you are freemen.\u201d\\n\\nAh\u2014I remembered. I came to myself; I said nothing. But the king stormed out:\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019re insane, man. It would be better, and more reasonable, for this thief and scoundrel here to prove that we are not freemen.\u201d\\n\\nYou see, he knew his own laws the way other people often know them\u2014by words, not by results. They take a meaning and make it feel very vivid when you apply it to yourself.\\n\\nEveryone shook their heads and looked disappointed; some turned away, no longer interested. The orator said\u2014this time in the tone of business, not sentiment:\\n\\n\u201cIf you don\u2019t know your country\u2019s laws, then it\u2019s time you learned them. You\u2019re strangers to us; you won\u2019t deny that. You may be freemen\u2014we don\u2019t deny that\u2014but you may also be slaves. The law is clear: it does not require the claimant to prove you are slaves; it requires you to prove you are not.\u201d\\n\\nI said:\\n\\n\u201cDear sir, give us only time to send to Astolat; or give us only time to send to the Valley of Holiness\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPeace, good man. These are extraordinary requests, and you can\u2019t hope they\u2019ll be granted. It would take too much time, and it would unreasonably inconvenience your master\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201c_Master_, idiot!\u201d the king stormed. \u201cI have no master\u2014I myself am the m\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSilence, for God\u2019s sake!\u201d\\n\\nI got the words out in time to stop the king. We were in trouble enough already; it wouldn\u2019t help us to give these people the idea that we were lunatics.\\n\\nThere\u2019s no point in dragging out the details. The earl put us up and sold us at auction. This same infernal law had existed in our own South in my own time, more than thirteen hundred years later, and under it hundreds of freemen who couldn\u2019t prove they were freemen were sold into lifelong slavery, without the circumstance making any particular impression on me; but the moment the minute law and the auction block came into my personal experience, something that had only been improper before became suddenly hellish. That\u2019s how we\u2019re made.\\n\\nYes, we were sold at auction, like swine. In a big town with an active market we would have brought a good price; but this place was utterly stagnant, and so we sold for a sum that makes me ashamed every time I think of it.\"}"
