          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0cae50d772a7ff7f5f50d307\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJoseph!! Joseph!!!\u201d Then he shook his head and tapped it, showing how he felt Joseph was lacking.\\n\\n\u201cBut my dear young friend,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, \u201cyou must be hungry, you must be exhausted. Sit down. Here is a chicken that was had from the Boar, here is a tongue that was had from the Boar, here\u2019s one or two little things that were had from the Boar\u2014things I hope you won\u2019t despise. But do I,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, getting up again the moment after he had sat down, \u201csee before me the man I used to joke with in his days of happy infancy? And may I\u2014may I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nThis \u201cMay I\u201d meant might he shake hands. I agreed, and he was fervent, and then sat down again.\\n\\n\u201cHere is wine,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook. \u201cLet us drink\u2014thanks to Fortune\u2014and may she always pick out her favorites with equal judgment! And yet I cannot,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, getting up again, \u201csee before me One\u2014and likewise drink to One\u2014without expressing again\u2014May I\u2014_may_ I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nI told him he could, and he shook hands with me again, emptied his glass, and turned it upside down. I did the same; and if I had turned myself upside down before drinking, the wine couldn\u2019t have gone more directly to my head.\\n\\nMr. Pumblechook walked me to the liver wing, and to the best slice of tongue (none of those out-of-the-way No Thoroughfares of Pork now), and took, comparatively speaking, no care of himself at all. \u201cAh! poultry, poultry! You little thought,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, addressing the fowl in the dish, \u201cwhen you were a young fledgling, what was in store for you. You little thought you were to be refreshment beneath this humble roof for one as\u2014call it a weakness, if you will,\u201d said Mr. Pumblechook, getting up again, \u201cbut may I? _may_ I\u2014?\u201d\\n\\nIt started to feel unnecessary to repeat the form of asking permission, so he did it at once. I don\u2019t know how he managed to do it so often without cutting himself with my knife.\\n\\n\u201cAnd your sister,\u201d he went on, after a little steady eating, \u201cwho had the honor of bringing you up by hand! It\u2019s a sad picture to think she\u2019s no longer able to fully understand the honor. May\u2014\u201d\\n\\nI saw he was about to come at me again, and I stopped him.\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019ll drink her health,\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cAh!\u201d cried Mr. Pumblechook, leaning back in his chair, quite limp with admiration, \u201cthat\u2019s the way you know \u2019em, sir!\u201d (I don\u2019t know who Sir was, but it certainly wasn\u2019t me, and there was no third person present); \u201cthat\u2019s the way you know the noble-minded, sir!\u201d\"}"
