e gruff and shrill voices\u2014are enough, of themselves, to raise a suspicion that ought to guide every step of further inquiry into the mystery. I said \u2018legitimate deductions;\u2019 but I mean something more than that. I intended to suggest that the deductions are the _only_ proper ones, and that the suspicion springs _inevitably_ from them, as the single outcome. What the suspicion is, however, I will not tell you yet. I only want you to keep in mind that, for me, it was strong enough to give my inquiries in the chamber a definite shape\u2014a certain direction.\\n\\n\u201cLet us now, in imagination, place ourselves in this chamber. What shall we look for first? The means of egress used by the murderers. It is not too much to say that neither of us believes in pr\u00e6ternatural events.\u201d\"}"
