          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"a7a5b3c87665b0765c82b2ed\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She was right about the rats. Every now and then you\u2019d see one poke his nose out of a hole in the corner. She told me she had to keep things ready to throw at them when she was by herself, or they wouldn\u2019t leave her in peace. She showed me a bar of lead twisted into a knot, and said she was a pretty steady shot with it generally, but she\u2019d wrenched her arm a day or two back and didn\u2019t know whether she could throw true now. Still, she kept her eyes open for a chance, and straightway she struck at a rat; but she missed him clean, and she cried out, \u201cOuch!\u201d\u2014it hurt her arm so. Then she told me to go for the next one.\\n\\nI wanted to be making off before the old man came back, but I didn\u2019t show it. I took the thing, and the first rat that showed itself I let fly at, and if he\u2019d stayed where he was he\u2019d have been a pretty sick rat. She said it was first-rate, and she figured I\u2019d have the next one too. She went and got the lump of lead again, brought it back, and along with it a hank of yarn she wanted me to help her with. I held my two hands up, and she laid the hank over them, then carried on talking about her and her husband\u2019s affairs. But she stopped short to say:\\n\\n\u201cMind the rats. You\u2019d best have the lead in your lap, ready.\u201d\\n\\nSo at that very moment she dropped the lump into my lap, and I clapped my legs together on it, and she went right on talking. Only about a minute passed. Then she took the hank away, looked me straight in the face, and in a very pleasant voice asked:\\n\\n\u201cNow then, what\u2019s your real name?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWh\u2014what is it, mum?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s your real name? Is it Bill, or Tom, or Bob\u2014or what is it?\u201d\\n\\nI thought I must have been shaking like a leaf. I didn\u2019t know what to do. But I managed to say, \u201cPlease don\u2019t make fun of a poor girl like me, mum. If I\u2019m in the way, I\u2019ll\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, you won\u2019t. Sit down and stay just where you are. I ain\u2019t going to hurt you, and I ain\u2019t going to tell on you neither. You just tell me your secret, and trust me. I\u2019ll keep it; and what\u2019s more, I\u2019ll help you. So will my old man, if you want him to. You see, you\u2019re a runaway \u2019prentice\u2014that\u2019s all. It ain\u2019t nothing. There ain\u2019t no harm in it. You\u2019ve been treated bad, and you decided to cut. Bless you, child\u2014I wouldn\u2019t tell on you.\u201d\"}"
