          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"73a6e02b09eecd4782b04b1c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cSo I\u2019m the owner of some knights,\u201d I said, as we rode off. \u201cWho would ever think I\u2019d live to list assets like that. I don\u2019t know what I\u2019ll do with them\u2014unless I raffle them off. How many are there, Sandy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSeven, please you, sir, and their squires.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s a good haul. Who are they? Where do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhere do they hang out?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes. Where do they live?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, I didn\u2019t understand you. I\u2019ll tell you right away.\u201d Then she paused, thinking, and said the words softly, as if tasting them: \u201cHang they out\u2014hang they out\u2014where hang\u2014where do they hang out; eh, right so; where do they hang out. Honestly, that phrase has a nice, charming sound, and it\u2019s worded so prettily. I\u2019ll repeat it again and again in my idle moments, and maybe I\u2019ll learn it. Where do they hang out. There\u2014it's already tripping off my tongue. And since\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t forget the cowboys, Sandy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cCowboys?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes; the knights, you know. You were going to tell me about them. A while back, remember? Figuratively speaking, the game\u2019s called.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGame\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes, yes! Get to the bat. I mean, get to work on your statistics, and don\u2019t waste so much kindling trying to get your fire started. Tell me about the knights.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will. And lightly I\u2019ll begin. So they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d\\n\\nYou see, I realized my mistake right away. I\u2019d started her on it, and that was my fault. It would take her thirty days to get to the facts. She usually started without any introduction and ended without any result. If I interrupted her, she would either keep going without noticing, or answer with a couple of words and then go back and say the sentence again. So interruptions only did harm. Still, I had to interrupt, and pretty often, too, just to save my life. A person would die if they let her monotony drip on them all day.\\n\\n\u201cGreat Scott!\u201d I said, in panic. She immediately began over again:\\n\\n\u201cSo they two departed and rode into a great forest. And\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhich two?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSir Gawaine and Sir Uwaine. And so they came to an abbey of monks, and they were well lodged. So on the morning they heard their masses in the abbey, and then they rode forth until they came to a great forest; and then Sir Gawaine noticed, in a valley by a turret, twelve fair damsels, and two knights armed on great horses, and the damsels went to and fro by a tree.\u201d\"}"
