          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"13dae401779241be6b35bf53\",\"rewritten_text\":\"He was handed over to you. You understand, then\u2014am I right in saying I\u2019m acquainted with the circumstances?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIndeed, that is so,\u201d said Defarge. He had been told to answer, in that brief, accidental moment when his wife\u2019s elbow brushed him while she knitted and hummed her little song, but always to keep it short.\\n\\n\u201cIt was to you,\u201d the spy went on, \u201cthat his daughter came; and it was from your attention that his daughter took him away, with a tidy brown monsieur beside her. What is he called?\u2014with a small wig\u2014Lorry\u2014of the bank of Tellson and Company\u2014across to England.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSuch is the fact,\u201d Defarge repeated.\\n\\n\u201cVery striking recollections!\u201d said the spy. \u201cI have known Doctor Manette and his daughter, in England.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes?\u201d said Defarge.\\n\\n\u201cYou don\u2019t hear much of them these days?\u201d asked the spy.\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d said Defarge.\\n\\n\u201cNot at all,\u201d madame put in, lifting her eyes from her work and her faint song. \u201cWe get word of their safe arrival, and maybe another letter\u2014or perhaps two; but after that they\u2019ve gone on, step by step, along their lives\u2014ours as well\u2014and we\u2019ve kept up no correspondence.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cJust so, madame,\u201d replied the spy. \u201cShe\u2019s to be married.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTo be married?\u201d madame echoed. \u201cShe was pretty enough to have been married long ago. You English seem so cold, that\u2019s what I think.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh! You know I\u2019m English.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI see your tongue is,\u201d returned madame; \u201cand I suppose the man is, too.\u201d\\n\\nHe didn\u2019t take the remark as a compliment; still, he made the best of it and brushed it off with a laugh. After finishing his cognac, he added:\\n\\n\u201cYes, Miss Manette is to be married. But not