          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"10019773af0f4b5e97a9def8\",\"rewritten_text\":\"In the middle of the rift, I saw a white spot, but at first I couldn\u2019t tell what it was. I adjusted the telescope\u2019s focus and looked again. This time I could make out that it was a human skull.\\n\\n\u201cOnce I found that,\u201d I said, \u201cI felt sure the puzzle was solved. The phrase \u2018main branch, seventh limb, east side\u2019 could only mean where the skull was on the tree. And \u2018shoot from the left eye of the death\u2019s head\u2019 could mean only one thing, if we\u2019re talking about finding buried treasure. I realized the plan was to drop a bullet from the skull\u2019s left eye. Then, if you draw a straight line\u2014a bee-line\u2014from the nearest point of the trunk through \u2018the shot\u2019 (the spot where the bullet fell), and extend that line for fifty feet, it should point to a specific place. Beneath that point, I thought, it was at least possible that something valuable was hidden.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAll of this,\u201d I said, \u201cis very clear. Even though it\u2019s clever, it\u2019s still simple and direct. When you left the Bishop\u2019s Hotel, what happened next?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFirst,\u201d he replied, \u201cI carefully took the tree\u2019s bearings and then started back home. But the moment I left \u2018the devil\u2019s seat,\u2019 the circular rift disappeared. No matter how I turned afterward, I couldn\u2019t see it again. The main clever part of the whole thing, as far as I can tell, is this: after repeated tests, I\u2019m convinced the circular opening can be seen from no other place than the narrow ledge on the rock\u2019s face.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIn that trip to the Bishop\u2019s Hotel, I had Jupiter with me. He must have noticed, for weeks, that I\u2019d been acting strangely, and he made sure I wasn\u2019t left alone. But the next day, I got up very early and managed to get away from him. I went into the hills to look for the tree. After a lot of work, I found it. When I got home that night, my valet suggested I should be flogged. As for the rest of the story, I think you know it as well as I do.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI take it,\u201d I said, \u201cthat you missed the spot the first time you tried digging, because Jupiter was careless and let the bug fall through the right eye instead of the left eye of the skull.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s exactly right,\u201d he said. \u201cThat mistake changed the \u2018shot\u2019 by about two and a half inches\u2014that is, it shifted the peg nearest the tree. If the treasure had been directly under the shot, the error wouldn\u2019t have mattered much. But the \u2018shot,\u2019 along with the nearest point of the tree, were only two points used to set the direction of a line. Even a small error at the start grows as you extend the line. By the time we had gone fifty feet, it had thrown us completely off the trail.\u201d\"}"
