rance, I\u2019ve let it have a place in my heart.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019ve always kept your place in my heart,\u201d I answered.\\n\\nThen we were silent once more, until she spoke again.\\n\\n\u201cI never imagined,\u201d said Estella, \u201cthat I should be taking leave of you when I take leave of this spot. I\u2019m glad to do it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGlad to part again, Estella? For me, parting is painful. The memory of our last parting has always been mournful and painful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut you told me,\u201d Estella replied, very earnestly, \u201c\u2018God bless you, God forgive you!\u2019 And if you could say that to me then, you won\u2019t hesitate to say it now\u2014now, when suffering has been stronger than every other lesson, and has taught me what your heart used to be. I\u2019ve been bent and broken, but\u2014I hope\u2014into something better.\u201d\"}"
