          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"fbbab90e5f393b100d0894c3\",\"rewritten_text\":\"A little after noon the boys took a small skiff from a citizen who happened to be away, and pushed off right away. After they\u2019d gone several miles below \u201cCave Hollow,\u201d Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cNow, look at this bluff\u2014down from the cave hollow it all seems the same, mile after mile. No houses, no wood-yards, just bushes that look alike. But see that white spot up yonder, where there\u2019s been a landslide? That\u2019s one of my marks. We\u2019ll land here.\u201d\\n\\nThey came ashore.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Huck, right where we\u2019re standing you ought to be able to reach that hole I dug out with a fishing-pole. See if you can spot it.\u201d\\n\\nHuck searched around and couldn\u2019t find a thing. Tom, feeling pleased with himself, marched straight into a thick clump of sumach bushes and said:\\n\\n\u201cThere you are! Look here, Huck; it\u2019s the snuggiest hole in the whole country. Keep it quiet, that\u2019s all. I\u2019ve been wanting to be a robber all along, but I knew I\u2019d need a place like this\u2014and the trouble was finding it. Well, we\u2019ve found it, and we\u2019ll keep it secret. Only we\u2019ll let Joe Harper and Ben Rogers in, because, of course, there has to be a Gang, or it wouldn\u2019t have any style to it. Tom Sawyer\u2019s Gang\u2014it sounds splendid, don\u2019t it, Huck?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt sure does, Tom. But who are we going to rob?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAlmost anybody. We\u2019ll waylay folks\u2014that\u2019s the main thing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd kill them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot always. We\u2019ll lock them up in the cave until they raise a ransom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s a ransom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMoney. You make them scrape together all they can, off their friends; and if, after you\u2019ve kept them a year, it still isn\u2019t raised, then you kill them. That\u2019s the usual way. Only you don\u2019t kill the women. You keep the women shut up, but you don\u2019t kill them. They\u2019re always beautiful and rich, and they\u2019re terribly scared. You take their watches and things, but you always take your hat off and act polite. There ain\u2019t anybody as polite as robbers\u2014you\u2019ll see that in any book. Well, the women start to like you, and after they\u2019ve been in the cave a week or two they stop crying, and then you couldn\u2019t get them to leave. If you drove them out, they\u2019d just turn around and come back. That\u2019s how it is in all the books.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhy, that\u2019s real bully, Tom. I reckon it\u2019s better\u2019n being a pirate.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, it\u2019s better in some ways, because it\u2019s close to home and there\u2019s circuses and all that.\u201d\\n\\nBy then everything was ready, and the boys went into the hole, Tom leading. They worked their way to the far end of the tunnel, then tied their spliced kite-strings fast and went on.\"}"
