          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"baf1baadb635430c0043ed4c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But don\u2019t imagine that I didn\u2019t feel it was evil in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDepend on it, they were all perfectly comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI might not like them any better for that, perhaps. Such a number of women and children have no _right_ to be comfortable on board.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you\u2019re talking quite idly. Pray, what would become of us poor sailors\u2019 wives, who often want to be taken to one port or another after our husbands, if everyone had your feelings?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy feelings, you see, didn\u2019t stop me from taking Mrs Harville and all her family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I hate to hear you talk like a fine gentleman\u2014talking as if women were all fine ladies, instead of rational creatures. None of us expect to be in smooth water all our days.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201cwhen he has got a wife, he\u2019ll sing a different tune. When he\u2019s married, if we\u2019re lucky enough to live to another war, we shall see him do as you and I, and a great many others, have done. We shall have him very thankful to anyone who will bring him his wife.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAy, that we shall.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I\u2019m done,\u201d cried Captain Wentworth. \u201cOnce married people start attacking me with\u2014\u2018Oh, you\u2019ll think very differently when you\u2019re married.\u2019 I can only say, \u2018No, I won\u2019t;\u2019 and then they say again, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and that\u2019s the end of it.\u201d\\n\\nHe got up and moved away.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a great traveller you must have been, ma\u2019am!\u201d said Mrs Musgrove to Mrs Croft.\\n\\n\u201cPretty well, ma\u2019am, in the fifteen years of my marriage; though many women have done more. I\u2019ve crossed the Atlantic four times, and I\u2019ve been once to the East Indies and back again\u2014only once. Besides that, I\u2019ve been in different places at home: Cork, and Lisbon, and Gibraltar. But I never went beyond the Streights, and I never was in the West Indies. We don\u2019t call Bermuda or Bahama the West Indies, you know.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove had not a word to say in disagreement; she couldn\u2019t accuse herself of ever calling them anything else in the whole course of her life.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I do assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d Mrs Croft went on, \u201cthat nothing can exceed the accommodations of a man-of-war; I mean, you know, the higher rates. When you come to a frigate, of course, you\u2019re more confined; though any reasonable woman may be perfectly happy in one of them. And I can safely say that the happiest part of my life has been spent on board a ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to be feared.\u201d\"}"
