nal blow came on September 19th. He had gone downstairs to the great entrance hall, feeling sure that at least there he would not be bothered, and he amused himself by making satirical remarks about the large Saroni photographs of the United States Minister and his wife, which had now replaced the Canterville family pictures. He was simply dressed but neatly, in a long shroud spotted with churchyard mould; he had tied up his jaw with a strip of yellow linen, and he carried a small lantern and a sexton\u2019s spade.\"}"
