          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"af12cfe27b062b845900ebbe\",\"rewritten_text\":\"There was something so remarkable in the growing glare of Mr. Wopsle\u2019s eye, and he seemed to be turning so many things over in his mind that he grew more and more confused, and I couldn\u2019t make out what he meant. I sat thinking about it long after he had gone up into the clouds in a large watch-case, and still I couldn\u2019t make it out. I was still thinking about it when I came out of the theatre an hour later and found him waiting for me near the door.\\n\\n\u201cHow do you do?\u201d I said, shaking hands with him as we walked down the street together. \u201cI saw that you saw me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSaw you, Mr. Pip!\u201d he answered. \u201cYes, of course I saw you. But who else was there?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWho else?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt is the strangest thing,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle, slipping back into his lost look; \u201cand yet I could swear to him.\u201d\\n\\nAlarmed, I urged Mr. Wopsle to explain what he meant.\\n\\n\u201cWhether I should have noticed him at first but for your being there,\u201d he went on, still in that same lost way, \u201cI can\u2019t be sure; but I think I should have.\u201d\\n\\nWithout meaning to, I looked around me, the way I was used to look around when I went home; these mysterious words gave me a chill.\\n\\n\u201cOh! He can\u2019t be in sight,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle. \u201cHe went out before I did. I saw him go.\u201d\\n\\nWith the reason I had for being suspicious, I even suspected this poor actor. I mistrusted some plan to trap me into admitting something. So as we walked on together, I glanced at him, but I said nothing.\\n\\n\u201cI had a ridiculous notion that he must be with you, Mr. Pip, until I saw that you were completely unaware of him\u2014sitting behind you there like a ghost.\u201d\\n\\nMy earlier chill crept over me again, but I was determined not to speak yet, because it was still possible, based on his words, that he might be trying to get me to connect these references with Provis. Of course, I was perfectly sure and safe that Provis hadn\u2019t been there.\\n\\n\u201cI suppose you\u2019re wondering about me, Mr. Pip; I can see you are,\u201d said Mr. Wopsle. \u201cBut it\u2019s so very strange! You\u2019ll hardly believe what I\u2019m about to tell you. I could hardly believe it myself, if you told me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIndeed?\u201d I said.\\n\\n\u201cNo, indeed. Mr. Pip, you remember, in the old days, a certain Christmas Day, when you were still quite a child, and I dined at Gargery\u2019s, and some soldiers came to the door to get a pair of handcuffs mended?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI remember it very well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd you remember there was a chase after two convicts, and that we joined in it, and that Gargery carried you on his back, and that I took the lead, and you kept up with me as best you could?\u201d\"}"
