celestial kingdom, to cast an alien brightness over our dark hour. Wherever her steps went, gratitude and praise were seen. Still, when she stood before us in quiet simplicity, playing with our children, or with girlish diligence performing small acts of kindness for Idris, one could not help wondering in what fair form of her pure loveliness, in what gentle, thrilling tone of her voice, so much heroism, wisdom, and active goodness could be found.\\n\\nThe summer dragged on, for we clung to the belief that winter would at least restrain the disease. To think it would wholly disappear was a hope too precious\u2014too deeply felt\u2014to be spoken aloud. Whenever such a thought was carelessly voiced, those who heard it answered with a rush of tears and passionate sobs, showing how great their fears were and how slight their hopes.\"}"
