          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8fb2090b82b4fb8884ab449c\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Biddy cried. In my own eyes, the darkening garden, the lane, and the stars that were starting to show all blurred together.\\n\\n\u201cNothing was ever found, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNothing.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you know what has happened to Orlick?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019d guess, from the color of his clothes, that he\u2019s working in the quarries.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSo you\u2019ve seen him, then? Why are you staring at that dark tree in the lane?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI saw him there the night she died.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat wasn\u2019t the last time either, Biddy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo. I\u2019ve seen him there since we\u2019ve been walking here. It\u2019s no use,\u201d said Biddy, putting her hand on my arm as I tried to run out. \u201cYou know I wouldn\u2019t lie to you. He wasn\u2019t there for even a minute, and he\u2019s gone.\u201d\\n\\nIt made me as angry as I could be to learn that this man was still after her. I felt a strong hatred for him. I told her so, and I told her I would spend any money or take any trouble to drive him out of that country. Little by little, she calmed me down and talked more calmly. She told me how Joe loved me, and how Joe never complained about anything. She didn\u2019t say anything about me, because she didn\u2019t need to; I understood what she meant. Joe always did his duty in his own way, with a firm hand, a quiet voice, and a gentle heart.\\n\\n\u201cTruly,\u201d I said, \u201cit would be hard to say too much about him. And, Biddy, we should talk about these things often, because I\u2019ll be coming down here a lot now. I\u2019m not going to leave poor Joe alone.\u201d\\n\\nBiddy didn\u2019t say a word.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy, don\u2019t you hear me?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Mr. Pip.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to mention the fact that you call me Mr. Pip, which sounds to me like bad manners, Biddy\u2014what do you mean by this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do I mean?\u201d Biddy asked, timidly.\\n\\n\u201cBy this?\u201d I said. \u201cNow don\u2019t repeat me. You didn\u2019t used to echo, Biddy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cUsed not!\u201d Biddy said. \u201cOh, Mr. Pip! Used!\u201d\\n\\nWell! I thought I might as well give up that point too. After another quiet turn in the garden, I went back to my main question.\\n\\n\u201cBiddy,\u201d I said, \u201cI made a remark about coming down here often to see Joe, and you answered it with a very noticeable silence. Please tell me why.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAre you sure, then, that you WILL come to see him often?\u201d Biddy asked. She stopped on the narrow path in the garden and looked at me clearly and honestly under the stars.\"}"
