 of Turkey\u2014and set out for Germany.\\n\\n\u201cShe arrived safely at a town about twenty leagues from De Lacey\u2019s cottage, but her attendant soon fell dangerously ill. Safie nursed her with the most devoted affection, yet the poor girl died, leaving the Arabian alone\u2014unable to speak the language of the country and completely ignorant of the world\u2019s customs. Still, she fell into good hands. The Italian had mentioned the name of the place they were traveling to, and after her death the woman of the house where they had lived made sure that Safie reached her lover\u2019s cottage safely.\u201d\"}"
