          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c045a15da9be186d8c3d620f\",\"rewritten_text\":\"We shouted so loudly and so sincerely that we were free men that we caught the attention of that liberty-speaking orator and his patriotic crowd. They gathered around us and took on a very determined look. The orator said:\\n\\n\u201cIf you really are free men, then you have nothing to fear. The God-given liberties of Britain are all around you, like a shield and shelter! (Applause.) You\u2019ll see soon. Bring out your proof.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat proof?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProof that you are free men.\u201d\\n\\nAh\u2014I remembered. I came to my senses, and I said nothing. But the king stormed out.\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019re insane, man. It would be better, and more reasonable, for this thief and scoundrel to prove that we are not free men.\u201d\\n\\nYou see, he knew his own laws the way other people often know laws: by words, not by results. They take a meaning and make it feel very real once you try to apply it to yourself.\\n\\nEveryone shook their heads and looked disappointed. Some turned away and lost interest. The orator said again, this time in a practical tone, not a sentimental one:\\n\\n\u201cIf you don\u2019t know your country\u2019s laws, then it\u2019s time you learned them. You are strangers to us, and you won\u2019t deny that. You might be free men\u2014we\u2019re not denying that\u2014but you might also be slaves. The law is clear. It does not require the person making the claim to prove you are slaves. It requires you to prove you are not.\u201d\\n\\nI said, \u201cSir, just give us time to send to Astolat, or give us time to send to the Valley of Holiness\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cPeace, good man. These are unusual requests, and you can\u2019t expect them to be granted. It would take too much time, and it would seriously inconvenience your master.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMaster,\u201d the king snapped, \u201cyou idiot! I have no master. I am the m\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSilence