          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"6f8facae67b023a89bcc3e67\",\"rewritten_text\":\"She was right about the rats. Every so often you\u2019d see one stick its nose out of a hole in the corner. She said she had to keep things ready to throw at them when she was alone, or they wouldn\u2019t leave her in peace. She showed me a bar of lead twisted into a knot, and said she was a good shot with it generally, but she\u2019d wrenched her arm a day or two ago and didn\u2019t know whether she could throw straight now. Still, she watched for a chance, and then she went for a rat\u2014she banged at it\u2014but she missed him badly, and she said, \u201cOuch!\u201d because it hurt her arm so much. Then she told me to try for the next one.\\n\\nI wanted to get away before the old man came back, but of course I didn\u2019t let on. I took the lead, and the first rat that showed its nose\u2014I let it have it. If it had stayed where it was, it would\u2019ve been a decent sick rat. She said that was first-rate and figured I\u2019d get the next one too. She went and got the lump of lead again, brought it back, and also brought a hank of yarn she wanted me to help her with. I held up my two hands, and she put the hank over them, then kept talking about her and her husband\u2019s business. But she stopped to say:\\n\\n\u201cKeep your eye on the rats. You\u2019d better have the lead in your lap, ready.\u201d\\n\\nSo she dropped the lump into my lap right then, and I clapped my legs together over it, and she went on talking. Only about a minute. Then she took the hank away, looked me straight in the face, and in a very pleasant voice said:\\n\\n\u201cCome on now\u2014what\u2019s your real name?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWh\u2014what, ma\u2019am?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat\u2019s your real name? Is it Bill, or Tom, or Bob?\u2014or what is it?\u201d\\n\\nI think I shook like a leaf. I didn\u2019t know what to do. But I said, \u201cPlease don\u2019t make fun of a poor girl like me, ma\u2019am. If I\u2019m in the way here, I\u2019ll\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, you won\u2019t. Sit down and stay where you are. I\u2019m not going to hurt you, and I\u2019m not going to tell on you either. You just tell me your secret, and trust me. I\u2019ll keep it\u2014and what\u2019s more, I\u2019ll help you. So will my old man, if you want him to. You see, you\u2019re a runaway apprentice\u2014that\u2019s all. It isn\u2019t anything. There\u2019s no harm in it. You\u2019ve been treated badly, and you decided to cut out. Bless you, child\u2014I wouldn\u2019t tell on you.\u201d\"}"
