n\\nThe piles of vegetables looked like blocks of green jade against the morning sky, like green jade against the pink petals of some amazing rose. Lord Arthur felt strangely moved, though he could not say why. There was something about the dawn\u2019s gentle beauty that seemed deeply sad to him. He thought about days that break in beauty and then end in storm. Even these country workers, with their rough but friendly voices and their relaxed ways, made him think: what a strange London they must see. A London without the sin of night and the smoke of day\u2014a pale, ghost-like city, a lonely town of tombs. He wondered what they thought of it, and whether they knew anything about its splendor and its shame, its fierce, fiery joys, and the terrible hunger of it\u2014everything it makes and ruins from morning to night.\"}"
