          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f1f221a9db9abda0f2684867\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cJust one more word, Rose. My dearest Rose\u2014just one more!\u201d Harry cried, throwing himself in front of her. \u201cIf I had been less\u2014if I had been less lucky, as the world would say\u2014if my life had been meant to be quiet and ordinary; if I had been poor, sick, helpless\u2014would you have turned away from me then? Or does the fact that I may soon become rich and respected make you hesitate now?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t ask me to answer,\u201d Rose said. \u201cThis question doesn\u2019t matter, and it never will. It\u2019s unfair, almost cruel, to keep pushing it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIf your answer is what I almost dare to hope,\u201d Harry replied, \u201cit will bring a little light to my lonely path and show me the way forward. It isn\u2019t nothing to do this, to give a few simple words to someone who loves you more than anything. Oh, Rose\u2014in the name of my deep and lasting love; in the name of everything I have suffered for you, and everything you force me to face\u2014answer me this one question!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen if your life had been different,\u201d Rose answered, \u201cif you had been only a little, but not so far, above me; if I could have been a comfort to you in some quiet, humble life, instead of being a burden in ambitious, well-known crowds\u2014you would have been spared this trial. I have every reason to be happy now, very happy. But, Harry, I admit I would have been happier.\u201d\\n\\nAs she said this, old hopes she had held onto since she was a girl came rushing back into Rose\u2019s mind. They brought tears with them, the way old hopes always do when they return broken and faded\u2014and yet they also helped her.\\n\\n\u201cI can\u2019t help this weakness, and it only makes my decision stronger,\u201d Rose said, reaching out her hand. \u201cI really must leave you now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI only ask for one promise,\u201d Harry said. \u201cJust once more\u2014only once\u2014say within a year, though it could be sooner\u2014I may speak to you about this subject one last time.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot to ask me to change my decision,\u201d Rose replied, with a sad smile. \u201cThat would be pointless.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo,\u201d Harry said. \u201cTo hear you say it again\u2014if you will\u2014your final answer. I will put whatever I have, in money or position, at your feet. And if you still hold to your choice, you won\u2019t try, with words or actions, to change it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen let it be so,\u201d Rose said. \u201cIt will be one more painful moment, and by then I may be able to bear it better.\u201d\\n\\nShe reached out her hand again.\"}"
