h the machinery, there was hope the clock might still work. He pointed to a time when he had sent a barometer to the military governor at Odessa. It was set to go off in ten days, but it did not explode for about three months. When it finally did, it only managed to blow a housemaid to pieces, because the governor had left town six weeks earlier. Even so, it showed that dynamite, when controlled by machinery, could be a powerful destructive force\u2014though it was, in a way, rather unreliable about the timing.\"}"
