          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0bcf92189b310c5dc74ea1c5\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I am very ignorant, and it worries me\u2014just a little.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTell me what it is.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have a cousin, my only relative, and she is an orphan too, like me. I love her very much. She is five years younger than I am, and she lives in a farmer\u2019s house in the south country. Poverty separated us, and she knows nothing about my fate\u2014because I cannot write. And even if I could, how would I tell her? It is better this way.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, yes. Better this way.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat I have been thinking as we came along, and what I am still thinking now as I look at your kind, strong face\u2014which gives me so much support\u2014is this: if the Republic really does good for the poor, and they are less hungry and suffer less in every way, then she may live a long time. She may even live to be old.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen what, my gentle sister?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDo you think,\u201d the quiet eyes that hold so much endurance fill with tears, and her lips part a little more and tremble, \u201cthat it will feel long to me while I wait for her in the better land, where I trust both you and I will be mercifully sheltered?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt cannot be, my child. There is no Time there, and no trouble there.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou comfort me so much. I am so ignorant. Am I to kiss you now? Has the moment come?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes.\u201d\\n\\nShe kisses his lips; he kisses hers. They bless each other solemnly. His spare hand does not shake when he lets go. On her patient face there is nothing worse than a sweet, steady brightness. She goes next before him\u2014she is gone; the knitting-women count Twenty-Two.\\n\\n\u201cI am the Resurrection and the Life, says the Lord: whoever believes in me, even if he is dead, will live. And whoever lives and believes in me will never die.\u201d\\n\\nThe murmuring of many voices, the lifting of many faces, the crowd pressing forward with many footsteps at the edge, until it swells ahead in one great mass, like a single heave of water\u2014all of it flashes away. Twenty-Three.\\n\\n*****\\n\\nThat night, people in the city said that his face was the most peaceful they had ever seen. Many also said he looked sublime and prophetic.\\n\\nOne of the most remarkable women who suffered under the same axe had asked, not long before, at the foot of the same scaffold, to be allowed to write down the thoughts that were inspiring her. If he had spoken his own thoughts, and if they were truly prophetic, they would have been these:\\n\\n\u201cI see Barsad, and Cly, Defarge, The Vengeance, the Juryman, the Judge\u2014long lines of the new oppressors who rise after the old ones are destroyed, perishing by this instrument of retribution, before it stops being used.\u201d\"}"
