          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"12bb9d305b1616e878543a9b\",\"rewritten_text\":\"I then went from shop to shop, buying whatever was needed to bring about the change in his appearance. Once that was done, I turned my thoughts, on my own business, toward Little Britain. Mr. Jaggers was at his desk; but the moment he saw me come in, he rose at once and took his place before the fire.\\n\\n\u201cNow, Pip,\u201d said he, \u201cbe careful.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI will, sir,\u201d I answered. As I had been walking, I had decided what I meant to say.\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t commit yourself,\u201d Mr. Jaggers warned, \u201cand don\u2019t commit anyone. Mind you\u2014anyone. Don\u2019t tell me anything. I don\u2019t want to know anything. I\u2019m not curious.\u201d\\n\\nOf course I understood that he already knew the man had arrived.\\n\\n\u201cI only want, Mr. Jaggers,\u201d I said, \u201cto satisfy myself that what I\u2019ve been told is true. I don\u2019t expect it to be false, but I can at least check it.\u201d\\n\\nMr. Jaggers nodded. \u201cBut did you say \u2018told\u2019 or \u2018informed\u2019?\u201d he asked, tilting his head to one side. He wasn\u2019t looking at me; he was looking, as if listening, at the floor. \u201cTold suggests a man speaking to you. You can\u2019t have verbal communication with someone in New South Wales, you know.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019ll say \u2018informed,\u2019 Mr. Jaggers.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cRight.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have been informed by a person named Abel Magwitch that he is the benefactor\u2014unknown to me until now.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat is the man,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, \u201cin New South Wales.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd only he?\u201d I asked.\\n\\n\u201cAnd only he,\u201d Mr. Jaggers replied.\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m not so unreasonable, sir, as to think you in any way responsible for my errors and wrong conclusions; still, I had always supposed it was Miss Havisham.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAs you say, Pip,\u201d returned Mr. Jaggers, fixing his eyes on me with a cool look, and biting his forefinger as he spoke. \u201cI\u2019m not in the least responsible for that.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd yet it looked so like it, sir,\u201d I urged, my heart cast down.\\n\\n\u201cNot a particle of evidence, Pip,\u201d said Mr. Jaggers, shaking his head and gathering up his skirts. \u201cTake nothing on its looks; take everything on evidence. That\u2019s the best rule.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have nothing more to say,\u201d I said at last, with a sigh, after standing silent for a little while. \u201cI\u2019ve verified my information, and that\u2019s the end of it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014having at last made himself known,\u201d Mr. Jaggers went on, \u201cyou will understand, Pip, how strictly, in all my dealings with you, I have kept to the straight line of fact. There has never been the smallest deviation from it. You know that, don\u2019t you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cQuite so, sir.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI told Magwitch\u2014in New South Wales\u2014when he first wrote to me\u2014from New South Wales\u2014that he must not expect me ever to swerve from the strict line of fact.\u201d\"}"
