st, would be impossible; and even if that time could be stretched to an hour and a quarter, the consequences could be disastrous. Thinking through this dilemma made me very uneasy. And it will hardly be believed that, after all the dangers I had already faced, I would treat this matter so seriously that I would give up hope of carrying out my ultimate plan and finally decide that I had no choice but to descend. But this hesitation lasted only a moment.\"}"
