          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"88564dd7280af79d980eeda4\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The moment it was seen, the Ourang-Outang burst through the chamber door, ran down the stairs, and then\u2014through an open window\u2014got into the street.\\n\\nThe Frenchman followed in despair. The ape still held the razor and would sometimes stop to look back at him and wave its arms, until he was almost close enough to catch it. Then it ran off again. The chase went on like this for a long time. The streets were completely silent, since it was nearly three in the morning.\\n\\nAs it ran down an alley behind the Rue Morgue, the ape noticed a light coming from an open window in Madame L\u2019Espanaye\u2019s room, on the fourth floor. It rushed to the building, climbed up the lightning rod with unbelievable skill, grabbed the shutter, which had been pushed fully back against the wall, and used it to swing itself straight onto the bed\u2019s headboard. The whole trick took less than a minute. As soon as it entered, the Ourang-Outang kicked the shutter open again.\\n\\nMeanwhile, the sailor felt both hopeful and confused. He thought he might be able to catch the animal now, because it seemed trapped in the room it had chosen. It could only get away by using the lightning rod, and he might intercept it as it came down. But he also had good reason to worry about what the ape might do inside the house. That fear made him keep following.\\n\\nClimbing a lightning rod is not hard, especially for a sailor. But when he reached the height of the window, which was far to his left, he could go no farther. All he could do was lean over and look into the room. When he saw what was inside, he nearly lost his grip from sheer horror.\\n\\nThat was when the terrible screams began, the ones that had woken the people in the Rue Morgue. Madame L\u2019Espanaye and her daughter, still in their night clothes, seemed to have been busy arranging papers in the iron chest mentioned earlier. The chest had been wheeled into the middle of the room. It was open, and its contents were lying on the floor beside it. The victims must have been sitting with their backs to the window. And because of the time between the ape entering and the screams starting, it seems likely they did not notice the animal right away. The shutter slamming shut would naturally have been blamed on the wind.\\n\\nAs the sailor looked in, the huge animal had grabbed Madame L\u2019Espanaye by the hair\u2014her hair was loose because she had been combing it\u2014and was waving the razor near her face, copying the movements of a barber.\"}"
