          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"8c503f62cbebcb761743a75a\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cDo you often come back?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have never been here since.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNor I.\u201d\\n\\nThe moon began to rise, and I thought about the calm look of the white ceiling, which was gone now. The moon began to rise again, and I remembered the pressure of his hand when I spoke the last words he ever heard on earth.\\n\\nEstella was the next one to break the silence between us.\\n\\n\u201cI have often hoped and planned to come back, but many things kept me away. Poor, poor old place!\u201d\\n\\nThe silvery mist caught the first light of the moon, and the same light fell on the tears that were running down her face. She did not know I saw them, and she tried to control herself. Then she said quietly,\u2014\\n\\n\u201cWere you wondering, as you walked along, how it ended up like this?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, Estella.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThe ground belongs to me. It is the only thing I have not given up. Everything else has slipped away from me, little by little, but I have kept this. It was the only thing I fought for, in all those miserable years.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs it going to be built on?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAt last, it is. I came here to say goodbye to it before it changes. And you,\u201d she asked, with a gentle interest in her voice, as if speaking to a traveler,\u2014\u201cyou still live abroad?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cStill.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd do well, I hope?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI work hard enough to make a living, so yes\u2014I do well.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI have often thought of you,\u201d Estella said.\\n\\n\u201cHave you?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLately, very often. There was a long, hard time when I kept myself from remembering what I had thrown away, before I knew how much it was worth. But since my duty has not stopped me from admitting that memory, I have made room for it in my heart.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou have always had your place in my heart,\u201d I answered.\\n\\nThen we were silent again until she spoke.\\n\\n\u201cI never thought,\u201d Estella said, \u201cthat I would be saying goodbye to you while I was saying goodbye to this place. I am glad to do it.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGlad to part again, Estella? For me, parting is painful. The memory of our last goodbye has always been sad and painful for me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut you told me,\u201d Estella replied, very earnestly, \u201c\u2018God bless you, God forgive you!\u2019 And if you could say that to me then, you will not hesitate to say it to me now\u2014now, when suffering has been stronger than everything else, and has taught me what your heart used to be. I have been bent and broken, but\u2014I hope\u2014into something better.\u201d\"}"
