          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"92cfed5bd711f7cc31b6f063\",\"rewritten_text\":\"These thoughts finally calmed me, and in the afternoon I fell into a deep sleep. But my fever would not let me have peaceful dreams. The terrible scene from the day before kept replaying in my mind: the women flying away, and Felix, furious, ripping me from my father\u2019s feet. When I woke, I was worn out. It was already night, so I slipped out from where I had been hiding and went looking for food.\\n\\n\u201cOnce I had eaten, I followed the familiar path that led to the cottage. Everything there seemed calm. I crawled into my hovel and waited in silence for the usual time when the family would get up. That time came and went. The sun rose high in the sky, but the cottagers did not appear. I shook with fear, sure that something dreadful had happened. Inside the cottage was dark, and I heard no movement. I cannot explain how painful that waiting was.\\n\\n\u201cNot long after, two countrymen passed by. They stopped near the cottage and began talking, with loud, forceful gestures. I could not understand them, because they spoke the language of the country, not the language my protectors used. Soon after that, Felix arrived with another man. I was shocked, because I knew Felix had not left the cottage that morning. I waited anxiously, hoping to learn from their conversation why things were so strange.\\n\\n\u201c\u2018Do you think,\u2019 his companion asked, \u2018that you will have to pay three months\u2019 rent and lose the produce from your garden? I don\u2019t want to take advantage of you unfairly. So please take a few days to think about what you decide.\u2019\\n\\n\u201c\u2018It\u2019s completely useless,\u2019 Felix answered. \u2018We can never live in your cottage again. My father\u2019s life is in the greatest danger because of what happened, and I told you about it. My wife and my sister will never get over the horror. Please don\u2019t keep arguing with me. Take your property and let me escape from this place.\u2019\\n\\n\u201cFelix trembled as he said this. He and his companion went into the cottage. They stayed there for a few minutes, then left. I never saw any of the De Lacey family again.\\n\\n\u201cI spent the rest of the day in my hovel, in complete and numb despair. My protectors had gone, and they had broken the only connection I had to the world. For the first time, feelings of revenge and hatred filled my chest. I did not try to control them. Instead, I let myself be carried along, and I turned my thoughts toward harm and death.\u201d\"}"
