9s infinitely better than Miss Grantley\u2019s.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMay I ask you to hold off on your excitement until I write again? Right now I don\u2019t have space to do it justice.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh, it doesn\u2019t matter. I\u2019ll see her in January. But do you always write such charming long letters to her, Mr. Darcy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019re usually long. As for whether they\u2019re always charming, that\u2019s not for me to decide.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s a rule for me: if someone can write a long letter easily, they can\u2019t write badly.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThat won\u2019t do as a compliment to Darcy, Caroline,\u201d her brother said. \u201cHe doesn\u2019t write with ease. He thinks too much about every word, even words of four syllables. Don\u2019t you, Darcy?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy writing style is very different from yours.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cOh,\u201d Miss Bingley said, \u201cCharles writes in the most careless way imaginable.\u201d\"}"
