sort. The truth is, I felt an irresistible presentiment of some great good fortune hanging over me. I can hardly say why. Perhaps it was more a longing than a real belief;\u2014but you know, Jupiter\u2019s foolish talk about the bug being of solid gold had a striking effect on my imagination. And then there was the whole chain of accidents and coincidences\u2014so extraordinary. Do you notice how it was mere chance that these events should have fallen on the one day of the year that is, or may be, cool enough for fire, and that, without the fire\u2014or without the dog\u2019s intervention at the exact moment when he appeared\u2014I should never have noticed the death\u2019s-head, and so never have become the owner of the treasure?\u201d\"}"
