our Grace\u2019s virtues,\u201d Mr. Podgers went on, and Lady Windermere burst into laughter.\\n\\n\u201cEconomy is a very fine thing,\u201d the Duchess said, pleased with herself; \u201cwhen I married Paisley he had eleven castles, and not a single house fit to live in.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd now he has twelve houses, and not a single castle,\u201d Lady Windermere retorted.\\n\\n\u201cWell, my dear,\u201d said the Duchess, \u201cI like\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cComfort,\u201d said Mr. Podgers. \u201cModern improvements. Hot water laid on in every bedroom. Your Grace is quite right. Comfort is the only thing our civilisation can offer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019ve described the Duchess\u2019s character beautifully, Mr. Podgers; and now you must tell Lady Flora\u2019s,\u201d and, at a nod from the smiling hostess, a tall girl with sandy Scotch hair and high shoulder-blades stepped awkwardly out from behind the sofa, holding out a long, bony hand with spatulate fingers.\\n\\n\u201cAh\u2014so a pianist! I see,\u201d said Mr. Podgers. \u201cAn excellent pianist, certainly, though perhaps hardly a musician.\u201d\"}"
