          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"fcd1ae23e776abf0a2bff0ec\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The insect\u2019s weight was truly remarkable, and, when I considered everything, I could hardly blame Jupiter for his opinion about it; but I couldn\u2019t, for the life of me, figure out what Legrand\u2019s agreement with that opinion meant.\\n\\n\u201cI sent for you,\u201d he said, in a grand, showy tone, after I finished examining the beetle. \u201cI sent for you so I could have your counsel and your help in carrying forward the plans of Fate\u2014and of the bug\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Legrand,\u201d I interrupted, \u201cyou\u2019re certainly unwell. You\u2019d better take some precautions. You should go to bed, and I\u2019ll stay with you for a few days until you recover. You\u2019re feverish, and\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cFeel my pulse,\u201d he said.\\n\\nI did, and to be honest I found not the slightest sign of fever.\\n\\n\u201cBut you could still be sick without having a fever. Let me prescribe for you\u2014just this once. First, go to bed. Next\u2014\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019re wrong,\u201d he cut in. \u201cI\u2019m as well as I can expect to be, given the excitement I\u2019m under. If you truly want me well, you\u2019ll relieve this excitement.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd how is that supposed to happen?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cVery simply. Jupiter and I are going on an expedition into the hills, on the mainland. In this expedition, we\u2019ll need the help of someone we can trust. You\u2019re the only person we can rely on. Whether we succeed or fail, the excitement you\u2019re seeing in me will be just as quickly settled.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m eager to help you in any way,\u201d I said. \u201cBut are you saying that this infernal beetle has anything to do with your trip into the hills?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt does.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen, Legrand, I can\u2019t take part in anything so absurd.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m sorry\u2014very sorry\u2014because we\u2019ll have to try it on our own.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTry it on your own! The man is surely mad!\u2014but wait\u2014how long do you plan to be gone?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cProbably all night. We\u2019ll leave right away, and we\u2019ll be back, at the latest, by sunrise.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAnd will you promise me\u2014on your honor\u2014that once your little stunt is over, and the bug business (good God!) is settled to your satisfaction, you\u2019ll return home and follow my advice without question, as if it were your physician\u2019s?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes; I promise. Now let\u2019s go\u2014we don\u2019t have time to waste.\u201d\\n\\nWith a heavy heart, I accompanied my friend. We set out at about four o\u2019clock\u2014Legrand, Jupiter, the dog, and I. Jupiter brought the scythe and the spades, insisting on carrying all of them himself\u2014more, it seemed to me, out of fear of leaving either tool within reach of his master than from any excess of industry or willingness to help.\"}"
