tepped back to judge the look\u2014put in a touch here and there\u2014then criticized the effect again\u2014Ben keeping his eyes on every move, getting more and more curious, more and more taken up with it. After a bit he said:\\n\\n\u201cSay, Tom, let _me_ whitewash a little.\u201d\\n\\nTom thought it over, and was about to agree; but then he changed his mind. \u201cNo\u2014no\u2014I reckon it wouldn\u2019t hardly do, Ben. You see, Aunt Polly\u2019s awful particular about this fence\u2014right here on the street, you know\u2014but if it was the back fence I wouldn\u2019t mind, and _she_ wouldn\u2019t. Yes, she\u2019s awful particular about this fence; it\u2019s got to be done very careful; I reckon there ain\u2019t one boy in a thousand, maybe two thousand, that can do it the way it\u2019s got to be done.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo\u2014is that so? Oh come now\u2014let me just try. Only just a little\u2014I\u2019d let _you_, if you was me, Tom.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBen, I\u2019d like to, honest injun; but Aunt Polly\u2014well, Jim wanted to do it, but she wouldn\u2019t let him; Sid wanted to do it, and she wouldn\u2019t let Sid.\u201d\"}"
