Without that clue, I would have started my attempts with Spanish and French, since those are the languages in which a secret like this would most naturally have been written by a pirate from the Spanish Main. As it was, I assumed the cryptograph was English.\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019ll notice there are no divisions between the words. If there had been, the task would have been comparatively easy. In that situation, I would have begun with a comparison and analysis of the shorter words, and if a word of a single letter appeared\u2014as is most likely, (a or I, for example,)\u2014I would have considered the solution essentially certain. But since there are no divisions, my first step was to determine the most common letters, as well as the least frequent.\u201d\"}"
