          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c3117c698f884e4209e4b251\",\"rewritten_text\":\"For a moment I was so stunned that I couldn\u2019t think clearly enough to be accurate. I knew that my design was very different in the details from this\u2014though there was a certain similarity in the overall outline. Soon after, I took a candle and, sitting at the other end of the room, began to examine the parchment more closely. When I turned it over, I saw my own sketch on the reverse, exactly as I had made it. My first reaction, then, was just surprise at the truly remarkable similarity of the outline\u2014the singular coincidence that, unknown to me, there should have been a skull on the other side of the parchment, immediately beneath my figure of the _scarab\u00e6us_, and that this skull, not only in outline but in size, should so closely resemble my drawing. I can say that the strangeness of this coincidence left me completely stunned for a time. That\u2019s the usual effect of coincidences like this. The mind tries to connect things\u2014to establish a chain of cause and effect\u2014and, unable to do so, it suffers a kind of temporary paralysis. But when I recovered from that shock, a conviction began to dawn on me gradually, and it startled me even more than the coincidence itself. I began to remember, clearly and positively, that there had been no drawing on the parchment when I made my sketch of the _scarab\u00e6us_. I was perfectly certain of it. I remembered turning it over first one way and then the other, looking for the cleanest spot. If the skull had been there then, of course I couldn\u2019t have failed to notice it. Here was indeed a mystery I felt I couldn\u2019t explain; yet even at that early moment, there seemed to flicker\u2014faintly, in the most distant and hidden chambers of my mind\u2014a kind of glow-worm idea of the truth that last night\u2019s adventure brought to such a magnificent demonstration. I got up at once, put the parchment away securely, and dismissed any further thought until I should be alone.\\n\\n\u201cWhen you had gone, and when Jupiter was fast asleep, I turned to a more methodical investigation of the matter. First, I considered how the parchment had come into my possession. The spot where we found the _scarab\u00e6us_ was on the coast of the mainland, about a mile east of the island, and only a short distance above the high-water mark. When I picked it up, it gave me a sharp bite, which made me drop it. Jupiter, with his usual caution, before seizing the insect\u2014which had flown toward him\u2014looked around for a leaf, or something like that, to hold it by.\u201d\"}"
