 them. Deep ravines, running in different directions, lent the whole scene an air of even harsher solemnity.\\n\\nThe natural platform we had scrambled up to was choked with brambles, and we soon found that we could not have forced our way through them without the scythe. At Legrand\u2019s bidding, Jupiter set about clearing a passage to the base of a tulip-tree of prodigious height, which stood\u2014together with some eight or ten oaks\u2014on the level ground, and far outshone them all, and every other tree I had ever seen then, in the beauty of its foliage and shape, in the wide sweep of its branches, and in the general grandeur of its appearance.\"}"
