1d\\n\\n\u201cNot now, Lord Arthur, but the Duchess is worried. I\u2019m afraid I have to go.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou won\u2019t go. The Duchess isn\u2019t in a hurry.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cLadies shouldn\u2019t be kept waiting, Lord Arthur,\u201d Mr. Podgers said, with a sickly smile. \u201cThe fair sex tends to get impatient.\u201d\\n\\nLord Arthur\u2019s well-shaped lips curled with irritated contempt. At that moment, the poor Duchess seemed almost meaningless to him. He crossed the room to where Mr. Podgers stood and held out his hand.\\n\\n\u201cTell me what you saw there,\u201d he said. \u201cTell me the truth. I have to know. I\u2019m not a child.\u201d\"}"
