t this was the right plan. But how could Mr. Woodhouse be persuaded to say yes? He had never even mentioned their marriage except as something far in the future.\\n\\nWhen they first brought it up, he was so miserable that they almost gave up hope. A second mention caused him less pain. He began to believe it would happen, and that he could not stop it. That was a hopeful step of the mind, moving toward resignation. Still, he was not happy. In fact, he seemed so different from before that Emma\u2019s courage failed. She could not bear to see him suffering, or to know that he was imagining himself neglected. Even though her better judgment almost agreed with the Mr. Knightleys\u2019 promise that once the wedding was over his distress would soon end, she hesitated. She could not go on.\"}"
