e of those papers, Tom?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen how are you going to find the marks?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI don\u2019t need any marks. They always bury it under a haunted house, or on an island, or under a dead tree with one limb sticking out. We tried Jackson\u2019s Island once, but we can try it again later. There\u2019s also that old haunted house on the Still-House branch, and there are lots of dead-limb trees. Dead ones, too.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIs it under all of them?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHow could you say that? No!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen how will you know which one to pick?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWe\u2019ll go for all of them.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cTom, that\u2019ll take all summer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cSo what? If you find a brass pot with a hundred dollars in it, all rusty and gray, or a rotten chest full of diamonds, what\u2019s wrong with that?\u201d\\n\\nHuck\u2019s eyes lit up.\\n\\n\u201cThat\u2019s great. Plenty great for me. Just give me the hundred dollars, and I don\u2019t want any diamonds.\u201d\"}"
