          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"75d204919480260f0fd81778\",\"rewritten_text\":\"They know what a clever lad he is; he\u2019ll be a lifer. They\u2019ll make the Artful nothing less than a lifer.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean by lagging and a lifer?\u201d demanded Mr. Bolter. \u201cWhat\u2019s the point of talking like that to me? Why don\u2019t you speak so I can understand you?\u201d\\n\\nFagin was about to translate those mysterious phrases into plain language; and once it was translated, Mr. Bolter would have been told that they meant that combination of words, \u201ctransportation for life,\u201d when the conversation was cut short by the entrance of Master Bates, with his hands in his breeches pockets and his face twisted into a look of half-comical misery.\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s all up, Fagin,\u201d said Charley, once he and his new companion had been introduced to each other.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThey\u2019ve found the gentleman who owns the box; two or three more are coming to identify him; and the Artful\u2019s been booked for a passage out,\u201d replied Master Bates. \u201cI\u2019ll need a full suit of mourning, Fagin, and a hatband to visit him in before he sets out on his travels. To think of Jack Dawkins\u2014lummy Jack\u2014the Dodger\u2014the Artful Dodger\u2014going abroad for a common two-penny-halfpenny sneeze-box! I never thought he\u2019d do it under a gold watch, chain, and seals, at the very lowest. Oh, why didn\u2019t he rob some rich old gentleman of all his valuables, and go out as a gentleman\u2014rather than like some common little nobody, with no honor and no glory!\u201d\\n\\nWith that outpouring of feeling for his unfortunate friend, Master Bates sat down in the nearest chair, looking chagrined and utterly downcast.\\n\\n\u201cWhat do you mean, talking about him having neither honor nor glory!\u201d Fagin snapped, flashing an angry look at his pupil. \u201cWasn\u2019t he always the best of you all? Is there one of you that could match him or come near him on any trail? Eh?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNot one,\u201d Master Bates replied, his voice rough with regret; \u201cnot one.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen what are you talking about?\u201d Fagin shot back, furious. \u201cWhat are you blubbering for?\u201d\\n\\n\u201c\u2019Cause it isn\u2019t on the record, is it?\u201d said Charley, stung into perfect defiance of his respected friend by the flood of his regrets. \u201c\u2019Cause it can\u2019t come out in the indictment; \u2019cause nobody will ever know half of what he was. How will he stand in the Newgate Calendar? Maybe he won\u2019t even be there. Oh, my eye, my eye\u2014what a blow it is!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHa! ha!\u201d cried Fagin, thrusting out his right hand and turning to Mr. Bolter as he burst into chuckling that shook him as though he had the palsy. \u201cLook at the pride they take in their profession, my dear.\u201d\"}"
