          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"eb4338b6d5d7362823454db9\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Not everyone would have handled it the way she did\u2014refusing to accept Jane\u2019s answer in such a gentle way. But she clearly said she would not write any denial yesterday, the way Jane asked. She would wait, and sure enough, by yesterday evening it was settled that Jane would go. I was truly surprised. I had no idea at all. Jane then took Mrs. Elton aside and told her right away that, after thinking through the advantages of Mrs. Smallridge\u2019s situation, she had decided to accept it. \u201cI didn\u2019t know a word of it until everything was already settled.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDid you spend the evening with Mrs. Elton?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, all of us. Mrs. Elton wanted us to come. It was decided on the hill while we were walking around with Mr. Knightley. \u2018You must all spend your evening with us,\u2019 she said. \u2018I positively must have you all come.\u2019\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMr. Knightley was there too, was he?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNo, not Mr. Knightley. He refused from the start. Even so, I thought he might come, because Mrs. Elton said she wouldn\u2019t let him off, but he didn\u2019t. Still, my mother, Jane, and I were all there, and we had a very pleasant evening. You know, Miss Woodhouse, you always find kind friends agreeable, even if everyone seemed rather tired after the morning\u2019s party. Pleasure, you know, can be tiring too, and I can\u2019t say any of them looked like they enjoyed it very much. Still, I will always think it was a very pleasant party, and I feel extremely grateful to the kind friends who included me.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMiss Fairfax, I suppose, though you weren\u2019t aware of it, had been deciding all day?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI dare say she had.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhenever the time comes, it must be hard for her and for all her friends. But I hope her engagement will have every comfort it possibly can. I mean, in terms of the family\u2019s character and manners.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThank you, dear Miss Woodhouse. Yes, there is everything in the world that can make her happy there. Except for the Sucklings and the Bragges, there isn\u2019t another nursery setup like it\u2014so generous and so elegant\u2014in all of Mrs. Elton\u2019s circle. Mrs. Smallridge is a truly delightful woman. The way they live is almost as good as Maple Grove. And as for the children\u2014except for the little Sucklings and the little Bragges\u2014there aren\u2019t any children anywhere who are more elegant or sweeter. Jane will be treated with so much respect and kindness. It will be nothing but pleasure\u2014a life of pleasure. And her salary\u2014well, I really can\u2019t bring myself to tell you her salary, Miss Woodhouse.\u201d\"}"
