the cheiromancy. I\u2019m for telepathy now. It\u2019s far more entertaining.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You mustn\u2019t say anything against cheiromancy here, Lady Windermere; it\u2019s the one topic Arthur doesn\u2019t like people to tease about. I can assure you he takes it very seriously.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You don\u2019t mean to tell me he believes in it, Sybil?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Ask him, Lady Windermere\u2014here he is\u2019; and Lord Arthur came up the garden with a big bunch of yellow roses in his hand, while his two children danced round him.\\n\\n\u2018Lord Arthur?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Yes, Lady Windermere.\u2019\\n\\n\u2018You don\u2019t mean to say you believe in cheiromancy?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Of course I do,\u2019 said the young man, smiling.\\n\\n\u2018But why?\u2019\\n\\n\u2018Because I owe to it all the happiness of my life,\u2019 he said softly, sinking into a wicker chair.\"}"
