          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"f295a98b8b27ff4f1ba5f73d\",\"rewritten_text\":\"\u201cWhy, you don\u2019t mean to say\u2014\u201d my sister began.\\n\\n\u201cYes I do, Mum,\u201d said Pumblechook. \u201cBut wait a bit. Go on, Joseph. Good for you! Go on!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWhat would respectable people say,\u201d Joe went on, \u201cabout twenty pounds?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cHandsome would be the word,\u201d my sister replied.\\n\\n\u201cWell, then,\u201d said Joe, \u201cit\u2019s more than twenty pounds.\u201d\\n\\nThat miserable hypocrite, Pumblechook, nodded again and said, with a smug laugh, \u201cIt\u2019s more than that, Mum. Good again! Follow her up, Joseph!\u201d\\n\\n\u201cThen to finish it,\u201d Joe said happily, handing the bag to my sister, \u201cit\u2019s twenty-five pounds.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cIt\u2019s twenty-five pounds, Mum,\u201d Pumblechook echoed, rising to shake her hand. \u201cAnd it\u2019s no more than your merits, as I said when my opinion was asked. I wish you joy of the money!\u201d\\n\\nIf the villain had stopped there, his behavior would already have been bad enough. But he made his guilt even worse by taking me into custody, with a kind of proud, bossy authority that made all his earlier wrongdoing seem small.\\n\\n\u201cNow you see, Joseph and wife,\u201d Pumblechook said, taking me by the arm just above the elbow, \u201cI\u2019m one of those people who always see things through once they\u2019ve started. This boy must be bound, right away. That\u2019s my way. Bound right away.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cGoodness knows, Uncle Pumblechook,\u201d my sister said, holding the money. \u201cWe\u2019re very grateful to you.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t worry about me, Mum,\u201d said that evil cornchandler. \u201cA pleasure is a pleasure for anyone. But this boy\u2014you know we have to have him bound. I said I\u2019d take care of it. To tell you the truth, I said I\u2019d see to it.\u201d\\n\\nThe Justices were sitting in the Town Hall nearby, so we went at