          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"0e236eb394305323ace291f8\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Yet despite all that, the boy grew more and more melancholy, pale, and dejected. She added hot baths, sitz baths, shower baths, and plunges. The boy stayed as grim as a hearse. She started to help the water along with a thin oatmeal diet and blister plasters. She calculated his capacity the way you would a jug\u2019s, and filled him up every day with quack cure-alls.\\n\\nTom had become indifferent to persecution by this point. This stage filled the old lady\u2019s heart with consternation. That indifference had to be broken up at any cost. Now she heard about Pain-killer for the first time. She ordered a lot at once. She tasted it and felt instantly grateful. It was simply fire in liquid form. She dropped the water treatment and everything else, and put all her faith in Pain-killer. She gave Tom a teaspoonful and watched with the deepest anxiety to see what would happen. Her troubles were instantly at rest, her soul at peace again; for the \u201cindifference\u201d had been broken up. The boy couldn\u2019t have shown a wilder, heartier interest if she\u2019d built a fire under him.\\n\\nTom felt it was time to wake up. This kind of life might be romantic enough, given his ruined condition, but it was starting to have too little feeling and too much distracting variety. So he thought through different plans for relief, and finally settled on pretending to be fond of Pain-killer. He asked for it so often he became a nuisance, and his aunt finally told him to help himself and stop bothering her. If it had been Sid, she would have had no reason to temper her delight; but because it was Tom, she watched the bottle in secret. She found that the medicine did, in fact, reduce, but it never occurred to her that the boy was using it to patch the crack in the sitting-room floor.\\n\\nOne day Tom was in the middle of dosing the crack when his aunt\u2019s yellow cat came along, purring, eyeing the teaspoon greedily, and begging for a taste. Tom said:\\n\\n\u201cDon\u2019t ask for it unless you want it, Peter.\u201d\\n\\nBut Peter made it clear that he did want it.\\n\\n\u201cYou\u2019d better be sure.\u201d\\n\\nPeter was sure.\\n\\n\u201cNow that you\u2019ve asked for it, I\u2019ll give it to you, because there ain\u2019t anything mean about me; but if you find you don\u2019t like it, you mustn\u2019t blame anybody but your own self.\u201d\\n\\nPeter agreed. So Tom pried his mouth open and poured in the Pain-killer. Peter sprang a couple of yards into the air, then let out a war-whoop and took off around the room, running in circles, crashing into furniture, knocking over flower-pots, and causing general havoc.\"}"
