          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"c260c5ff4fdf2160ac668708\",\"rewritten_text\":\"When Mr. Hiram B. Otis, the American Minister, bought Canterville Chase, nearly everyone told him he was making a big mistake, because there was no doubt at all that the house was haunted. In fact, Lord Canterville himself, a man known for being very proper and careful about honor, felt he had to warn Mr. Otis when they met to talk about the deal.\\n\\n\u201cWe haven\u2019t lived there ourselves,\u201d said Lord Canterville. \u201cNot since my great-aunt, the Dowager Duchess of Bolton, was so frightened that she had a fit. She never really recovered. It happened when two skeleton hands were placed on her shoulders while she was getting dressed for dinner. I should tell you, Mr. Otis, that the ghost has been seen by several members of my family who are still alive. It has also been seen by the rector of the parish, the Rev. Augustus Dampier, who is a Fellow of King\u2019s College, Cambridge. After what happened to the Duchess, none of our younger servants would stay with us. Lady Canterville also often got very little sleep at night because of the strange noises coming from the corridor and the library.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy Lord,\u201d the Minister replied, \u201cI will buy the furniture and the ghost at a fair price. I come from a modern country, where we can get anything money can buy. And with all our energetic young men painting the Old World red, and taking your best actresses and famous performers, I think that if there were such a thing as a ghost in Europe, we would have it back home in no time. We\u2019d put it in a public museum, or we\u2019d turn it into a show on the road.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI\u2019m afraid the ghost is real,\u201d said Lord Canterville, smiling. \u201cIt may have refused the offers of your bold showmen, but it has been known for three hundred years. In fact, since 1584. It always appears before the death of someone in our family.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cWell, the family doctor shows up too, Lord Canterville,\u201d Mr. Otis said. \u201cBut there is no such thing as a ghost. And I don\u2019t think the laws of nature are going to be changed just for the British aristocracy.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou are certainly very sensible in America,\u201d Lord Canterville answered. He did not fully understand what Mr. Otis meant, but he went on. \u201cAnd if you don\u2019t mind a ghost in the house, then it\u2019s fine. Just remember\u2014I warned you.\u201d\\n\\nA few weeks later, the purchase was finished. At the end of the season, the Minister and his family went down to Canterville Chase. Mrs. Otis, who had been Miss Lucretia R. Tappan from West 53rd Street and was once a famous New York beauty, was now a very handsome, middle-aged woman with fine eyes and an excellent profile.\u201d}\"}"
