nd my sister will never recover from their horror. I beg you not to argue with me anymore. Take possession of your property and let me flee this place.\u2019\\n\\n\u201cFelix trembled violently as he said this. He and his companion went into the cottage, stayed there for a few minutes, and then left. I never saw any of the De Lacey family again.\\n\\n\u201cI spent the rest of the day in my hovel in total, numb despair. My protectors were gone, and they had broken the only connection that kept me in the world. For the first time, feelings of revenge and hatred filled my chest, and I didn\u2019t try to control them. Instead, letting myself be carried along by the current, I turned my mind toward injury and death.\"}"
