t be any annoying uncertainty about where to dig. They kept nudging each other, over and over\u2014clear, excited nudges that only meant one thing: \u201cAin\u2019t you glad we\u2019re here now!\u201d\\n\\nJoe\u2019s knife hit something.\\n\\n\u201cHello!\u201d he said.\\n\\n\u201cWhat is it?\u201d his partner asked.\\n\\n\u201cHalf-rotten plank\u2014no, it\u2019s a box, I think. Here, help me. Let\u2019s see what it\u2019s for. Never mind\u2014I\u2019ve already made a hole.\u201d\\n\\nHe reached in and pulled it out\u2014\\n\\n\u201cMan, it\u2019s money!\u201d\\n\\nThe two men looked through the handful of coins. They were gold. The boys above were just as excited as the men, and just as happy.\\n\\nJoe\u2019s partner said, \u201cWe\u2019ll get this done fast. There\u2019s an old rusty pick out in the weeds in the corner on the other side of the fireplace. I saw it a minute ago.\u201d\"}"
