urry.\\n\\nThe sailor\u2019s face turned red, as if he were struggling to breathe. He sprang up and grabbed his cudgel, but the next moment he collapsed back into his seat, shaking violently, with an expression like death itself. He did not say a word. I felt real pity for him.\\n\\n\u201cMy friend,\u201d said Dupin, in a gentle voice, \u201cyou\u2019re frightening yourself for no reason. We mean you no harm. I give you my word as a gentleman\u2014and as a Frenchman\u2014that we intend you no injury. I know very well that you are innocent of the atrocities on the Rue Morgue. Still, it won\u2019t do to pretend you\u2019re not in some way involved.\u201d}\"}"
