          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"b7bf79c9783fa0bfef9d09ac\",\"rewritten_text\":\"The next day he did not leave the house. In fact, he spent most of his time in his own room, sick with a fierce fear of dying, and yet strangely indifferent to life itself. The feeling that someone was hunting him, trapping him, and tracking him down began to take over his mind. If the tapestry even slightly shook in the wind, he would shake too. The dead leaves blowing against the leaded windows looked to him like his own broken plans and wild regrets. When he closed his eyes, he saw the sailor\u2019s face again, staring through the misty glass, and horror seemed to press its hand on his heart once more.\\n\\nBut maybe it was only his imagination that had called vengeance out of the night and put those ugly shapes of punishment in front of him. Real life is chaos, but the imagination can make things feel terribly logical. It is the imagination that makes remorse follow sin. It is the imagination that gives each crime its twisted offspring. In the everyday world of facts, bad people are not punished and good people are not rewarded. The strong get success, and the weak get failure. That was all. Also, if some stranger had been wandering around the house, the servants or the guards would have seen him. If any footprints had been found in the flower beds, the gardeners would have reported them. Yes, it must have been only fancy. Sibyl Vane\u2019s brother had not come back to kill him. He had sailed away in his ship to sink in some winter sea. At least, from him, he was safe. The man did not even know who he was, and could not know who he was. The mask of youth had protected him.\\n\\nStill, if it was only an illusion, it was terrifying to think that conscience could create such frightening ghosts, give them a visible shape, and make them move right in front of him. What kind of life would he have if, day and night, shadows of his crime kept watching him from quiet corners, mocking him from hidden places, whispering to him while he ate, and waking him with cold fingers while he slept? As the thought spread through his mind, he turned pale with fear, and the air felt suddenly colder. Oh, what a wild moment of madness it had been when he killed his friend! How awful the memory of that scene was. He saw it all again. Every terrible detail returned, bringing even more horror. From the dark cave of time, wrapped in scarlet, the image of his sin rose up.\"}"
