          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"ef5ba866f659f4cf90344251\",\"rewritten_text\":\"Knights and horses in heavy armor couldn\u2019t travel very fast. They would make the best time they could, and now that the ground was in good condition\u2014no snow, no mud\u2014they would probably manage a seven-mile pace. They\u2019d have to switch horses a couple of times; they\u2019d arrive around six, or a little after. It would still be light enough. They would see the white cloth I would tie around my right arm, and I would take command. We would surround that prison and get the king out in no time. It would be showy and picturesque enough, all things considered, though I would have preferred midday, because the more theatrical side of the whole thing would be better then.\\n\\nNow, then, to increase the strings to my bow, I thought I\u2019d look up some of the people I\u2019d recognized before and make myself known. That would help us out of our scrape, without the knights. But I had to proceed cautiously, because it was a risky business. I needed to get into sumptuous clothes, and it wouldn\u2019t do to run and jump into them. No\u2014I\u2019d have to work up to it gradually, buying suit after suit from shops far apart, getting a little finer piece each time, until I finally reached silk and velvet and was ready for my plan. So I started.\\n\\nBut the scheme fell apart like scat. The first corner I turned, I ran straight into one of our slaves, snooping around with a watchman. I coughed at the moment, and he gave me a sudden look that went right through me. I figure he thought he\u2019d heard that cough before. I turned immediately into a shop and worked my way along the counter, pricing things and watching out of the corner of my eye. Those people had stopped and were talking together, looking in at the door. I decided I\u2019d get out the back way, if there was one, and I asked the shopwoman if I could step out there and look for the escaped slave, who was believed to be hiding back there somewhere. I told her I was an officer in disguise, and that my partner was yonder at the door with one of the murderers in charge. Would she be kind enough to go tell him he didn\u2019t need to wait, but should go at once to the far end of the back alley and be ready to head him off when I rousted him out?\\n\\nShe was burning with eagerness to see one of those already celebrated murderers, and she set off on the errand at once.\"}"
