          "text": "{\"request_id\":\"992703217387175d74248696\",\"rewritten_text\":\"But don\u2019t think that I didn\u2019t feel it was evil in itself.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBe sure of it, they were all perfectly comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cI may not like it any better for that. With so many women and children on board, they have no right to be comfortable.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cMy dear Frederick, you\u2019re talking in a careless way. What would happen to poor sailors\u2019 wives, who often need to be taken to one port or another after their husbands, if everyone had your feelings?\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYou see, my feelings didn\u2019t stop me from taking Mrs Harville and all her family to Plymouth.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cBut I can\u2019t stand hearing you talk like a gentleman, as if women were all fine ladies instead of sensible people. None of us expects to have smooth sailing every day.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cAh, my dear,\u201d said the Admiral, \u201cwhen he has a wife, he\u2019ll change his mind. If we\u2019re lucky enough to live to another war, we\u2019ll see him do what you and I, and many others, have done. He\u2019ll be very grateful to anyone who can bring his wife to him.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cYes, he will.\u201d\\n\\n\u201cNow I\u2019m done,\u201d Captain Wentworth cried. \u201cOnce married people start telling me, \u2018Oh, you\u2019ll feel differently when you\u2019re married,\u2019 I can only say, \u2018No, I won\u2019t.\u2019 Then they say again, \u2018Yes, you will,\u2019 and that\u2019s the end of it.\u201d\\n\\nHe stood up and walked away.\\n\\n\u201cWhat a great traveler you must have been, ma\u2019am!\u201d Mrs Musgrove said to Mrs Croft.\\n\\n\u201cPretty well, ma\u2019am, in the fifteen years since I married, though many women have done more. I crossed the Atlantic four times, and I went once to the East Indies and came back again, and only once. Besides that, I\u2019ve been in different places at home: Cork, Lisbon, and Gibraltar. But I never went beyond the Straits, and I never was in the West Indies. You know we don\u2019t call Bermuda or Bahama the West Indies.\u201d\\n\\nMrs Musgrove had nothing to say against it. She couldn\u2019t accuse herself of ever calling them anything else in all her life.\\n\\n\u201cAnd I assure you, ma\u2019am,\u201d Mrs Croft went on, \u201cthat nothing can be better than the accommodations on a man-of-war. I mean the higher rates. When you move to a frigate, you\u2019re more cramped, though any sensible woman can be perfectly happy in one. And I can safely say that the happiest part of my life has been spent on board a ship. While we were together, you know, there was nothing to be afraid of.\u201d}\"}"
